1
00:02:07,813 --> 00:02:09,188
<i>Greetings to all!</i>

2
00:02:09,563 --> 00:02:12,021
<i>Let me tell you a story
through this film.</i>

3
00:02:13,396 --> 00:02:15,687
<i>Any locality in Chennai
could claim its dominance.</i>

4
00:02:15,688 --> 00:02:19,895
<i>But the OG locality in Chennai
that's truly dominant</i>

5
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:21,271
<i>is none but Perambur.</i>

6
00:02:24,396 --> 00:02:28,813
<i>The only place in Chennai
without a traffic signal.</i>

7
00:02:30,146 --> 00:02:32,771
<i>It has three different types
of railway stations.</i>

8
00:02:33,146 --> 00:02:34,645
<i>A variety of delicacies.</i>

9
00:02:34,646 --> 00:02:36,270
<i>Paired with a variety of desserts.</i>

10
00:02:36,271 --> 00:02:37,521
It's fun all the time!

11
00:02:38,438 --> 00:02:40,146
<i>Those who hailed from Burma.</i>

12
00:02:40,271 --> 00:02:42,271
<i>Telugu people who came from Andhra.</i>

13
00:02:42,396 --> 00:02:44,646
<i>Anglo-Indians who immigrated from abroad.</i>

14
00:02:45,271 --> 00:02:47,770
<i>Also, Tamil people like me who migrated
from Bengaluru.</i>

15
00:02:47,771 --> 00:02:50,396
<i>Like this, Perambur, the land of love,</i>

16
00:02:50,521 --> 00:02:52,021
<i>houses people
from different corners of the world.</i>

17
00:02:52,396 --> 00:02:56,271
<i>This is a love story of my dearest friend</i>

18
00:02:56,396 --> 00:02:59,938
<i>who has been living in this land of love
for a long time now.</i>

19
00:03:02,271 --> 00:03:03,563
<i>And his name is...</i>

20
00:03:03,771 --> 00:03:05,771
<i>Chirumamilla Sita Krishna!</i>

21
00:03:05,896 --> 00:03:07,896
In short... CSK!

22
00:03:10,521 --> 00:03:12,646
<i>If you would like to
learn about his character...</i>

23
00:03:12,896 --> 00:03:16,313
He's the "take it easy, life is breezy"
kind of boy.

24
00:03:17,896 --> 00:03:20,521
<i>Don't peg him as a slacker
after listening to me.</i>

25
00:03:22,146 --> 00:03:23,938
<i>He used to be a former athlete.</i>

26
00:03:24,313 --> 00:03:26,146
<i>Now he works a coach</i>

27
00:03:29,563 --> 00:03:31,062
<i>"I may have not succeeded as an athlete."</i>

28
00:03:31,063 --> 00:03:33,020
<i>"But I would love to see others succeed."</i>

29
00:03:33,021 --> 00:03:36,438
<i>That makes him today's philanthropist,
coaching for a nominal fee.</i>

30
00:03:37,646 --> 00:03:38,938
<i>It pains me to hype him up.</i>

31
00:03:39,146 --> 00:03:40,645
Forward and back.

32
00:03:40,646 --> 00:03:41,396
Watch me.

33
00:03:41,646 --> 00:03:42,396
That's it!

34
00:03:42,646 --> 00:03:44,020
Hey! What are you doing?

35
00:03:44,021 --> 00:03:47,021
If I had to speak about his girlfriend,
Magic...

36
00:03:47,813 --> 00:03:49,271
She's an Anglo-Indian girl.

37
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:52,021
- She looks like...
- Hey!

38
00:03:52,188 --> 00:03:53,146
What's with the tone?!

39
00:03:53,396 --> 00:03:54,770
I can pick it up from here.
Go away!

40
00:03:54,771 --> 00:03:56,145
Alright, you be the narrator.

41
00:03:56,146 --> 00:03:56,938
Get lost!

42
00:03:57,188 --> 00:03:58,646
He and his beehive head.

43
00:03:59,438 --> 00:04:00,896
Her name is... Magic!

44
00:04:01,021 --> 00:04:04,521
<i>Living up to her name,
she's the magic in my life.</i>

45
00:04:04,646 --> 00:04:06,021
<i>Jesus is her everything.</i>

46
00:04:06,271 --> 00:04:08,896
<i>Her most important decisions
are made in His presence.</i>

47
00:04:09,521 --> 00:04:12,145
<i>And she's never afraid to speak her mind.</i>

48
00:04:12,146 --> 00:04:13,271
You have to accept!

49
00:04:14,188 --> 00:04:15,021
No, Father,

50
00:04:15,563 --> 00:04:16,771
I don't agree with you.

51
00:04:17,521 --> 00:04:20,396
<i>Our queen loves anything black.</i>

52
00:04:20,646 --> 00:04:21,771
<i>Including me.</i>

53
00:04:24,563 --> 00:04:30,271
<i>They are a genuine, happy-go-lucky
Anglo-Indian family.</i>

54
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:32,146
Magic is also a model.

55
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:35,146
<i>It's only a matter of days
before she moves to Australia.</i>

56
00:04:35,438 --> 00:04:38,312
<i>To adjust to Australia's timing...</i>

57
00:04:38,313 --> 00:04:41,271
<i>she's currently working in the
Australian time zone for an IT company.</i>

58
00:04:42,813 --> 00:04:47,521
<i>Our CSK has been in love
with Magic since college.</i>

59
00:04:53,438 --> 00:04:56,146
<i>He has been awaiting her reply
ever since.</i>

60
00:04:57,188 --> 00:04:59,145
<i>To this day, every New Year
and Valentine’s Day...</i>

61
00:04:59,146 --> 00:05:02,895
<i>even during Diwali and Christmas, he greets
her with a card and diligently waits.</i>

62
00:05:02,896 --> 00:05:04,396
Stop here. Stop! Stop!

63
00:05:05,063 --> 00:05:06,187
<i>But in all these years...</i>

64
00:05:06,188 --> 00:05:10,562
<i>He can't even enter Magic's street,
forget her heart.</i>

65
00:05:10,563 --> 00:05:11,771
You're wasting your time, bugger!

66
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:15,271
<i>Meanwhile, when CSK's mom
had his horoscope read,</i>

67
00:05:15,438 --> 00:05:18,521
<i>was foretold that he needs to be
married in 2 months' time.</i>

68
00:05:18,646 --> 00:05:19,896
Two months?

69
00:05:20,188 --> 00:05:20,771
Yes!

70
00:05:20,938 --> 00:05:23,021
If he doesn't marry now,
it might never happen.

71
00:05:23,646 --> 00:05:24,313
But how?

72
00:05:25,188 --> 00:05:26,895
Two months isn't enough time.

73
00:05:26,896 --> 00:05:29,437
<i>Rome wasn't built in a day.</i>

74
00:05:29,438 --> 00:05:32,021
<i>However, our CSK aims to achieve it
within 2 months.</i>

75
00:05:32,146 --> 00:05:33,938
<i>Let's wait and watch what unfolds.</i>

76
00:06:04,313 --> 00:06:06,438
Dad, I just wrapped up training.

77
00:06:07,688 --> 00:06:09,146
- Meet at Shalimar as usual?
- Yes!

78
00:06:09,521 --> 00:06:11,020
- You coming?
- On my way

79
00:06:11,021 --> 00:06:11,646
Okay.

80
00:06:12,521 --> 00:06:14,563
- Let’s go, guys!
- Sure, let's go.

81
00:06:42,271 --> 00:06:43,437
Uncle, what is all this?

82
00:06:43,438 --> 00:06:44,313
Just for fun!

83
00:06:44,521 --> 00:06:45,270
What are you having?

84
00:06:45,271 --> 00:06:46,895
Mom has already made us breakfast.

85
00:06:46,896 --> 00:06:48,896
Don’t be a Mama’s boy!

86
00:06:49,271 --> 00:06:49,896
Bro!

87
00:06:51,021 --> 00:06:51,645
Yes, Sir.

88
00:06:51,646 --> 00:06:53,771
For me, two sets of Appam and Paya.

89
00:06:53,938 --> 00:06:54,771
What, Paya, Sir?

90
00:06:55,396 --> 00:06:56,896
Pepper Paya!

91
00:06:57,021 --> 00:06:58,562
Guys, give him your orders.

92
00:06:58,563 --> 00:07:00,020
Parotta, egg kurma.

93
00:07:00,021 --> 00:07:00,687
One egg dosa.

94
00:07:00,688 --> 00:07:01,438
I'll have the same.

95
00:07:02,438 --> 00:07:03,313
Great song!

96
00:07:08,396 --> 00:07:09,063
Bhaskar!

97
00:07:32,396 --> 00:07:33,771
Hey! What?

98
00:07:34,271 --> 00:07:35,771
Haven't you seen girls before?

99
00:07:35,938 --> 00:07:37,020
Quit bothering them!

100
00:07:37,021 --> 00:07:38,395
Who do you think you are?

101
00:07:38,396 --> 00:07:40,145
- Get lost!
- You don't know these people.

102
00:07:40,146 --> 00:07:43,063
It's 'cause of them Anglo-Indian women
are not able to roam freely.

103
00:07:43,396 --> 00:07:44,146
Delinquents!

104
00:07:44,271 --> 00:07:45,645
- Hey! Who's the delinquent?
- Dirtbag!

105
00:07:45,646 --> 00:07:47,270
Who are you calling a dirt bag?

106
00:07:47,271 --> 00:07:50,146
Hey, Bhaskar!
Don't do it!

107
00:07:50,271 --> 00:07:52,021
- I’ll knock your teeth out!
- Dad, cut it out!

108
00:07:52,146 --> 00:07:54,146
Don't you dare! I'm warning you!

109
00:07:54,271 --> 00:07:54,896
Zip it!

110
00:07:55,146 --> 00:07:56,437
Do you expect me to sit
and take insults?

111
00:07:56,438 --> 00:07:58,020
- I didn't say anything wrong.
- Just pipe down!

112
00:07:58,021 --> 00:07:59,895
Dad, why did you climb over
the table just now?

113
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:00,895
Hey, Bhaskar!

114
00:08:00,896 --> 00:08:02,521
We thought you didn't like Anglo-Indians?

115
00:08:02,688 --> 00:08:03,437
What do you mean?

116
00:08:03,438 --> 00:08:04,438
Your order, sir.

117
00:08:05,271 --> 00:08:06,896
- Why is Anglo-Indian a big deal?
- Exactly!

118
00:08:07,021 --> 00:08:09,063
Family first gawks,
then tries to cover it up.

119
00:08:09,396 --> 00:08:11,521
I wasn't gawking at them, Uncle.

120
00:08:11,771 --> 00:08:13,145
I was checking who it was.

121
00:08:13,146 --> 00:08:14,646
You were drooling over them.

122
00:08:14,813 --> 00:08:15,520
We saw you gawking.

123
00:08:15,521 --> 00:08:17,271
Do you really think
we have a chance with them?

124
00:08:17,396 --> 00:08:18,896
Hey! Who's "we"?

125
00:08:19,688 --> 00:08:20,812
My son's a stud!

126
00:08:20,813 --> 00:08:21,645
What does he lack?

127
00:08:21,646 --> 00:08:22,896
He doesn't lack anything.

128
00:08:23,396 --> 00:08:25,312
They're not the kind to be wooed easily.

129
00:08:25,313 --> 00:08:26,646
Half of them are foreigners.

130
00:08:26,896 --> 00:08:30,521
Your son should find a girl
in some village in Andhra instead.

131
00:08:30,646 --> 00:08:31,813
He has better chances out there.

132
00:08:33,563 --> 00:08:34,646
Hey! Shut up!

133
00:08:35,813 --> 00:08:37,313
You guys are going overboard!

134
00:08:37,938 --> 00:08:38,938
I'm challenging you all.

135
00:08:39,896 --> 00:08:40,646
Right here in Perambur,

136
00:08:40,771 --> 00:08:45,271
if my son, Chirumamilla Sita Krishna,
fails to marry an Anglo-Indian girl.

137
00:08:46,063 --> 00:08:49,021
My name is no longer
Chirumamilla Aadhinarayana Bhaskar.

138
00:08:50,063 --> 00:08:51,063
Let's go, my boy!

139
00:08:56,146 --> 00:08:57,563
You spoke fiercely!

140
00:08:57,771 --> 00:08:59,771
No, that's too far away.
We'll ride straight.

141
00:09:00,313 --> 00:09:01,271
Damn you, man!

142
00:09:01,646 --> 00:09:02,896
Remember to wear this.

143
00:09:03,646 --> 00:09:04,688
Hey, Bhaskar!

144
00:09:04,896 --> 00:09:07,771
I was saying to you
that you spoke out of rage.

145
00:09:07,896 --> 00:09:08,521
Hey!

146
00:09:08,771 --> 00:09:10,271
I didn't speak out of rage.

147
00:09:10,938 --> 00:09:14,396
I’ve been feuding
with some Anglo-Indians for a while.

148
00:09:14,813 --> 00:09:17,938
That's why I was enraged
to hear them speak that way.

149
00:09:18,563 --> 00:09:21,313
Why can't you fall in love
with Anglo-Indian girls?

150
00:09:21,771 --> 00:09:23,521
Listen, they're very beautiful.

151
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:26,188
Dad, please be practical.

152
00:09:26,396 --> 00:09:27,896
Even the local girl
doesn't give me a second look.

153
00:09:28,021 --> 00:09:29,271
And you want me to aim
for Anglo-Indians.

154
00:09:29,646 --> 00:09:30,646
Take it I find one girl...

155
00:09:30,813 --> 00:09:32,688
Mom would never approve.

156
00:09:32,813 --> 00:09:33,770
Really?!

157
00:09:33,771 --> 00:09:35,562
It sounds like
you have something going on.

158
00:09:35,563 --> 00:09:37,771
Dad, as if I'm that lucky.

159
00:09:37,896 --> 00:09:38,812
Listen, Dad.

160
00:09:38,813 --> 00:09:40,520
All I can do
is marry whoever Mom picks out.

161
00:09:40,521 --> 00:09:42,520
Even if I were to have a love marriage...

162
00:09:42,521 --> 00:09:44,020
it would be with Mom’s approval

163
00:09:44,021 --> 00:09:46,520
and a girl from our own caste.

164
00:09:46,521 --> 00:09:47,021
Hey!

165
00:09:47,521 --> 00:09:48,562
What now?

166
00:09:48,563 --> 00:09:49,313
Aren't you ashamed?

167
00:09:50,646 --> 00:09:52,896
I lost my love
because of caste discrimination.

168
00:09:53,521 --> 00:09:56,771
No matter whom you love,
I'll support you all the way.

169
00:09:57,646 --> 00:09:58,396
Mummy?

170
00:09:58,771 --> 00:10:00,270
Your Mother has no control over me.

171
00:10:00,271 --> 00:10:00,896
Hand that over!

172
00:10:01,021 --> 00:10:01,563
Give it to me

173
00:10:04,938 --> 00:10:08,063
<i>If you're wondering
why he’s staring him down...</i>

174
00:10:08,271 --> 00:10:10,646
<i>it's because CSK's mother
is a fierce character.</i>

175
00:10:12,938 --> 00:10:14,313
<i>Vakkalanka Sarala!</i>

176
00:10:14,646 --> 00:10:18,313
<i>She's the head of this family,
and everything needs to be.</i>

177
00:10:18,521 --> 00:10:20,146
<i>She runs a flour shop.</i>

178
00:10:20,646 --> 00:10:24,063
<i>Even when her sons
and husband make their living</i>

179
00:10:24,271 --> 00:10:26,187
<i>She proudly refuses
to borrow a dime from them.</i>

180
00:10:26,188 --> 00:10:28,313
How did you forget
to bring loose change?

181
00:10:28,938 --> 00:10:30,646
<i>She's a Woman of Steel!</i>

182
00:10:32,521 --> 00:10:34,938
<i>Nothing happens in their family
without her approval.</i>

183
00:10:35,271 --> 00:10:37,021
<i>She's extremely devout!</i>

184
00:10:37,438 --> 00:10:38,813
What kind of dress is this?

185
00:10:39,146 --> 00:10:41,520
Girls who wear sleeveless
won't be suitable for my family.

186
00:10:41,521 --> 00:10:44,271
<i>For her, everything is religion and caste.</i>

187
00:10:44,646 --> 00:10:46,521
<i>It applies not only to her family...</i>

188
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:49,021
<i>She is a key member of her community.</i>

189
00:10:54,021 --> 00:10:55,937
<i>Meet CSK's brother.</i>

190
00:10:55,938 --> 00:10:57,896
<i>Chirumamilla Chiranjeevi Shankar.</i>

191
00:10:58,271 --> 00:10:59,687
<i>State government employee!</i>

192
00:10:59,688 --> 00:11:01,896
What is this?
Why didn’t you check this?

193
00:11:02,063 --> 00:11:06,520
<i>He lives up to his mom's expectations.</i>

194
00:11:06,521 --> 00:11:08,813
Look at him.
Learn from your younger brother.

195
00:11:08,938 --> 00:11:11,062
How do you refer to yourself
as Chiranjeevi's brother?

196
00:11:11,063 --> 00:11:12,313
Shame on you! Kneel down!

197
00:11:12,896 --> 00:11:14,645
Even after being Chiranjeevi's brother...

198
00:11:14,646 --> 00:11:16,187
is this the most you could score?

199
00:11:16,188 --> 00:11:18,771
Is Chiranjeevi's brother
working in an athlete camp?

200
00:11:18,896 --> 00:11:20,063
Couldn't you find a better job?

201
00:11:20,188 --> 00:11:20,938
Whatever!

202
00:11:21,938 --> 00:11:24,271
<i>If there is someone
he loves in this house...</i>

203
00:11:24,521 --> 00:11:26,562
<i>It has to be his sister,
Chirumamilla Sathyavadhi,</i>

204
00:11:26,563 --> 00:11:28,021
<i>and her daughter, Bommi.</i>

205
00:11:30,438 --> 00:11:31,437
- Out!
- Dad!

206
00:11:31,438 --> 00:11:32,438
Who is it? Who's it?

207
00:11:32,896 --> 00:11:33,438
Dad, it's time!

208
00:11:33,563 --> 00:11:36,687
<i>This is Chirumamilla Aadhinarayana Bhaskar.</i>

209
00:11:36,688 --> 00:11:38,771
<i>Even his name is as long as a train.</i>

210
00:11:38,938 --> 00:11:41,562
<i>Which is why he works
at the train manufacturing unit.</i>

211
00:11:41,563 --> 00:11:43,063
I can still see a white patch.
Do it right!

212
00:11:45,146 --> 00:11:47,021
<i>His friends matter most to him.</i>

213
00:11:47,438 --> 00:11:48,520
<i>Even at his age...</i>

214
00:11:48,521 --> 00:11:51,563
<i>He cycles between tea shops
and Shalimar with them.</i>

215
00:11:53,271 --> 00:11:55,438
Starts each morning with a football match.

216
00:11:55,896 --> 00:11:57,563
<i>Cause he's from the sports reservation.</i>

217
00:11:58,438 --> 00:12:01,146
<i>Our daddy here is a total playboy.</i>

218
00:12:01,396 --> 00:12:02,896
<i>You haven't seen it all.</i>

219
00:12:03,063 --> 00:12:06,270
<i>He does one thing
that Mummy can't forgive him for.</i>

220
00:12:06,271 --> 00:12:07,270
Hey, why are you taking mine?

221
00:12:07,271 --> 00:12:09,896
<i>At dusk, he drowns in alcohol.</i>

222
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:11,063
- Hey, Boomer!
- Dad!

223
00:12:12,646 --> 00:12:16,646
<i>But when he's sober,
he's nothing less than a scared cat.</i>

224
00:12:16,813 --> 00:12:17,813
Don't say anything!

225
00:12:20,688 --> 00:12:21,438
Hey!

226
00:12:22,396 --> 00:12:23,521
Coming, dear.

227
00:12:23,771 --> 00:12:25,313
How many times should I call you?

228
00:12:25,438 --> 00:12:26,771
Don't you have any responsibility?

229
00:12:27,521 --> 00:12:29,771
Uncle is waiting with wedding invites.

230
00:12:30,396 --> 00:12:31,313
I was stuck in a meeting

231
00:12:31,563 --> 00:12:32,437
Are they waiting?

232
00:12:32,438 --> 00:12:34,271
Get inside. Go!

233
00:12:34,938 --> 00:12:35,813
Brother!

234
00:12:36,646 --> 00:12:37,270
Welcome!

235
00:12:37,271 --> 00:12:38,396
I'll bring the coffee.

236
00:12:38,646 --> 00:12:40,438
- How have you been?
- Real good, Bhaskar.

237
00:12:40,563 --> 00:12:41,396
- Look at him all grown up.
- Welcome!

238
00:12:42,063 --> 00:12:43,521
Looks like
you're still practicing football.

239
00:12:43,771 --> 00:12:45,145
It got me a job in the railway.

240
00:12:45,146 --> 00:12:46,187
How can I leave that behind?

241
00:12:46,188 --> 00:12:47,437
That's not the case, Uncle.

242
00:12:47,438 --> 00:12:48,771
He still considers himself a child.

243
00:12:48,896 --> 00:12:50,145
Always hanging out with friends.

244
00:12:50,146 --> 00:12:51,563
He's a fun character, dear.

245
00:12:53,021 --> 00:12:54,396
Please hand out the invitation.

246
00:12:55,896 --> 00:12:57,812
Make sure you bring your family, Bhaskar.

247
00:12:57,813 --> 00:12:59,688
- Okay, dear?
- For sure!

248
00:13:00,688 --> 00:13:01,521
Please sit.

249
00:13:05,396 --> 00:13:06,563
The wedding is during the weekend.

250
00:13:06,688 --> 00:13:09,146
- No excuses. You must come.
- Of course, I won't miss it.

251
00:13:09,438 --> 00:13:11,771
Isn't the girl form our caste?

252
00:13:15,771 --> 00:13:16,896
It's a love marriage.

253
00:13:17,063 --> 00:13:18,063
What do you expect us to do?

254
00:13:18,271 --> 00:13:19,271
So what?

255
00:13:19,396 --> 00:13:20,896
Do you agree to anything?

256
00:13:21,188 --> 00:13:23,438
Our caste deserves some respect.

257
00:13:23,563 --> 00:13:24,896
Sarala, that's enough.

258
00:13:27,146 --> 00:13:27,771
Sarala...

259
00:13:27,896 --> 00:13:30,646
kids these days don’t listen to us anymore.

260
00:13:32,063 --> 00:13:33,563
- Sathyavadhi!
- Mom!

261
00:13:34,521 --> 00:13:35,396
Mom?

262
00:13:35,563 --> 00:13:37,188
Who chose your husband?

263
00:13:37,521 --> 00:13:38,396
It was you, Mother.

264
00:13:39,688 --> 00:13:40,646
Chiranjeevi!

265
00:13:42,688 --> 00:13:43,146
Mom?

266
00:13:43,271 --> 00:13:45,063
Which caste will you marry into?

267
00:13:45,313 --> 00:13:47,396
A girl from our caste, as per your choice.

268
00:13:49,021 --> 00:13:49,813
Krishna!

269
00:13:50,021 --> 00:13:50,563
Mom!

270
00:13:50,938 --> 00:13:52,563
Who will you marry?

271
00:14:00,146 --> 00:14:01,188
- Krishna!
- Mom!

272
00:14:02,021 --> 00:14:03,771
Whoever you choose.

273
00:14:06,271 --> 00:14:07,271
Did you see?

274
00:14:08,146 --> 00:14:10,896
Say it the right way,
and everyone will listen.

275
00:14:11,313 --> 00:14:13,437
It all depends on upbringing.

276
00:14:13,438 --> 00:14:15,396
Alright, our upbringing wasn’t right.

277
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:18,021
We'll have another kid
and raise it properly.

278
00:14:18,271 --> 00:14:19,521
For now, just come to this wedding.

279
00:14:20,396 --> 00:14:21,271
When is it?

280
00:14:22,146 --> 00:14:23,270
25th of next month.

281
00:14:23,271 --> 00:14:25,146
My husband and Chiranjeevi can't take off.

282
00:14:25,313 --> 00:14:26,271
We can’t make it!

283
00:14:29,646 --> 00:14:30,521
Oh!

284
00:14:32,271 --> 00:14:33,521
I see how it is.

285
00:14:34,563 --> 00:14:36,313
The other two boys are yet to be married.

286
00:14:36,938 --> 00:14:37,771
We'll see!

287
00:14:38,521 --> 00:14:40,063
Hey, come on!

288
00:14:40,688 --> 00:14:42,020
I'll see you around.

289
00:14:42,021 --> 00:14:43,021
Hey, come on!

290
00:14:44,563 --> 00:14:45,563
We'll see, he says!

291
00:14:46,521 --> 00:14:48,271
Sarala, this isn't right.

292
00:14:49,646 --> 00:14:52,146
I've arranged so many marriages
in our community…

293
00:14:52,271 --> 00:14:54,771
and now one person
from our own family marries an outsider

294
00:14:55,021 --> 00:14:58,396
do you expect me
to bless that marriage?

295
00:15:01,021 --> 00:15:03,021
If anyone attends that wedding...

296
00:15:03,396 --> 00:15:04,396
that’s the end of it!

297
00:15:10,688 --> 00:15:11,396
Phew!

298
00:15:11,771 --> 00:15:14,396
Seeing what my mom did
scared even me.

299
00:15:14,521 --> 00:15:16,521
If I told them about Magic

300
00:15:16,646 --> 00:15:18,145
they'll bury me alive.

301
00:15:18,146 --> 00:15:20,145
You just have to say it the right way.

302
00:15:20,146 --> 00:15:22,146
Hey, no matter how he says it,
his mother will never agree.

303
00:15:22,313 --> 00:15:24,938
And if he waits for her approval,
he’ll never get married.

304
00:15:25,063 --> 00:15:26,896
Hey, Big guy. So what?

305
00:15:27,021 --> 00:15:28,938
Do you expect me to elope with her?

306
00:15:29,146 --> 00:15:31,271
- I would love to see you elope.
- Damn you!

307
00:15:31,438 --> 00:15:32,895
Maggie, what do you say?

308
00:15:32,896 --> 00:15:34,270
Aren't you guys in love?

309
00:15:34,271 --> 00:15:35,520
Who needs permission?

310
00:15:35,521 --> 00:15:36,770
- Just run away together!
- Bro!

311
00:15:36,771 --> 00:15:38,646
Like that's ever going to happen.

312
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:40,770
Are you implying
that I don't have the guts?

313
00:15:40,771 --> 00:15:43,562
Bro! You have the guts.

314
00:15:43,563 --> 00:15:46,021
But the girl has to agree to it.

315
00:15:47,146 --> 00:15:48,771
It's delusional to talk about marriage

316
00:15:48,896 --> 00:15:51,020
when it's an unrequited love.

317
00:15:51,021 --> 00:15:52,146
I don't get it!

318
00:15:52,271 --> 00:15:53,563
Hey! Shut up!

319
00:15:53,771 --> 00:15:54,896
She likes me a lot.

320
00:15:55,021 --> 00:15:57,396
Liking someone and being in love
are not the same.

321
00:16:00,521 --> 00:16:01,896
What else?

322
00:16:02,021 --> 00:16:04,770
That girl hasn't invited him
over to her house once.

323
00:16:04,771 --> 00:16:06,938
She doesn't even let him onto her street.

324
00:16:07,188 --> 00:16:10,021
Her relatives don’t even know
that he exists.

325
00:16:10,271 --> 00:16:12,395
And he calls this love!
Shameless!

326
00:16:12,396 --> 00:16:13,646
Hey, I'll end you--

327
00:16:14,771 --> 00:16:16,021
Hey, it's Magic!

328
00:16:19,021 --> 00:16:19,937
Hello, Magic!

329
00:16:19,938 --> 00:16:21,146
<i>Hey Krishna, where are you at?</i>

330
00:16:21,396 --> 00:16:23,145
Here, with my friends.

331
00:16:23,146 --> 00:16:24,271
<i>You know my church, right?</i>

332
00:16:24,646 --> 00:16:26,562
I guess so.

333
00:16:26,563 --> 00:16:27,521
<i>Can you get there, man?</i>

334
00:16:27,646 --> 00:16:28,771
<i>I want you to meet my uncle.</i>

335
00:16:28,938 --> 00:16:30,396
<i>I was just telling him about you.</i>

336
00:16:30,521 --> 00:16:32,021
You spoke to your Uncle...

337
00:16:32,396 --> 00:16:33,312
about me!

338
00:16:33,313 --> 00:16:33,938
Yeah, man

339
00:16:34,146 --> 00:16:34,896
Okay, okay.

340
00:16:35,021 --> 00:16:35,813
I'm on my way.

341
00:16:36,146 --> 00:16:38,188
Dude, hear me out.

342
00:16:38,313 --> 00:16:40,396
I know everything about Anglos-Indians.

343
00:16:40,521 --> 00:16:42,771
They are everywhere in Bangalore.

344
00:16:42,896 --> 00:16:43,521
Really?

345
00:16:43,771 --> 00:16:47,896
I'm telling the truth.
Their women are very smart.

346
00:16:48,146 --> 00:16:49,645
Unless a guy is serious...

347
00:16:49,646 --> 00:16:52,021
they don't let him anywhere
near their community.

348
00:16:52,146 --> 00:16:54,145
Then why would she want me to
meet her Uncle?

349
00:16:54,146 --> 00:16:57,145
It means that she's serious about you.

350
00:16:57,146 --> 00:16:59,187
Go there and fix a date for the marriage.

351
00:16:59,188 --> 00:16:59,896
Really?!

352
00:17:00,021 --> 00:17:01,312
Trust me, dude!

353
00:17:01,313 --> 00:17:04,021
I know everything about Anglo-Indians.

354
00:17:17,188 --> 00:17:18,438
Oh, wow! Beautiful girls!

355
00:17:19,146 --> 00:17:20,021
- Oh, no!
- Hey!

356
00:17:20,396 --> 00:17:22,021
I slipped, Dude!

357
00:17:23,688 --> 00:17:24,938
Dude, she’s coming to us.

358
00:17:25,396 --> 00:17:26,146
- Hi
- Hi!

359
00:17:26,646 --> 00:17:28,312
- Hi, Krishna.
- Hi, Magic.

360
00:17:28,313 --> 00:17:29,395
Thanks for coming here, man.

361
00:17:29,396 --> 00:17:30,520
- You must have been busy?
- No problem!

362
00:17:30,521 --> 00:17:31,520
Not even close.

363
00:17:31,521 --> 00:17:33,645
He was waiting by his phone
for your call.

364
00:17:33,646 --> 00:17:35,145
Hey, Bugger. Really?

365
00:17:35,146 --> 00:17:36,313
He's just mocking me!

366
00:17:36,771 --> 00:17:38,688
You have to meet my Uncle, okay?

367
00:17:39,021 --> 00:17:40,437
Uncle, please come here.

368
00:17:40,438 --> 00:17:41,146
Uncle?

369
00:17:41,521 --> 00:17:43,145
This is the man they were talking about.

370
00:17:43,146 --> 00:17:44,062
We can even have the wedding here, right?

371
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:44,771
It'll be awesome!

372
00:17:45,771 --> 00:17:46,771
- Hello, gentlemen!
- Hi, Uncle!

373
00:17:47,063 --> 00:17:49,146
I'm Rosario.
You're Krishna, right?

374
00:17:49,771 --> 00:17:51,312
You even know his name?

375
00:17:51,313 --> 00:17:52,271
How could I not?

376
00:17:52,521 --> 00:17:54,771
Magic has spoken so much about Krishna.

377
00:17:55,063 --> 00:17:55,646
Dude...

378
00:17:56,438 --> 00:17:57,396
You believe me now?

379
00:17:57,521 --> 00:17:59,645
I know everything about Anglo-Indians.

380
00:17:59,646 --> 00:18:00,771
Keep it down.

381
00:18:01,021 --> 00:18:02,396
What is your friend saying?

382
00:18:02,521 --> 00:18:03,771
Nothing, Uncle. Chill!

383
00:18:04,563 --> 00:18:09,146
It must be because of this sudden meet-up.

384
00:18:09,271 --> 00:18:09,896
That must be it!

385
00:18:10,021 --> 00:18:11,021
You're absolutely right

386
00:18:12,063 --> 00:18:13,938
Magic will not do anything
without a reason.

387
00:18:14,313 --> 00:18:16,021
And if she chooses, she chooses right!

388
00:18:17,021 --> 00:18:18,270
See if everything checks out?

389
00:18:18,271 --> 00:18:20,771
Uncle, that’s all he’s done so far.

390
00:18:20,896 --> 00:18:23,063
Shut up.
It might be some formality.

391
00:18:29,563 --> 00:18:31,896
Looks good to me, Uncle!

392
00:18:32,021 --> 00:18:34,271
Why are you looking there?
Look here.

393
00:18:34,396 --> 00:18:35,396
He is down here.

394
00:18:37,188 --> 00:18:38,271
Him?

395
00:18:38,688 --> 00:18:40,438
Yeah, he's the one I suggested.

396
00:18:40,771 --> 00:18:43,271
I heard you run an athletic camp
in this area?

397
00:18:43,438 --> 00:18:45,646
And he happens to be interested
in athletics.

398
00:18:46,271 --> 00:18:47,938
See if he fits the bill.

399
00:18:50,146 --> 00:18:51,520
Okay, he can join my classes.

400
00:18:51,521 --> 00:18:52,521
You happy, child?

401
00:18:53,438 --> 00:18:55,062
That's it?
Isn't there anything else?

402
00:18:55,063 --> 00:18:55,688
Like what?

403
00:18:56,146 --> 00:18:57,271
What else do you want, bugger?

404
00:18:57,521 --> 00:19:00,021
I'll drop him off tomorrow myself.
Okay?

405
00:19:00,271 --> 00:19:01,396
See you. Bye.

406
00:19:01,521 --> 00:19:02,271
- Yeah, bye.
- Bye!

407
00:19:02,396 --> 00:19:03,521
- See you!
- Come, let's go child!

408
00:19:03,646 --> 00:19:04,895
- She's gone.
- Are you happy?

409
00:19:04,896 --> 00:19:07,646
Dude, don't get upset.

410
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:10,771
If she shared this much with her uncle,
it must be love.

411
00:19:11,396 --> 00:19:12,645
Trust me, dude.

412
00:19:12,646 --> 00:19:14,312
I know everything about Anglo-Indians.

413
00:19:14,313 --> 00:19:15,188
I’ll kill you!

414
00:19:17,646 --> 00:19:18,396
You’re done for!

415
00:19:24,021 --> 00:19:27,146
Keep walking!
What are you waiting for?

416
00:19:27,938 --> 00:19:29,938
♪ Keeping the Lord in my thoughts ♪

417
00:19:30,146 --> 00:19:31,895
I kept on walking

418
00:19:31,896 --> 00:19:32,396
Is it?

419
00:19:32,771 --> 00:19:34,396
God, try to stop me if you can,

420
00:19:34,896 --> 00:19:36,771
I’m going in with full frustration

421
00:19:37,563 --> 00:19:39,521
<i>♪ Keeping the Lord in my thoughts ♪</i>

422
00:19:39,771 --> 00:19:41,646
<i>♪ I kept on Walking ♪</i>

423
00:19:42,313 --> 00:19:43,938
<i>♪ God, try to stop me if you can, ♪</i>

424
00:19:44,438 --> 00:19:46,271
<i>♪ I’m going in with full frustration ♪</i>

425
00:19:46,896 --> 00:19:49,063
<i>♪ Oh, my love, Diana ♪</i>

426
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:51,146
<i>♪ You’re the one I love ♪</i>

427
00:19:52,271 --> 00:19:53,896
<i>♪ If you and I become one ♪</i>

428
00:19:54,021 --> 00:19:56,146
<i>♪ We’ll be lovestruck couples! ♪</i>

429
00:19:57,313 --> 00:19:58,812
<i>♪ I became a total fool because of you ♪</i>

430
00:19:58,813 --> 00:20:01,438
<i>♪ Became a hit and got hurt too ♪</i>

431
00:20:02,146 --> 00:20:03,562
<i>♪ If you touch me, I become fit ♪</i>

432
00:20:03,563 --> 00:20:06,188
<i>♪ But bro,
There’s no “touching” happening here ♪</i>

433
00:20:06,313 --> 00:20:08,646
<i>♪ Sharp girl, Sharp girl ♪</i>

434
00:20:08,771 --> 00:20:11,521
<i>♪ The boy asking for a pair is a dummy ♪</i>

435
00:20:12,688 --> 00:20:13,771
Who’s it for?

436
00:20:14,438 --> 00:20:15,645
Grab a plate.

437
00:20:15,646 --> 00:20:16,396
Hey!

438
00:20:17,396 --> 00:20:18,313
Get lost!

439
00:20:18,688 --> 00:20:20,938
<i>♪ The boy asking for a pair is a dummy ♪</i>

440
00:20:21,146 --> 00:20:25,438
<i>♪ After falling, head over heels,
I’ve turned into a fiery force ♪</i>

441
00:20:25,646 --> 00:20:27,813
You look great in that dress.

442
00:20:28,063 --> 00:20:30,063
- It makes you look like a model.
- Really?

443
00:20:30,188 --> 00:20:31,396
Dude, what’s with him?

444
00:20:32,146 --> 00:20:34,271
Hey, Baba, let's go have some tea.

445
00:20:34,521 --> 00:20:38,146
Your tea addiction
is what gives corporations power.

446
00:20:38,396 --> 00:20:41,021
Consume organic instead.

447
00:20:41,271 --> 00:20:43,520
Did you forget about
your girl in Bangalore?

448
00:20:43,521 --> 00:20:45,395
Stop flirting with every girl you see.

449
00:20:45,396 --> 00:20:47,020
Do you want me to call your girlfriend?

450
00:20:47,021 --> 00:20:47,895
Let’s go to the tea shop.

451
00:20:47,896 --> 00:20:49,271
I'm already in enough trouble.

452
00:20:54,146 --> 00:20:56,770
<i>♪ In your presence,
I lose myself ♪</i>

453
00:20:56,771 --> 00:20:58,896
<i>♪ I've been caught
In love's relentless pull ♪</i>

454
00:20:59,146 --> 00:21:01,562
<i>♪ A flame I shouldn't lay a finger on ♪</i>

455
00:21:01,563 --> 00:21:03,813
<i>♪ Instead of finding love,
I find myself conquered by it ♪</i>

456
00:21:04,021 --> 00:21:06,146
<i>♪ Sharp girl, Sharp girl ♪</i>

457
00:21:06,438 --> 00:21:08,896
<i>♪ The boy asking for a pair is a dummy ♪</i>

458
00:21:09,146 --> 00:21:13,771
<i>♪ After falling, head over heels,
I’ve turned into a fiery force ♪</i>

459
00:21:13,896 --> 00:21:16,063
<i>♪ Sharp girl, Sharp girl ♪</i>

460
00:21:16,271 --> 00:21:18,563
<i>♪ The boy asking for a pair is a dummy ♪</i>

461
00:21:18,688 --> 00:21:23,563
<i>♪ After falling, head over heels,
I’ve turned into a fiery force ♪</i>

462
00:21:30,521 --> 00:21:31,438
What's your next move?

463
00:21:32,646 --> 00:21:33,938
I'm going to have another dosa.

464
00:21:34,188 --> 00:21:38,313
Uncle, he wants to know your plan in life.

465
00:21:38,688 --> 00:21:40,896
Even the kid gets it, but you don't.

466
00:21:41,396 --> 00:21:43,271
- What does he lack?
- Thanks, Mom.

467
00:21:43,438 --> 00:21:45,813
He's a coach.
And earns a good living.

468
00:21:46,021 --> 00:21:47,271
What more does he need?

469
00:21:47,688 --> 00:21:48,396
Look here...

470
00:21:48,646 --> 00:21:51,395
making a living by any means is not life.

471
00:21:51,396 --> 00:21:52,646
Dad is a central government employee.

472
00:21:52,771 --> 00:21:53,896
I work for the state government.

473
00:21:54,063 --> 00:21:56,146
Unless he finds a good government job,
he will find a good girl to marry.

474
00:21:56,271 --> 00:21:57,063
Okay, boomer!

475
00:21:57,313 --> 00:21:58,271
That's enough, Brother!

476
00:21:58,521 --> 00:22:00,895
Studying and working
aren't what life is about either.

477
00:22:00,896 --> 00:22:02,521
It doesn't give you any right
over others.

478
00:22:02,688 --> 00:22:04,896
Everyone has their own version of winning.

479
00:22:05,021 --> 00:22:06,063
Hey, Chiranjeevi!

480
00:22:06,313 --> 00:22:08,396
Stop wasting your time with him.

481
00:22:09,063 --> 00:22:10,688
Let him keep running
in the streets.

482
00:22:11,021 --> 00:22:13,187
When you marry a good girl...

483
00:22:13,188 --> 00:22:14,895
- Then he'll feel jealous.
- Yeah, right!

484
00:22:14,896 --> 00:22:16,313
Sure thing!

485
00:22:16,563 --> 00:22:17,771
I've heard it all before.

486
00:22:18,521 --> 00:22:20,396
It's all a lie, my son!

487
00:22:20,521 --> 00:22:21,646
Every word is a lie!

488
00:22:22,396 --> 00:22:24,396
No matter how successful you become...

489
00:22:24,896 --> 00:22:27,062
you'll only marry a girl you don't like.

490
00:22:27,063 --> 00:22:29,646
Just like I married your mother.

491
00:22:29,896 --> 00:22:31,271
Good lord!

492
00:22:31,688 --> 00:22:33,896
Every day is the same with you.
You're drunk!

493
00:22:34,896 --> 00:22:36,771
Shut up. Don't talk.

494
00:22:39,563 --> 00:22:42,563
The girl I loved
was from a different caste.

495
00:22:42,688 --> 00:22:44,771
So, my Dad got me married to you.

496
00:22:44,896 --> 00:22:45,520
Dad!

497
00:22:45,521 --> 00:22:47,437
It was a loveless marriage.

498
00:22:47,438 --> 00:22:48,021
Sure!

499
00:22:48,146 --> 00:22:51,146
Then explain
how I got pregnant in a month.

500
00:22:51,813 --> 00:22:54,396
That's personal... my weakness

501
00:22:54,521 --> 00:22:55,646
Let's not go there.

502
00:22:56,146 --> 00:22:59,770
The man behind closed doors
isn't the same man outside.

503
00:22:59,771 --> 00:23:01,771
- Right?
- What do you want now?

504
00:23:02,021 --> 00:23:04,021
- What do I want?!
- I ought to!

505
00:23:04,521 --> 00:23:05,521
I want peace!

506
00:23:06,021 --> 00:23:07,938
I want to be rid of you all.

507
00:23:08,396 --> 00:23:09,271
Freedom!

508
00:23:09,521 --> 00:23:11,063
I want freedom!

509
00:23:11,396 --> 00:23:12,896
Can you give me that?

510
00:23:13,646 --> 00:23:16,021
- He's getting out of hand.
- Hey, I won't spare you, people.

511
00:23:25,021 --> 00:23:26,646
Are you going to sleep or not?

512
00:23:26,771 --> 00:23:30,395
Oh, my Shanthi!
My dear, Shanthi!

513
00:23:30,396 --> 00:23:32,062
Always calling her name
instead of mine.

514
00:23:32,063 --> 00:23:34,896
I do all the work,
but she gets the credit.

515
00:23:35,521 --> 00:23:37,938
Don't take it out
while I'm still talking.

516
00:23:39,271 --> 00:23:40,896
I can't hear a thing.

517
00:23:41,021 --> 00:23:42,520
I won't be able to anymore.

518
00:23:42,521 --> 00:23:44,521
Feel free to say anything you want.

519
00:23:49,896 --> 00:23:53,188
Your hair is such a mess to deal with.

520
00:23:54,438 --> 00:23:57,146
- Yay! Daddy! daddy!
- Sweetie!

521
00:23:58,021 --> 00:23:59,063
Welcome, Son-in-law.

522
00:23:59,188 --> 00:24:00,313
Greet him!

523
00:24:02,271 --> 00:24:05,063
You look happy.
Does that mean you won't come back home?

524
00:24:05,813 --> 00:24:07,146
Nothing like that, Son.

525
00:24:07,938 --> 00:24:10,396
She's miserable here without you.

526
00:24:10,521 --> 00:24:12,395
Then why doesn’t she come back home?

527
00:24:12,396 --> 00:24:13,688
Your mom will be there too, right?

528
00:24:13,938 --> 00:24:14,813
What did she do to you?

529
00:24:15,146 --> 00:24:17,396
- Not me, but my daughter--
- Hey!

530
00:24:18,146 --> 00:24:19,271
She calls her a nutcase.

531
00:24:19,521 --> 00:24:20,146
Sathya?

532
00:24:20,521 --> 00:24:21,646
I keep trying to explain...

533
00:24:21,771 --> 00:24:23,021
What mild autism is?

534
00:24:24,521 --> 00:24:25,770
If she were fully autistic,

535
00:24:25,771 --> 00:24:26,938
she might have killed her.

536
00:24:27,063 --> 00:24:28,521
How's it my fault
if she doesn't understand?

537
00:24:28,688 --> 00:24:29,813
I'm still fond of my kid.

538
00:24:29,938 --> 00:24:31,771
It's the only reason I still speak to you.

539
00:24:31,896 --> 00:24:33,896
I am asking you to live as a family
away from your folks.

540
00:24:34,771 --> 00:24:35,770
If you're not on board...

541
00:24:35,771 --> 00:24:38,395
I'd rather stay here at my mothers
for my kid.

542
00:24:38,396 --> 00:24:39,021
Hey!

543
00:24:39,563 --> 00:24:40,938
What are you talking about?

544
00:24:41,688 --> 00:24:43,646
Life is all about compromises.

545
00:24:44,021 --> 00:24:47,521
I searched our whole community
to find you a respectable family.

546
00:24:47,938 --> 00:24:49,271
He's a great husband!

547
00:24:50,063 --> 00:24:52,563
Did you think I will feed you forever?

548
00:24:52,896 --> 00:24:54,188
It's okay if you don't feed me.

549
00:24:54,813 --> 00:24:56,021
I can live on my own.

550
00:24:56,521 --> 00:24:57,896
I'll raise her alone.

551
00:24:59,396 --> 00:25:01,646
No one can enslave an educated woman.

552
00:25:20,771 --> 00:25:21,771
Next, to this side.

553
00:25:22,021 --> 00:25:22,771
Krishna?

554
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:24,521
- Hi!
- Hey, Bugger!

555
00:25:25,146 --> 00:25:26,021
He's all yours!

556
00:25:26,563 --> 00:25:27,021
Huh?

557
00:25:27,188 --> 00:25:28,646
She says he's your responsibility
from now on.

558
00:25:28,771 --> 00:25:30,146
Can’t you even understand that?

559
00:25:30,563 --> 00:25:31,271
Useless!

560
00:25:31,396 --> 00:25:33,271
I never said I didn't get it.

561
00:25:33,396 --> 00:25:34,438
I just didn't hear it.

562
00:25:34,646 --> 00:25:35,521
Soon to judge!

563
00:25:36,271 --> 00:25:38,271
- Hey, child. Say hi to your coach.
- Hi, Coach!

564
00:25:38,438 --> 00:25:39,771
Hi, come here!

565
00:25:40,271 --> 00:25:41,937
What's your full name?

566
00:25:41,938 --> 00:25:43,063
Alexander Arnold.

567
00:25:43,438 --> 00:25:44,813
Alexander Arnold...

568
00:25:45,146 --> 00:25:46,021
Whatever!

569
00:25:46,396 --> 00:25:47,937
Follow those kids and start running.

570
00:25:47,938 --> 00:25:49,646
- Run! Run! Run!
- Yes, coach.

571
00:25:50,396 --> 00:25:52,396
Hey, Bugger, thank you.

572
00:25:53,271 --> 00:25:55,271
- We'll wait there. Come on.
- Please carry on.

573
00:25:55,521 --> 00:25:56,813
- Bye.
- Get lost!

574
00:26:03,646 --> 00:26:05,021
Everyone, start stretching!

575
00:26:05,271 --> 00:26:08,896
You're looking at him as if you’ve
just met him for the first time.

576
00:26:10,771 --> 00:26:11,688
Crazy bugger!

577
00:26:12,021 --> 00:26:14,396
He hasn’t changed a bit since college.

578
00:26:21,146 --> 00:26:23,896
<i>♪ She's as dazzling as a glass marble ♪</i>

579
00:26:24,146 --> 00:26:27,271
<i>♪ Your silent gaze overwhelms me ♪</i>

580
00:26:27,521 --> 00:26:30,271
<i>♪ She's dazzling enough to slay ♪</i>

581
00:26:30,646 --> 00:26:32,813
<i>♪ I'm swept by strange feelings ♪</i>

582
00:26:33,896 --> 00:26:36,646
<i>♪ There's barely time for a hello ♪</i>

583
00:26:38,188 --> 00:26:40,563
- Nice glasses!
- It's a fake.

584
00:26:40,771 --> 00:26:41,896
I just wear it for style.

585
00:26:43,521 --> 00:26:45,563
<i>♪ My whole world is changing ♪</i>

586
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:47,688
- Hang on a minute.
- Hi!

587
00:26:48,021 --> 00:26:50,896
I’ve always wanted to explore street food.

588
00:26:51,271 --> 00:26:52,521
Can you take me?

589
00:26:53,021 --> 00:26:54,438
You see...

590
00:26:55,688 --> 00:26:56,812
I'll pay for it.

591
00:26:56,813 --> 00:26:58,063
Fine, let's go!

592
00:26:58,271 --> 00:26:59,646
Cheap skate!

593
00:26:59,896 --> 00:27:00,271
Come!

594
00:27:00,438 --> 00:27:06,562
<i>♪ Walking with you,
I wish the road would never end ♪</i>

595
00:27:06,563 --> 00:27:12,938
<i>♪ I'm not myself anymore...
Enough, enough ♪</i>

596
00:27:13,146 --> 00:27:18,688
<i>♪ At that quiet moment,
I'll stand by you, hand in hand ♪</i>

597
00:27:22,521 --> 00:27:25,396
<i>♪ Will this moment last a little longer? ♪</i>

598
00:27:28,896 --> 00:27:31,437
<i>♪ I pleaded with tears in my eyes ♪</i>

599
00:27:31,438 --> 00:27:32,146
Wow!

600
00:27:35,313 --> 00:27:38,146
<i>♪ Will this moment last a little longer? ♪</i>

601
00:27:41,688 --> 00:27:43,938
<i>♪ I pleaded with tears in my eyes ♪</i>

602
00:27:44,271 --> 00:27:45,438
Amazing!

603
00:27:46,063 --> 00:27:47,646
It's like a wonderland.

604
00:27:48,021 --> 00:27:48,563
Hey!

605
00:27:49,021 --> 00:27:49,771
Wonderland?

606
00:27:50,188 --> 00:27:51,688
- That's a good name for it.
- Yeah!

607
00:28:05,188 --> 00:28:06,145
Hey, Bugger!

608
00:28:06,146 --> 00:28:08,396
What was so important
that you had to tell me?

609
00:28:08,521 --> 00:28:11,770
Tomorrow, we have to perform
a skit at college.

610
00:28:11,771 --> 00:28:13,021
That too, in English.

611
00:28:13,146 --> 00:28:15,396
You're well aware of my English.

612
00:28:16,271 --> 00:28:17,813
I had it written in Tamil.

613
00:28:18,021 --> 00:28:20,396
Can you please translate it into English?

614
00:28:22,313 --> 00:28:23,271
Is that all?

615
00:28:23,938 --> 00:28:25,312
Is this what you call important?

616
00:28:25,313 --> 00:28:26,146
That's it

617
00:28:26,271 --> 00:28:27,188
What else?

618
00:28:28,396 --> 00:28:29,146
Fine, tell me.

619
00:28:36,146 --> 00:28:36,896
My love!

620
00:28:37,771 --> 00:28:40,021
In this fast-paced world...

621
00:28:40,521 --> 00:28:44,188
the only face
that brings me peace is yours.

622
00:28:45,521 --> 00:28:47,771
Even though my mind is filled
with thousands of thoughts...

623
00:28:48,146 --> 00:28:52,021
Your name is the only one among them.

624
00:28:54,146 --> 00:28:55,563
This is not just love.

625
00:28:56,271 --> 00:28:57,396
It's a promise.

626
00:28:58,521 --> 00:29:00,438
This is not just a moment's feeling...

627
00:29:00,896 --> 00:29:02,271
It's a lifetime decision!

628
00:29:05,521 --> 00:29:06,396
Magic...

629
00:29:08,021 --> 00:29:08,771
I love you!

630
00:29:37,646 --> 00:29:38,813
- Me too--
- This is a dialogue from my skit.

631
00:29:40,896 --> 00:29:42,188
Oh, okay, okay.

632
00:29:42,771 --> 00:29:44,271
Were you about to say something?

633
00:29:45,521 --> 00:29:47,313
Were you about to say something?
I interrupted!

634
00:29:47,438 --> 00:29:48,895
Nothing! I'm leaving!

635
00:29:48,896 --> 00:29:50,438
Wait! Magic? Magic!

636
00:29:50,896 --> 00:29:51,771
Magic!

637
00:29:53,063 --> 00:29:53,771
Magic!

638
00:29:57,438 --> 00:30:00,021
<i>Some power held him back that day
from proposing his love to me.</i>

639
00:30:00,646 --> 00:30:02,771
So far, I respect that power.

640
00:30:03,771 --> 00:30:05,438
I believe Jesus is guiding me.

641
00:30:07,021 --> 00:30:08,063
I have a doubt.

642
00:30:08,521 --> 00:30:10,146
Millions of people worship Him.

643
00:30:10,396 --> 00:30:12,021
Everyone shares their trouble.

644
00:30:12,146 --> 00:30:13,563
But ignoring it all...

645
00:30:13,771 --> 00:30:16,521
He’s getting in the way of you two.

646
00:30:16,646 --> 00:30:18,063
Some nerve, I say.

647
00:30:18,188 --> 00:30:19,771
Are you mocking me?

648
00:30:20,021 --> 00:30:20,813
What do you think?

649
00:30:21,021 --> 00:30:23,271
If you like the guy,
just marry him already.

650
00:30:23,396 --> 00:30:24,271
Instead,

651
00:30:24,396 --> 00:30:26,396
My liking him alone doesn't matter.

652
00:30:26,771 --> 00:30:27,688
Our family matters too!

653
00:30:28,438 --> 00:30:29,396
Moreover...

654
00:30:29,688 --> 00:30:31,521
I like him. That's about it.

655
00:30:32,313 --> 00:30:34,896
There's a world of difference
between liking someone and loving them.

656
00:30:36,021 --> 00:30:36,771
Let's see!

657
00:30:43,188 --> 00:30:46,771
I'd say they're closer than you think.

658
00:31:02,563 --> 00:31:03,396
What happened, Dad?

659
00:31:04,396 --> 00:31:05,521
It's about Barbara.

660
00:31:06,271 --> 00:31:07,145
What happened to her?

661
00:31:07,146 --> 00:31:07,813
What do you think?!

662
00:31:08,396 --> 00:31:09,896
She's pregnant now!

663
00:31:11,313 --> 00:31:12,771
How many times did I warn you?

664
00:31:13,146 --> 00:31:14,896
To be careful
with these bloody Tamil buggers.

665
00:31:15,521 --> 00:31:17,146
She never bloody listens to me.

666
00:31:17,271 --> 00:31:18,438
Hold your horses, Davey!

667
00:31:19,063 --> 00:31:20,063
This is our daughter.

668
00:31:20,521 --> 00:31:21,938
No use in yelling.

669
00:31:22,271 --> 00:31:24,021
Magic, take your cousin inside.

670
00:31:24,813 --> 00:31:25,646
Yeah, sure.

671
00:31:28,146 --> 00:31:29,521
Contact a family doctor.

672
00:31:29,688 --> 00:31:30,770
Let's abort it!

673
00:31:30,771 --> 00:31:31,562
Don't be stupid, man.

674
00:31:31,563 --> 00:31:32,063
See, Dave

675
00:31:32,563 --> 00:31:33,313
Listen...

676
00:31:33,521 --> 00:31:35,188
Let's talk to the Tamil guy first.

677
00:31:35,438 --> 00:31:37,188
Let's see where his family stands
on this matter.

678
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:39,895
You can certainly speak
with the Tamil guy's family.

679
00:31:39,896 --> 00:31:40,438
Say what?

680
00:31:41,646 --> 00:31:42,938
You want me to talk to those folks?

681
00:31:43,896 --> 00:31:45,396
It's embarrassing to even admit.

682
00:31:45,771 --> 00:31:47,895
The grand daughter of Randy Wilkins
is marrying a Tamil--

683
00:31:47,896 --> 00:31:49,896
What man!
You're being stupid!

684
00:31:50,396 --> 00:31:52,437
Dave, you were born
and raised here after all.

685
00:31:52,438 --> 00:31:56,313
Where did all this pride come from?

686
00:31:59,396 --> 00:32:01,395
What?
Is this a joke to you?

687
00:32:01,396 --> 00:32:02,396
Then what, man?

688
00:32:02,521 --> 00:32:05,271
More than your family and pride...

689
00:32:05,396 --> 00:32:07,020
your daughter's happiness
is most important.

690
00:32:07,021 --> 00:32:09,396
Listen, Dave,
her happiness is most important.

691
00:32:09,521 --> 00:32:11,021
He was never going to
tell his folks about us.

692
00:32:11,646 --> 00:32:12,646
Cheater!

693
00:32:15,813 --> 00:32:17,021
Our boys are best!

694
00:32:17,896 --> 00:32:19,021
After getting married...

695
00:32:19,396 --> 00:32:21,271
we should just move to
Australia or England and settle down.

696
00:32:22,188 --> 00:32:24,563
We have no future in this place.

697
00:32:26,896 --> 00:32:29,271
Magic, I only have one thing to say to you.

698
00:32:30,646 --> 00:32:32,563
Don't fall for these Tamil guys.

699
00:32:34,063 --> 00:32:35,313
Bum Buggers!

700
00:32:45,646 --> 00:32:46,271
Big sis!

701
00:32:46,521 --> 00:32:47,937
My daughter just graduated college.

702
00:32:47,938 --> 00:32:49,563
Since she wishes to continue
her studies in Chennai.

703
00:32:49,896 --> 00:32:51,271
So we came for admission.

704
00:32:51,521 --> 00:32:53,396
- Graduated, huh?
- Yeah!

705
00:32:54,521 --> 00:32:55,187
Brother! Brother!

706
00:32:55,188 --> 00:32:55,896
Where are you off to?

707
00:32:56,021 --> 00:32:56,771
Get over here!

708
00:32:56,896 --> 00:32:57,896
Give her your blessing.

709
00:32:58,396 --> 00:32:59,646
What’s all this for?

710
00:33:00,271 --> 00:33:01,187
Best of luck, dear!

711
00:33:01,188 --> 00:33:02,271
We wish you all the best.

712
00:33:02,396 --> 00:33:02,938
Please sit.

713
00:33:04,146 --> 00:33:04,771
Brother-in-law!

714
00:33:05,021 --> 00:33:05,771
She's a topper!

715
00:33:05,896 --> 00:33:06,645
Is that so?

716
00:33:06,646 --> 00:33:07,521
Very good! Very good!

717
00:33:07,771 --> 00:33:10,271
Even the principal
wrote her a letter of appreciation.

718
00:33:10,813 --> 00:33:11,771
Impressive!

719
00:33:12,396 --> 00:33:13,646
Quick! Quick!

720
00:33:17,021 --> 00:33:18,021
- Oh, no!
- What's wrong?

721
00:33:18,563 --> 00:33:20,063
I can't read Telugu.

722
00:33:20,646 --> 00:33:22,521
It slipped my mind. Hand it to me.

723
00:33:22,896 --> 00:33:23,813
You read it out.

724
00:33:23,938 --> 00:33:25,438
That won't be necessary.

725
00:33:25,563 --> 00:33:28,313
Krishna needs to get married
in two months.

726
00:33:28,688 --> 00:33:30,771
Let’s get them married first,
she can study later.

727
00:33:30,896 --> 00:33:32,395
She can attend the college
from here, too.

728
00:33:32,396 --> 00:33:33,521
No problem!

729
00:33:33,771 --> 00:33:35,521
I had the same idea, Big sis.

730
00:33:35,646 --> 00:33:36,813
Tanisha would like the same.

731
00:33:37,521 --> 00:33:39,813
- Is that right?
- I had the same thought, Auntie.

732
00:33:40,188 --> 00:33:41,563
The man of the hour is here!

733
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:43,813
Couldn’t have picked a worse timing.

734
00:33:44,813 --> 00:33:46,521
Big sis, so is this official?

735
00:33:46,646 --> 00:33:48,771
Hey! Whatever I say goes!

736
00:33:49,021 --> 00:33:50,396
I don't go back on my word.

737
00:33:50,646 --> 00:33:52,188
Your daughter is for Krishna.

738
00:33:52,313 --> 00:33:53,688
That's enough, sis.

739
00:33:55,146 --> 00:33:56,645
We can have the wedding next month.

740
00:33:56,646 --> 00:33:57,937
Sure thing!

741
00:33:57,938 --> 00:34:00,688
I'll fix the engagement date soon.

742
00:34:01,646 --> 00:34:03,438
You're fine with it, right?

743
00:34:10,396 --> 00:34:12,521
Ye-- Yes, Mom!

744
00:34:13,021 --> 00:34:13,646
Super!

745
00:34:17,521 --> 00:34:18,646
There you go!

746
00:34:18,771 --> 00:34:20,312
- What do you say?
- Super.

747
00:34:20,313 --> 00:34:21,771
What about you?

748
00:34:28,896 --> 00:34:30,646
What did you say to me?

749
00:34:31,146 --> 00:34:33,270
That I can go anywhere
from Madras to Mumbai.

750
00:34:33,271 --> 00:34:35,520
But your love for me remains steady.

751
00:34:35,521 --> 00:34:38,645
And now you want to marry
Lawrence Thangaraj.

752
00:34:38,646 --> 00:34:40,520
<i>While you're there...</i>

753
00:34:40,521 --> 00:34:42,645
<i>How do you expect me
to overcome my needs?</i>

754
00:34:42,646 --> 00:34:45,313
Oh!
Now you care about your needs?

755
00:34:45,688 --> 00:34:47,395
But when I tried to make a move on you...

756
00:34:47,396 --> 00:34:49,020
didn’t you say you were
saving yourself for marriage.

757
00:34:49,021 --> 00:34:51,771
<i>So, you'd never make a move.
You're useless!</i>

758
00:34:51,938 --> 00:34:52,770
<i>Hang up!</i>

759
00:34:52,771 --> 00:34:54,270
Don't hang up! Don't--

760
00:34:54,271 --> 00:34:55,313
Damn, that woman!

761
00:34:55,438 --> 00:34:57,188
- Right! Smash it on your head.
- Hey, Baba!

762
00:34:58,021 --> 00:34:59,521
Are you nuts?
What are you doing?

763
00:34:59,646 --> 00:35:01,188
Hey, morons!

764
00:35:01,438 --> 00:35:04,146
How could you not stop him from
smashing the bottle against his head?

765
00:35:04,271 --> 00:35:05,896
You just got here
and don't run your mouth.

766
00:35:06,021 --> 00:35:08,521
For the past two hours,
he spoke about everything he wanted to.

767
00:35:08,688 --> 00:35:10,063
It's his third time around.

768
00:35:10,188 --> 00:35:11,645
That too after having half a beer.

769
00:35:11,646 --> 00:35:13,896
- What is all this?
- She threw me away!

770
00:35:14,688 --> 00:35:15,812
My love is doomed!

771
00:35:15,813 --> 00:35:16,688
Five years down the drain.

772
00:35:18,146 --> 00:35:20,521
I'm at the brink of getting drunk myself.

773
00:35:21,438 --> 00:35:23,937
Did your girl leave you too?

774
00:35:23,938 --> 00:35:26,146
She has to love him first
before she can leave him.

775
00:35:26,271 --> 00:35:27,771
It's unrequited love, Dude.

776
00:35:28,021 --> 00:35:29,396
Five years of love!

777
00:35:29,646 --> 00:35:30,896
It's all gone now.

778
00:35:31,271 --> 00:35:32,771
Hey, Bangalore!

779
00:35:32,896 --> 00:35:34,520
If you call it unrequited love again...

780
00:35:34,521 --> 00:35:36,188
I'll crack your head open with this bottle.

781
00:35:36,563 --> 00:35:37,396
Pissing me off!

782
00:35:37,938 --> 00:35:40,188
I’m being forced to marry my cousin.

783
00:35:40,313 --> 00:35:41,771
That’s good news!

784
00:35:41,896 --> 00:35:42,520
Please marry her!

785
00:35:42,521 --> 00:35:44,646
Either way, you won't propose to Magic.

786
00:35:49,021 --> 00:35:50,271
Why do you guys do this to me?

787
00:35:50,938 --> 00:35:54,645
I can neither get the approval
of my mother

788
00:35:54,646 --> 00:35:56,770
nor can I confess my love to the girl

789
00:35:56,771 --> 00:35:59,271
so, as my last resort,
I came to my friends to vent out...

790
00:35:59,646 --> 00:36:01,771
but all you guys do is mock me.

791
00:36:02,646 --> 00:36:04,646
You can’t even empathize
with your friend.

792
00:36:04,813 --> 00:36:06,938
Are you even good friends?

793
00:36:08,021 --> 00:36:08,896
Hey!

794
00:36:09,813 --> 00:36:11,437
What do you want from us?

795
00:36:11,438 --> 00:36:13,270
You proposed to her
during your days in college...

796
00:36:13,271 --> 00:36:14,396
and still moping around for her reply.

797
00:36:15,021 --> 00:36:16,063
I’ll smack you!

798
00:36:16,563 --> 00:36:19,188
Call her right away
and find out whether she loves you.

799
00:36:19,563 --> 00:36:21,146
Enough with the crocodile tears.

800
00:36:22,271 --> 00:36:23,520
You have a point!

801
00:36:23,521 --> 00:36:24,521
- I'm calling her right now.
- Do it!

802
00:36:29,146 --> 00:36:30,021
<i>What’s up, Krishna?</i>

803
00:36:31,396 --> 00:36:32,021
Magic!

804
00:36:32,396 --> 00:36:34,437
I want to talk to you
about something important.

805
00:36:34,438 --> 00:36:35,313
<i>What about?</i>

806
00:36:37,688 --> 00:36:38,938
It's about our love.

807
00:36:39,063 --> 00:36:41,563
<i>Look, Krishna, talk about anything else.</i>

808
00:36:41,938 --> 00:36:44,813
<i>Don’t ever call me about love.
You irritating Bugger!</i>

809
00:36:45,146 --> 00:36:45,896
Magic--

810
00:36:48,521 --> 00:36:49,063
"Bugger."

811
00:37:00,896 --> 00:37:03,021
Shall I call Magic again?

812
00:37:03,146 --> 00:37:06,271
Dude, check out the time.
It's 02:30 a.m.

813
00:37:06,396 --> 00:37:07,312
Just go to sleep!

814
00:37:07,313 --> 00:37:09,020
She works in an Australian shift.

815
00:37:09,021 --> 00:37:10,646
She would have just left for work.

816
00:37:10,896 --> 00:37:12,187
If I don’t act now...

817
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,688
I'll end up marrying my cousin.

818
00:37:13,896 --> 00:37:16,646
This will be last attempt with Magic.

819
00:37:16,771 --> 00:37:19,062
If it doesn't work,
I'll marry my cousin.

820
00:37:19,063 --> 00:37:21,813
So as soon as you drop me off,
I'm going to call her.

821
00:37:21,938 --> 00:37:24,437
Are you not ashamed of yourself?

822
00:37:24,438 --> 00:37:26,896
You still want to call her
after all the humiliation.

823
00:37:27,021 --> 00:37:28,396
A man should be the dominant one.

824
00:37:28,813 --> 00:37:31,646
Right!
I'm a man, and I should be dominant.

825
00:37:31,771 --> 00:37:33,063
- I won't call her again.
- Don't!

826
00:37:33,271 --> 00:37:34,521
Never in my life!

827
00:37:34,896 --> 00:37:37,563
Stop it! Stop it!

828
00:37:38,563 --> 00:37:39,521
What happened?

829
00:37:40,646 --> 00:37:42,063
What are you doing?

830
00:37:42,271 --> 00:37:43,896
I'm calling Magic.

831
00:37:44,313 --> 00:37:45,688
For God’s sake!

832
00:37:46,063 --> 00:37:47,145
Shameless fellow!

833
00:37:47,146 --> 00:37:50,021
Love leaves no space for shame.

834
00:37:54,521 --> 00:37:56,813
Hey, bugger! What do you want?

835
00:37:56,938 --> 00:37:58,270
Call me whatever you prefer...

836
00:37:58,271 --> 00:38:00,020
but don't ever call me Bugger!

837
00:38:00,021 --> 00:38:00,896
Oh, God!

838
00:38:01,021 --> 00:38:02,395
What do you want, Krishna?

839
00:38:02,396 --> 00:38:05,396
Am I not allowed to speak anymore?

840
00:38:06,396 --> 00:38:07,271
Look here, Krishna.

841
00:38:07,646 --> 00:38:09,688
You can talk anything apart from love.

842
00:38:09,813 --> 00:38:11,146
<i>We're still good friends.</i>

843
00:38:11,396 --> 00:38:12,021
<i>Of course!</i>

844
00:38:12,271 --> 00:38:15,770
All these years,
I've loved only you and waited for you.

845
00:38:15,771 --> 00:38:16,688
I deserve it!

846
00:38:16,813 --> 00:38:17,646
This is how you'd treat me.

847
00:38:17,771 --> 00:38:20,062
Because you take boys for granted.

848
00:38:20,063 --> 00:38:21,562
<i>Hello! Slow down!</i>

849
00:38:21,563 --> 00:38:22,438
Why should I?

850
00:38:22,646 --> 00:38:25,396
You can't just drive recklessly
because there's no traffic.

851
00:38:25,646 --> 00:38:27,313
Oh, not me!

852
00:38:27,896 --> 00:38:28,937
You'd better be afraid of me.

853
00:38:28,938 --> 00:38:30,146
Afraid?

854
00:38:30,396 --> 00:38:31,188
Afraid of what?

855
00:38:31,438 --> 00:38:32,271
Afraid of...?

856
00:38:33,646 --> 00:38:36,271
You're just afraid of
falling in love with me.

857
00:38:37,563 --> 00:38:40,063
Are you guys still using
these corny dialogues?

858
00:38:40,646 --> 00:38:42,021
- So funny!
- Sure!

859
00:38:42,396 --> 00:38:43,396
We are funny!

860
00:38:43,563 --> 00:38:45,813
It must be so funny
to have someone love you this much.

861
00:38:46,021 --> 00:38:48,771
It must be funny watching us suffer.

862
00:38:48,938 --> 00:38:50,145
Until my final breath--

863
00:38:50,146 --> 00:38:52,896
<i>Hey, don't you have any sense?
Can't you hear me?</i>

864
00:38:53,813 --> 00:38:56,271
<i>Don't you comprehend anything?
I'm being patient with you.</i>

865
00:38:56,563 --> 00:38:58,437
<i>If you keep this up,
I'll file a complaint.</i>

866
00:38:58,438 --> 00:39:00,020
Magic, I didn't mean to.

867
00:39:00,021 --> 00:39:02,021
The car shouldn't go over
40 Miles per hour.

868
00:39:02,396 --> 00:39:04,021
<i>He's simply bloody irritating.</i>

869
00:39:04,396 --> 00:39:05,396
Not me again.

870
00:39:06,271 --> 00:39:07,146
Tell me!

871
00:39:07,521 --> 00:39:08,396
<i>Look, Magic...</i>

872
00:39:08,563 --> 00:39:10,687
I have no ounce of self-respect.

873
00:39:10,688 --> 00:39:12,563
It’s impossible to humiliate me.

874
00:39:12,688 --> 00:39:14,145
Even in sudden death...

875
00:39:14,146 --> 00:39:15,688
I'll love you!

876
00:39:21,146 --> 00:39:21,771
Hello?

877
00:39:22,313 --> 00:39:23,021
Hello?

878
00:39:23,146 --> 00:39:25,146
<i>- My head is injured.</i>
- Hello, Magic?

879
00:39:25,688 --> 00:39:28,063
<i>[over phone]
See what happened out there.</i>

880
00:39:29,146 --> 00:39:30,271
<i>Check what happened to Madam.</i>

881
00:39:30,438 --> 00:39:31,562
Hello? Hello?

882
00:39:31,563 --> 00:39:33,146
<i>- She's bleeding!</i>
- Bleeding?

883
00:39:33,771 --> 00:39:35,396
<i>Hey, help me move.</i>

884
00:39:35,771 --> 00:39:36,938
<i>Take them to hospital.</i>

885
00:39:38,188 --> 00:39:39,146
<i>Be careful!</i>

886
00:39:40,646 --> 00:39:41,770
<i>She was on a call.
Where's her phone?</i>

887
00:39:41,771 --> 00:39:43,020
Someone pick up the phone.

888
00:39:43,021 --> 00:39:43,437
<i>There it is!</i>

889
00:39:43,438 --> 00:39:45,146
Please pick up the phone.

890
00:39:46,021 --> 00:39:46,646
<i>Hello!</i>

891
00:39:46,771 --> 00:39:48,271
- It hurts!
- It's alright

892
00:39:53,771 --> 00:39:55,021
How did it happen?

893
00:39:55,771 --> 00:39:58,188
Rash driving!

894
00:39:58,521 --> 00:40:00,188
Did you tell him to slow down?

895
00:40:00,313 --> 00:40:03,313
I kept repeating it.

896
00:40:03,438 --> 00:40:04,563
What about the security?

897
00:40:05,396 --> 00:40:07,521
Sir, you're needed out here.

898
00:40:07,646 --> 00:40:08,521
I'll be right back.

899
00:40:09,271 --> 00:40:10,646
Okay, okay, please don't cry.

900
00:40:14,396 --> 00:40:14,813
Hey!

901
00:40:15,271 --> 00:40:16,813
You caused this!

902
00:40:19,646 --> 00:40:23,521
You proposed your love,
and I met with an accident.

903
00:40:25,271 --> 00:40:29,020
Didn’t I tell you we weren’t meant to be?

904
00:40:29,021 --> 00:40:30,396
Yeah, you did!

905
00:40:30,771 --> 00:40:31,896
Now look here.

906
00:40:32,271 --> 00:40:36,520
My favorite T-shirt is covered in blood.

907
00:40:36,521 --> 00:40:37,813
Relax!

908
00:40:38,021 --> 00:40:39,021
How did this happen?

909
00:40:39,646 --> 00:40:40,396
Magic...

910
00:40:41,688 --> 00:40:44,396
Sir, he applied sudden brake...

911
00:40:44,938 --> 00:40:49,896
and it caused me
to bump into the front seat.

912
00:40:50,271 --> 00:40:52,521
Sir, can't you come at a better time?

913
00:40:52,646 --> 00:40:53,771
Do you have to inquire right away?

914
00:40:53,896 --> 00:40:55,271
You can file the report later.

915
00:40:55,438 --> 00:40:56,937
Can't you see she's in pain?

916
00:40:56,938 --> 00:41:00,063
Isn't she your colleague?
Can't you wait until she returns to work?

917
00:41:00,396 --> 00:41:01,521
Leave and mind you business.

918
00:41:03,396 --> 00:41:05,812
So, am I not allowed
to treat my patients?

919
00:41:05,813 --> 00:41:06,521
Wait, what?

920
00:41:06,771 --> 00:41:08,396
Oh, no, he is a Doctor!

921
00:41:08,896 --> 00:41:12,145
- Sorry! Sorry!
- Can’t you get anything right?

922
00:41:12,146 --> 00:41:13,020
Sorry, Magic!

923
00:41:13,021 --> 00:41:14,437
I swear
I didn't know he was a Doctor.

924
00:41:14,438 --> 00:41:15,813
- I can barely lift my hand.
- Doctor!

925
00:41:16,021 --> 00:41:16,771
Sir! Sir!

926
00:41:17,021 --> 00:41:17,771
Sir!

927
00:41:18,021 --> 00:41:19,062
- Sorry about that.
- What now?

928
00:41:19,063 --> 00:41:21,063
I didn’t know you were a doctor.
I'm sorry.

929
00:41:21,313 --> 00:41:23,063
Please come back.

930
00:41:23,521 --> 00:41:24,521
Please, Sir.

931
00:41:25,271 --> 00:41:26,063
Magic.

932
00:41:30,438 --> 00:41:32,645
Nurse, tend to her wounds
and bandage them.

933
00:41:32,646 --> 00:41:33,313
Okay, Doctor.

934
00:41:34,271 --> 00:41:35,813
- Get her to an X-ray.
- Yes, sir.

935
00:41:39,521 --> 00:41:40,771
Now, where is that X-ray?

936
00:41:49,896 --> 00:41:51,770
I was the driver.

937
00:41:51,771 --> 00:41:53,521
Weren’t you the punk at Shalimar
the other day?

938
00:41:54,021 --> 00:41:55,896
You don't know how to drive.
But aspire to fly it.

939
00:42:02,146 --> 00:42:03,146
What happened?

940
00:42:03,438 --> 00:42:05,313
Watch where you’re going!

941
00:42:14,396 --> 00:42:15,896
Nurse, is she feeling better?

942
00:42:16,146 --> 00:42:17,187
Nothing to worry about.

943
00:42:17,188 --> 00:42:18,312
She’s been given six stitches.

944
00:42:18,313 --> 00:42:19,521
You can see your sister now.

945
00:42:19,771 --> 00:42:20,396
Sister?

946
00:42:20,813 --> 00:42:22,271
Do we look like siblings to you?

947
00:42:22,396 --> 00:42:23,063
Get lost!

948
00:42:32,188 --> 00:42:32,896
Magic?

949
00:42:33,438 --> 00:42:35,563
You're alright. We can leave.

950
00:42:37,271 --> 00:42:37,896
Magic?!

951
00:42:39,021 --> 00:42:40,895
- I’ll call you back
- Are you okay?

952
00:42:40,896 --> 00:42:42,771
Baby girl, what happened?

953
00:42:42,896 --> 00:42:44,313
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine!

954
00:42:44,896 --> 00:42:45,771
This is Krishna.

955
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:46,646
My best friend!

956
00:42:46,896 --> 00:42:48,688
He came at the right time
and helped me.

957
00:42:48,938 --> 00:42:50,770
Thank you.
Thank you so much, man

958
00:42:50,771 --> 00:42:51,771
I really appreciate it.

959
00:42:52,021 --> 00:42:53,520
I'll take her from here and go home.

960
00:42:53,521 --> 00:42:54,270
Thanks again!

961
00:42:54,271 --> 00:42:56,520
Dude, go bring the car.
Go quickly!

962
00:42:56,521 --> 00:42:57,937
Careful

963
00:42:57,938 --> 00:42:59,771
- Let's go.
- Take it slow.

964
00:43:00,896 --> 00:43:01,896
Mom, Dad.

965
00:43:02,188 --> 00:43:03,646
Just give me two minutes, okay?

966
00:43:04,021 --> 00:43:04,771
I'll be there.

967
00:43:05,313 --> 00:43:06,146
- Just two minutes
- Okay

968
00:43:06,271 --> 00:43:07,146
Come on, let's go.

969
00:43:10,396 --> 00:43:12,395
She’s talking personally.
Leave her.

970
00:43:12,396 --> 00:43:13,438
That’s her business.

971
00:43:13,896 --> 00:43:14,896
Sorry, Krishna.

972
00:43:15,521 --> 00:43:16,896
I said many things out of pain.

973
00:43:17,771 --> 00:43:18,771
It's okay, Magic.

974
00:43:19,563 --> 00:43:20,771
Take care of your health.

975
00:43:21,646 --> 00:43:22,813
Yeah, sure!

976
00:43:23,521 --> 00:43:24,771
- See you later.
- Bye.

977
00:43:28,521 --> 00:43:29,271
Hey, Bugger.

978
00:43:31,146 --> 00:43:32,021
Hey, careful!

979
00:43:35,521 --> 00:43:36,521
Here's your report.

980
00:43:37,896 --> 00:43:38,688
Thanks.

981
00:43:45,646 --> 00:43:46,938
<i>♪ Don't drift away... ♪</i>

982
00:43:48,021 --> 00:43:51,521
<i>♪ A bloom whose eyes
Leave hearts enchanted ♪</i>

983
00:43:52,021 --> 00:43:54,895
<i>♪ You bloom with honeyed sweetness ♪</i>

984
00:43:54,896 --> 00:43:56,146
<i>♪ Don't drift away ♪</i>

985
00:43:57,146 --> 00:43:59,396
<i>♪ A bewitching flame of longing ♪</i>

986
00:43:59,646 --> 00:44:00,646
<i>♪ So gently, ♪</i>

987
00:44:01,188 --> 00:44:02,895
<i>♪ You set my heart ablaze ♪</i>

988
00:44:02,896 --> 00:44:04,020
<i>♪ And stole it away ♪</i>

989
00:44:04,021 --> 00:44:06,021
<i>♪ You turn back just once ♪</i>

990
00:44:06,313 --> 00:44:08,645
<i>♪ Yet that single glance
Haunts me for countless moments ♪</i>

991
00:44:08,646 --> 00:44:09,396
<i>♪ In an instant ♪</i>

992
00:44:09,521 --> 00:44:12,646
<i>♪ My heart melts. ♪</i>

993
00:44:13,146 --> 00:44:14,271
<i>♪ Standing close to me ♪</i>

994
00:44:14,438 --> 00:44:17,396
<i>♪ Your quiet whispers a thousand lessons ♪</i>

995
00:44:17,771 --> 00:44:19,687
<i>♪ Like rain sinking into thirsty sand ♪</i>

996
00:44:19,688 --> 00:44:22,312
<i>♪ You slip into every part of me,
Again and again. ♪</i>

997
00:44:22,313 --> 00:44:23,646
<i>♪ In the endless sky, ♪</i>

998
00:44:24,646 --> 00:44:26,645
<i>♪ Two clouds reunite ♪</i>

999
00:44:26,646 --> 00:44:28,146
<i>♪ Across every distance ♪</i>

1000
00:44:29,146 --> 00:44:31,271
<i>♪ My loneliness travels to find its end ♪</i>

1001
00:44:31,396 --> 00:44:32,896
<i>♪ Like a dream ♪</i>

1002
00:44:33,771 --> 00:44:35,771
<i>♪ We weave stories
Until they blossom into love ♪</i>

1003
00:44:35,896 --> 00:44:37,396
<i>♪ Deep within my soul ♪</i>

1004
00:44:38,313 --> 00:44:40,396
<i>♪ Desire quietly overflows. ♪</i>

1005
00:44:40,646 --> 00:44:43,521
<i>♪ A single enduring glance
From you is enough ♪</i>

1006
00:44:43,813 --> 00:44:44,896
<i>♪ Glancing ♪</i>

1007
00:44:45,188 --> 00:44:47,813
<i>♪ All I seek is
A few more moments with you ♪</i>

1008
00:44:48,271 --> 00:44:49,438
<i>♪ Longing... ♪</i>

1009
00:44:58,896 --> 00:45:00,271
<i>♪ In the endless sky ♪</i>

1010
