<i>♪ Glancing ♪</i>

1019
00:45:21,771 --> 00:45:24,313
<i>♪ All I seek is
A few more moments with you ♪</i>

1020
00:45:24,771 --> 00:45:26,021
<i>♪ Longing ♪</i>

1021
00:45:35,688 --> 00:45:37,688
Sathya, What's taking so long?

1022
00:45:37,813 --> 00:45:39,063
- Almost done.
- Hurry up!

1023
00:45:39,521 --> 00:45:41,395
All of you take a bath.

1024
00:45:41,396 --> 00:45:42,020
Will do!

1025
00:45:42,021 --> 00:45:43,770
Oh no, rice!

1026
00:45:43,771 --> 00:45:45,645
I don't want to eat rice.

1027
00:45:45,646 --> 00:45:47,396
Mom, I want some bread omelet.

1028
00:45:47,521 --> 00:45:48,438
You're going to get smacked.

1029
00:45:48,646 --> 00:45:51,396
For one more month,
no egg or non-veg.

1030
00:45:51,521 --> 00:45:52,146
What?!

1031
00:45:52,438 --> 00:45:53,896
Until the Purattasi month is over.

1032
00:45:54,021 --> 00:45:54,813
What's all this?

1033
00:45:54,938 --> 00:45:56,813
- Go over to your Uncle.
- Come to me.

1034
00:45:57,313 --> 00:45:57,938
Sit.

1035
00:45:58,521 --> 00:46:00,646
I'll take you outside
and buy whatever you want to eat.

1036
00:46:01,146 --> 00:46:01,896
Hey!

1037
00:46:02,313 --> 00:46:05,146
If I find out
that you had meat outside.

1038
00:46:05,313 --> 00:46:06,938
I won't let you back in the house.

1039
00:46:07,688 --> 00:46:08,646
Especially, you!

1040
00:46:08,771 --> 00:46:10,396
I wouldn’t dream of it.

1041
00:46:11,021 --> 00:46:13,771
Dad! What’s happening?

1042
00:46:14,771 --> 00:46:16,521
Never mind her.

1043
00:46:16,813 --> 00:46:18,270
We are heading to Shalimar right after.

1044
00:46:18,271 --> 00:46:20,188
And feast on four appams and paya.

1045
00:46:20,396 --> 00:46:21,021
Paya?

1046
00:46:21,563 --> 00:46:23,313
Pepper Paya!

1047
00:46:24,396 --> 00:46:25,687
- My little brother.
- What?

1048
00:46:25,688 --> 00:46:27,062
Do you know why Mom's fasting?

1049
00:46:27,063 --> 00:46:27,813
Why's that?

1050
00:46:28,146 --> 00:46:30,938
For you and Chiranjeevi to marry the girl
you've always dreamed of.

1051
00:46:31,396 --> 00:46:32,438
Girl of your dreams.

1052
00:46:32,771 --> 00:46:33,771
Magic. Magic.

1053
00:46:34,521 --> 00:46:36,770
Dad, I am going to be fasting.

1054
00:46:36,771 --> 00:46:37,563
Don't spoil me!

1055
00:46:39,646 --> 00:46:41,146
- Bloody, old man.
- What's with him?

1056
00:46:41,521 --> 00:46:43,771
He might be more shameless than I am.

1057
00:46:54,521 --> 00:46:55,563
Dude?

1058
00:46:56,021 --> 00:46:59,896
Whenever your girl asks to come home,
would you take me along?

1059
00:47:00,396 --> 00:47:02,646
What nonsense are you talking about?

1060
00:47:02,771 --> 00:47:05,145
You see, your girl called you over...

1061
00:47:05,146 --> 00:47:06,271
It might lead to something steamy.

1062
00:47:06,646 --> 00:47:09,021
So, I feel I might get in the way.

1063
00:47:10,021 --> 00:47:11,188
Dude, am I right?

1064
00:47:11,813 --> 00:47:13,771
It's the first time she's invited me over.

1065
00:47:13,896 --> 00:47:16,396
I thought it'd feel less awkward
with you there.

1066
00:47:16,813 --> 00:47:18,521
But you're talking nonsense.

1067
00:47:19,771 --> 00:47:22,896
If a girl calls someone over,
it doesn't mean she's calling for that.

1068
00:47:23,771 --> 00:47:28,271
Lust may be part of a man's life,
but it cannot define it.

1069
00:47:28,521 --> 00:47:29,771
You don't have to tag along.
Get off the bike.

1070
00:47:29,896 --> 00:47:31,771
- Get off!
- Sorry, dude!

1071
00:47:31,896 --> 00:47:32,896
I was out of line.
Please go!

1072
00:47:33,021 --> 00:47:34,521
If you say anything else,
I'll kill you.

1073
00:47:38,646 --> 00:47:39,271
Magic?

1074
00:47:46,521 --> 00:47:47,396
Woah!

1075
00:47:47,521 --> 00:47:48,771
What a beauty?

1076
00:47:48,896 --> 00:47:51,187
- Hey!
- I meant the house, Dude.

1077
00:47:51,188 --> 00:47:52,895
- Hi, Krishna. Hi!
- Hi.

1078
00:47:52,896 --> 00:47:54,188
- Please come in.
- Coming! Coming!

1079
00:47:56,646 --> 00:47:59,188
All these plants inside the house
remind me of Bangalore.

1080
00:47:59,521 --> 00:48:00,146
Hey, Dad!

1081
00:48:00,521 --> 00:48:01,146
They're here!

1082
00:48:01,271 --> 00:48:02,187
Hey, Krishna!

1083
00:48:02,188 --> 00:48:04,145
Hi! Hi! Welcome home!

1084
00:48:04,146 --> 00:48:04,771
Come! Come!

1085
00:48:05,021 --> 00:48:05,937
- Who’s this?
- Greetings, Uncle.

1086
00:48:05,938 --> 00:48:06,895
He's my friend, Uncle.

1087
00:48:06,896 --> 00:48:08,271
Baba! Bangalore Baba!

1088
00:48:08,396 --> 00:48:09,812
Hey, Bangalore!

1089
00:48:09,813 --> 00:48:10,938
Nice, Man!

1090
00:48:11,063 --> 00:48:12,770
Welcome, have a seat.

1091
00:48:12,771 --> 00:48:13,896
Have a seat. Sit down.

1092
00:48:15,146 --> 00:48:17,395
Sir, I know all about Anglo-Indians.

1093
00:48:17,396 --> 00:48:19,312
All friends in my area know me.

1094
00:48:19,313 --> 00:48:22,895
Hey, Baba, I'm part white,
yet I speak good Tamil.

1095
00:48:22,896 --> 00:48:24,063
Why are you struggling to speak English?

1096
00:48:25,396 --> 00:48:26,687
You deserved that.

1097
00:48:26,688 --> 00:48:27,687
- Dad.
- Yeah, Baby girl.

1098
00:48:27,688 --> 00:48:28,521
Fix them a drink.

1099
00:48:28,771 --> 00:48:30,063
Yeah, done, sure.

1100
00:48:30,271 --> 00:48:32,521
So, boys,
what would you like to have?

1101
00:48:32,646 --> 00:48:34,646
- Tea, coffee--
- Whisky or Brandy?

1102
00:48:36,771 --> 00:48:38,688
Sir, is this for real?

1103
00:48:39,021 --> 00:48:41,021
Hey, this is our custom, man.

1104
00:48:41,188 --> 00:48:42,270
Fine, what do you like to drink?

1105
00:48:42,271 --> 00:48:44,270
Then I’ll have a whisky on the rocks.

1106
00:48:44,271 --> 00:48:45,271
Not bad, man!

1107
00:48:45,646 --> 00:48:46,895
Krishna, what are you having?

1108
00:48:46,896 --> 00:48:47,520
- I'll--
- Sir!

1109
00:48:47,521 --> 00:48:49,270
He doesn't drink any liquor.

1110
00:48:49,271 --> 00:48:50,146
He's a good boy!

1111
00:48:50,271 --> 00:48:52,813
Does that make us bad people!

1112
00:48:53,021 --> 00:48:54,438
That's some backwards logic.

1113
00:48:54,646 --> 00:48:56,938
No, sir.
I only said what people usually say.

1114
00:48:57,271 --> 00:48:58,688
Drinking is a personal choice, Baba!

1115
00:48:59,021 --> 00:49:01,396
No one has the right to judge them.

1116
00:49:01,521 --> 00:49:02,563
Moderation is the key.

1117
00:49:02,688 --> 00:49:03,646
Correct, sir!

1118
00:49:03,938 --> 00:49:06,771
Drinking at home should be normalized.

1119
00:49:06,896 --> 00:49:08,395
You're rocking, Sir.

1120
00:49:08,396 --> 00:49:09,770
Now you're catching up.

1121
00:49:09,771 --> 00:49:11,313
Alright.
One whiskey on the rocks!

1122
00:49:11,521 --> 00:49:14,021
Dude, he wasn't kidding around.

1123
00:49:14,396 --> 00:49:16,645
What's with them?
They have drinks at home.

1124
00:49:16,646 --> 00:49:17,771
Have fun, Dude!

1125
00:49:19,396 --> 00:49:21,438
Baba, I’ve poured you one small.

1126
00:49:21,688 --> 00:49:22,937
Finish this and I’ll refill it.

1127
00:49:22,938 --> 00:49:24,396
Krishna, I’ll keep this here.

1128
00:49:24,688 --> 00:49:27,396
- Drink whenever you feel like it.
- Uncle, I don't want it.

1129
00:49:27,521 --> 00:49:29,021
Hey, it's just wine, Krishna.

1130
00:49:29,563 --> 00:49:30,771
It doesn't matter. I don't want it.

1131
00:49:30,938 --> 00:49:31,813
Krishna!

1132
00:49:33,771 --> 00:49:34,813
You’re insulting us.

1133
00:49:35,396 --> 00:49:37,146
Dad, leave him be.

1134
00:49:37,396 --> 00:49:39,313
No, no.
I'll drink it for Uncle.

1135
00:49:39,896 --> 00:49:40,896
Yeah!

1136
00:49:42,938 --> 00:49:43,938
That’s my boy

1137
00:49:44,146 --> 00:49:46,521
Alright!
I, too, shall fix a drink for myself.

1138
00:49:53,021 --> 00:49:55,563
Wine is straight fire, Sir.

1139
00:49:55,938 --> 00:49:56,896
Was it homemade?

1140
00:49:57,021 --> 00:49:58,271
Yes, homemade.

1141
00:49:58,396 --> 00:50:00,896
I even sell it if you want to buy.

1142
00:50:02,271 --> 00:50:04,146
- So it was a sample.
- You said it best.

1143
00:50:04,396 --> 00:50:07,021
Hey, bugger.
Dad always jokes around.

1144
00:50:07,146 --> 00:50:08,021
Don't mind, okay.

1145
00:50:08,188 --> 00:50:09,270
Come, let's eat.

1146
00:50:09,271 --> 00:50:11,521
Come on!
Make yourselves comfortable.

1147
00:50:13,021 --> 00:50:15,020
There were so many surprises
with the drinks.

1148
00:50:15,021 --> 00:50:17,020
I don't even know what to expect in food.

1149
00:50:17,021 --> 00:50:17,938
Nothing special.

1150
00:50:18,146 --> 00:50:20,521
Beef fry, beef biryani, chilly beef.

1151
00:50:20,646 --> 00:50:22,146
Pork fry, and meat.

1152
00:50:22,271 --> 00:50:23,188
That's all!

1153
00:50:23,771 --> 00:50:25,521
Pass me the pork.
I'll serve Krishna.

1154
00:50:30,771 --> 00:50:31,771
<i>You're going to get smacked!</i>

1155
00:50:31,896 --> 00:50:34,770
<i>For one more month,
no egg or non-veg.</i>

1156
00:50:34,771 --> 00:50:36,020
<i>Until the Purattasi month is over.</i>

1157
00:50:36,021 --> 00:50:37,562
Try Aunty’s Pork.

1158
00:50:37,563 --> 00:50:39,146
Her cooking is special.

1159
00:50:40,021 --> 00:50:41,521
- Just try.
- Do you want some beef?

1160
00:50:41,646 --> 00:50:42,646
That's enough for me.

1161
00:50:46,271 --> 00:50:50,146
[offering prayers]

1162
00:50:52,688 --> 00:50:54,770
Eat your fill. Don't feel shy.

1163
00:50:54,771 --> 00:50:55,771
That's enough.

1164
00:51:00,563 --> 00:51:01,563
Dude, stop!

1165
00:51:02,438 --> 00:51:04,521
Just hold on a second, Dude.

1166
00:51:05,146 --> 00:51:06,688
Beef looked fire!

1167
00:51:07,188 --> 00:51:08,771
You ruined my chances of a good feast.

1168
00:51:09,063 --> 00:51:10,271
What the hell is your problem?

1169
00:51:11,021 --> 00:51:11,646
Dude...

1170
00:51:12,563 --> 00:51:14,271
If Magic and I got together

1171
00:51:14,896 --> 00:51:18,521
How will I tell my mother
that they cook beef and pork?

1172
00:51:20,771 --> 00:51:22,146
That too, during Puratasi month.

1173
00:51:23,896 --> 00:51:27,646
Dude, you mustn't be thinking
from this angle.

1174
00:51:28,021 --> 00:51:31,396
You have to convince Magic
to adjust to your family's liking.

1175
00:51:32,438 --> 00:51:35,271
Because you’re going to live
with your parents.

1176
00:51:36,021 --> 00:51:38,688
First, ask her what Puratasi even means.

1177
00:51:40,146 --> 00:51:43,021
You keep thinking like your Mom.

1178
00:51:46,021 --> 00:51:48,062
Magic, I'm sorry.

1179
00:51:48,063 --> 00:51:51,271
On that day, my mother warned me strictly
not to eat non-veg because it's Puratasi.

1180
00:51:51,438 --> 00:51:54,145
So I was afraid
that I might end up eating.

1181
00:51:54,146 --> 00:51:54,896
Hey, bugger!

1182
00:51:55,188 --> 00:51:56,187
I understand!

1183
00:51:56,188 --> 00:51:58,771
But it was no way to behave
in front of my parents.

1184
00:51:59,021 --> 00:52:02,437
- It was humiliating!
- Oh, no, I'm sorry, Magic.

1185
00:52:02,438 --> 00:52:04,021
I'm really sorry, Magic.

1186
00:52:04,271 --> 00:52:05,021
Okay, forget it.

1187
00:52:05,646 --> 00:52:08,063
Do you know what Puratasi is?

1188
00:52:08,521 --> 00:52:10,063
And why don't we eat meat?

1189
00:52:10,188 --> 00:52:13,271
Yes, I know all about Puratasi.

1190
00:52:13,563 --> 00:52:15,896
- Is it?
- The most peaceful time for our people.

1191
00:52:16,771 --> 00:52:18,271
Peaceful? How's that?

1192
00:52:18,521 --> 00:52:21,021
Yes, most of you avoid eating non-veg.

1193
00:52:21,188 --> 00:52:23,396
So we can get chicken and fish cheaply.

1194
00:52:23,563 --> 00:52:25,938
Apart from that,
why would I care about Puratasi?

1195
00:52:26,063 --> 00:52:26,813
What?

1196
00:52:29,896 --> 00:52:30,520
What?

1197
00:52:30,521 --> 00:52:31,146
Come along!

1198
00:52:38,646 --> 00:52:39,313
Hello.

1199
00:52:39,938 --> 00:52:40,646
Yes, sir.

1200
00:52:41,021 --> 00:52:41,938
Are you at our camp?

1201
00:52:42,313 --> 00:52:44,646
- I'll be there in 10 minutes.
- Hey, there!

1202
00:52:44,771 --> 00:52:46,020
Hey, what are you doing here?

1203
00:52:46,021 --> 00:52:47,437
I told you about the check-up.

1204
00:52:47,438 --> 00:52:48,271
Oh, right!

1205
00:52:48,521 --> 00:52:49,938
Listen, she's my niece.

1206
00:52:50,688 --> 00:52:51,937
I brought her to the hospital.

1207
00:52:51,938 --> 00:52:54,396
Suddenly, a parent has arrived
at the camp to pay the fee.

1208
00:52:54,521 --> 00:52:57,146
- Can you babysit her for 10 Minutes?
- Yeah, sure!

1209
00:52:59,271 --> 00:53:01,313
- What's your name?
- Bommi!

1210
00:53:01,438 --> 00:53:03,396
That’s a cool name!

1211
00:53:03,563 --> 00:53:04,521
Who named you?

1212
00:53:04,896 --> 00:53:06,313
My dad, who else.

1213
00:53:06,521 --> 00:53:08,770
Okay, what's your name?

1214
00:53:08,771 --> 00:53:09,938
My name is...

1215
00:53:10,521 --> 00:53:11,271
Magic!

1216
00:53:11,813 --> 00:53:15,020
Oh! You're that Magic?

1217
00:53:15,021 --> 00:53:16,270
Do you know me?

1218
00:53:16,271 --> 00:53:18,438
Yes, I know you very well.

1219
00:53:18,646 --> 00:53:21,270
I've heard about you often.

1220
00:53:21,271 --> 00:53:23,396
About me? From whom?

1221
00:53:23,521 --> 00:53:25,521
Who else? My Uncle.

1222
00:53:25,646 --> 00:53:28,270
Magic is like this and that...

1223
00:53:28,271 --> 00:53:30,312
I like her this much.

1224
00:53:30,313 --> 00:53:32,646
He's been saying it for a long time.

1225
00:53:33,271 --> 00:53:36,771
Don't you like my uncle?

1226
00:53:37,146 --> 00:53:37,771
Your Uncle--

1227
00:53:41,146 --> 00:53:41,771
Let's go.

1228
00:53:44,896 --> 00:53:46,521
I think I like someone

1229
00:53:46,896 --> 00:53:47,396
Who?

1230
00:53:48,271 --> 00:53:48,896
Clifton?

1231
00:53:52,688 --> 00:53:53,270
Then?

1232
00:53:53,271 --> 00:53:53,896
Krishna.

1233
00:53:55,063 --> 00:53:56,271
- Who?
- CSK.

1234
00:53:57,021 --> 00:53:57,896
CSK?!

1235
00:53:58,313 --> 00:53:59,771
What? Are you mad?

1236
00:54:00,021 --> 00:54:02,188
I told you not to fall
for these Tamil guys.

1237
00:54:02,396 --> 00:54:04,021
Did you learn nothing
from my experience?

1238
00:54:04,271 --> 00:54:05,813
Don’t stereotype, Barbara.

1239
00:54:06,313 --> 00:54:07,313
Just because your man did it

1240
00:54:07,646 --> 00:54:09,146
doesn't mean they're all the same.

1241
00:54:09,938 --> 00:54:13,021
Aren't many of our folks happy
marrying them?

1242
00:54:13,313 --> 00:54:14,270
No way, Dude.

1243
00:54:14,271 --> 00:54:15,771
We can't live happily.

1244
00:54:16,396 --> 00:54:17,896
It'll be very tough.

1245
00:54:18,521 --> 00:54:19,438
Why dude?

1246
00:54:20,896 --> 00:54:21,688
You want to know why?

1247
00:54:22,188 --> 00:54:24,270
Mom already made up her mind
about my cousin.

1248
00:54:24,271 --> 00:54:26,688
If I decided to marry Magic instead...

1249
00:54:27,271 --> 00:54:28,396
no one else in the family
can be happy.

1250
00:54:28,521 --> 00:54:30,813
What do I care if others are happy or not?

1251
00:54:31,063 --> 00:54:32,563
Isn't our happiness enough?

1252
00:54:33,896 --> 00:54:35,396
Love is all about the couple.

1253
00:54:35,563 --> 00:54:36,396
Not family.

1254
00:54:37,396 --> 00:54:38,563
The couple are the problem.

1255
00:54:39,271 --> 00:54:41,313
The problem in loving the boys here is...

1256
00:54:41,438 --> 00:54:42,896
the way they see us.

1257
00:54:43,813 --> 00:54:45,396
Anglo means easily approachable.

1258
00:54:45,563 --> 00:54:46,896
All they care about is sex.

1259
00:54:47,271 --> 00:54:49,062
Once the serious commitment comes up...

1260
00:54:49,063 --> 00:54:50,146
it runs into danger.

1261
00:54:50,521 --> 00:54:51,770
Dress appropriately.

1262
00:54:51,771 --> 00:54:52,895
Don't party too much.

1263
00:54:52,896 --> 00:54:55,521
They don't know our culture and torture us.

1264
00:54:57,521 --> 00:55:00,188
Look at Clifton following you
everywhere with his eyes.

1265
00:55:00,646 --> 00:55:02,771
Ask him out.
You'll live a good life.

1266
00:55:03,063 --> 00:55:04,521
What do you want me to do?

1267
00:55:05,063 --> 00:55:06,521
Do I really have to choose between them?

1268
00:55:06,646 --> 00:55:08,646
Choosing is your only way out, Dude!

1269
00:55:08,813 --> 00:55:10,520
That too, within a month.

1270
00:55:10,521 --> 00:55:13,771
You have to convince
both Magic and your mother.

1271
00:55:13,896 --> 00:55:15,521
Within 30 days.

1272
00:55:15,646 --> 00:55:17,438
30 Days is too much.

1273
00:55:17,813 --> 00:55:19,146
15 days at most.

1274
00:55:19,438 --> 00:55:21,021
It's all up to Magic.

1275
00:55:21,896 --> 00:55:23,520
It’s quite a conundrum.

1276
00:55:23,521 --> 00:55:25,396
What do I do now?

1277
00:55:25,521 --> 00:55:27,521
Let me tell you what to do.

1278
00:55:29,021 --> 00:55:29,813
Test him.

1279
00:55:30,396 --> 00:55:30,938
What?

1280
00:55:31,521 --> 00:55:32,396
Give him a test.

1281
00:55:32,896 --> 00:55:35,771
Test the waters
to see if it works out.

1282
00:55:36,771 --> 00:55:38,646
What if it doesn’t work out?

1283
00:55:39,396 --> 00:55:40,396
If he doesn't fit in?

1284
00:55:40,521 --> 00:55:43,646
If he doesn’t work out,
don’t even bring it up at home.

1285
00:55:43,771 --> 00:55:45,146
Keep it quiet!

1286
00:55:45,521 --> 00:55:47,938
If it works out, then take the risk.

1287
00:55:48,563 --> 00:55:51,063
Alright, let me give it a shot.

1288
00:55:51,271 --> 00:55:53,146
Okay. I'll give it a shot.

1289
00:56:07,938 --> 00:56:09,146
<i>Hey, Dude, move it!</i>

1290
00:56:13,646 --> 00:56:14,813
<i>Up your game, Dude.</i>

1291
00:56:16,146 --> 00:56:16,771
<i>Oh, no!</i>

1292
00:56:26,146 --> 00:56:27,521
<i>There it goes!</i>

1293
00:56:28,271 --> 00:56:30,896
<i>♪ I'm trapped beyond escape ♪</i>

1294
00:56:31,063 --> 00:56:33,521
<i>♪ Everything keeps piling up ♪</i>

1295
00:56:34,021 --> 00:56:36,396
<i>♪ Every nerve tingles ♪</i>

1296
00:56:36,771 --> 00:56:39,396
<i>♪ I've been hit hard by love ♪</i>

1297
00:56:40,146 --> 00:56:40,938
<i>♪ Hey, idiot! ♪</i>

1298
00:56:42,771 --> 00:56:43,771
<i>♪ Damn, you fool ♪</i>

1299
00:56:45,771 --> 00:56:46,646
<i>♪ Hey, idiot! ♪</i>

1300
00:56:46,771 --> 00:56:49,396
<i>♪ You're trapped Damn, you fool ♪</i>

1301
00:56:50,563 --> 00:56:53,396
<i>♪ I'm trapped beyond escape ♪</i>

1302
00:56:54,313 --> 00:56:56,313
I saw her in a party dress
for the first time.

1303
00:56:56,521 --> 00:56:57,813
What kind of clothing is that?

1304
00:56:58,063 --> 00:56:59,146
Hey, Dude!

1305
00:56:59,396 --> 00:57:01,437
Anglos' always dress to kill.

1306
00:57:01,438 --> 00:57:02,271
I knew that already.

1307
00:57:02,521 --> 00:57:05,396
All this time, it felt like
only I was checking her out.

1308
00:57:05,521 --> 00:57:07,896
But now when I think about
marrying her...

1309
00:57:10,188 --> 00:57:12,896
I feel everyone around is checking her out.

1310
00:57:34,313 --> 00:57:35,813
<i>♪ She's got me chasing after her ♪</i>

1311
00:57:40,396 --> 00:57:41,146
Like that!

1312
00:57:41,396 --> 00:57:42,938
She hugs everyone head-on.

1313
00:57:43,188 --> 00:57:44,895
- Why can't she hug them sideways?
- Dude!

1314
00:57:44,896 --> 00:57:46,562
It’s infuriating to watch these things.

1315
00:57:46,563 --> 00:57:47,895
It’s very wrong, Bro.

1316
00:57:47,896 --> 00:57:48,646
Hey, Bugger!

1317
00:57:49,063 --> 00:57:51,313
How about we try a different approach?

1318
00:57:52,646 --> 00:57:53,521
Meaning?

1319
00:57:56,188 --> 00:57:57,563
Like a situationship.

1320
00:57:58,271 --> 00:57:59,146
Or a fling.

1321
00:58:00,146 --> 00:58:01,021
Living together.

1322
00:58:01,271 --> 00:58:02,396
Something like that.

1323
00:58:03,646 --> 00:58:05,145
Situationship just means...

1324
00:58:05,146 --> 00:58:08,812
instead of marriage
and all other commitments,

1325
00:58:08,813 --> 00:58:10,520
just staying together
for emotional needs.

1326
00:58:10,521 --> 00:58:12,271
While having a little fun on the side.

1327
00:58:12,396 --> 00:58:13,313
Dude!

1328
00:58:13,438 --> 00:58:15,645
That sounds like a good option.
Agree to it.

1329
00:58:15,646 --> 00:58:17,646
Stop irritating me.
Shut up, damn it.

1330
00:58:20,438 --> 00:58:22,646
- Run! Run!
- You're overthinking it.

1331
00:58:22,813 --> 00:58:23,896
What about the fling?

1332
00:58:24,021 --> 00:58:25,396
It's just about having fun.

1333
00:58:26,646 --> 00:58:29,020
I already knew
what living together meant.

1334
00:58:29,021 --> 00:58:30,187
The rest are all new to me.

1335
00:58:30,188 --> 00:58:32,521
She might be breadcrumbing you.

1336
00:58:32,813 --> 00:58:33,687
Meaning...

1337
00:58:33,688 --> 00:58:37,437
They won’t seriously commit
but keep you on the hook.

1338
00:58:37,438 --> 00:58:40,188
I swear, that’s exactly it.
Give me your hand.

1339
00:58:40,396 --> 00:58:41,271
Thank you!

1340
00:58:41,521 --> 00:58:43,646
- She’s doing something wrong.
- Score a run.

1341
00:58:43,938 --> 00:58:45,188
Don't miss it, Dude.

1342
00:58:47,396 --> 00:58:48,396
That was an easy ball.

1343
00:58:48,521 --> 00:58:50,313
- Buffalo!
- Look at him play.

1344
00:58:51,146 --> 00:58:52,188
Hey, Magic is calling him.

1345
00:58:53,896 --> 00:58:54,521
Tell me.

1346
00:58:55,063 --> 00:58:56,063
Where are you, Krish?

1347
00:58:56,438 --> 00:58:57,396
Did you call me Krish?

1348
00:58:57,563 --> 00:58:58,771
That's new.

1349
00:58:59,021 --> 00:59:00,146
I’m here with friends.

1350
00:59:00,521 --> 00:59:01,521
Why don't you come over to my house?

1351
00:59:01,896 --> 00:59:03,021
We have the house to ourselves.

1352
00:59:03,563 --> 00:59:05,938
- Go! Go right now!
- Go over there!

1353
00:59:07,521 --> 00:59:09,646
Have the house to ourselves?

1354
00:59:10,313 --> 00:59:11,646
Yeah, are you coming?

1355
00:59:11,771 --> 00:59:13,146
No... No, Magic.

1356
00:59:13,646 --> 00:59:14,646
I'm busy with important work.

1357
00:59:15,063 --> 00:59:16,895
I'm stuck with something important.

1358
00:59:16,896 --> 00:59:18,563
<i>- Hello? Hello?</i>
- Bye, bye, bye, bye.

1359
00:59:19,146 --> 00:59:19,896
You're hopeless!

1360
00:59:20,938 --> 00:59:22,896
She's definitely not marriage material.

1361
00:59:24,188 --> 00:59:24,896
Damn!

1362
00:59:25,396 --> 00:59:26,313
What happened?

1363
00:59:27,063 --> 00:59:28,813
- Passed!
- Hey!

1364
00:59:31,271 --> 00:59:37,021
I don't have a single point
to defend her before Mom.

1365
00:59:37,146 --> 00:59:39,313
Oh, no! Are you serious?

1366
00:59:40,146 --> 00:59:42,271
Looks like fate has chosen
Uncle's daughter for me.

1367
00:59:45,396 --> 00:59:47,813
The daughter, I'm fine with.

1368
00:59:47,938 --> 00:59:50,271
But the giggling Uncle is the problem.

1369
00:59:50,396 --> 00:59:53,021
Hey, bike taxi, stop.
We've reached home.

1370
00:59:53,396 --> 00:59:56,188
- Oh, it's you.
- Get down!

1371
00:59:56,521 --> 00:59:58,520
Look, it's embarrassing
he's wearing shoes on his neck.

1372
00:59:58,521 --> 01:00:00,521
Like you're royalty or something.

1373
01:00:00,896 --> 01:00:02,188
- Get lost!
- Dad!

1374
01:00:02,563 --> 01:00:04,771
Are you nuts?
Why are you lashing out at him?

1375
01:00:04,896 --> 01:00:06,188
You want to know why?

1376
01:00:06,688 --> 01:00:09,270
He got drunk and picked a fight
at the Shalimar entrance.

1377
01:00:09,271 --> 01:00:10,688
All my coworkers were there.

1378
01:00:10,896 --> 01:00:12,146
Do you know how embarrassed I felt?

1379
01:00:12,521 --> 01:00:14,021
I'm a state government employee.

1380
01:00:14,146 --> 01:00:16,437
- There he goes again.
- Dear lord in heaven!

1381
01:00:16,438 --> 01:00:16,938
What?

1382
01:00:17,146 --> 01:00:20,063
Even a state’s CM
wouldn't repeat this phrase so often.

1383
01:00:20,271 --> 01:00:21,021
Go away!

1384
01:00:21,396 --> 01:00:22,645
Dad, I'm running out of patience.

1385
01:00:22,646 --> 01:00:23,896
- Don't test me.
- Shut up!

1386
01:00:24,021 --> 01:00:27,563
What do you always call him?

1387
01:00:28,646 --> 01:00:29,812
I got it!

1388
01:00:29,813 --> 01:00:31,396
What's that? What?

1389
01:00:32,438 --> 01:00:33,646
Boomer!

1390
01:00:34,188 --> 01:00:35,396
You're a Boomer!

1391
01:00:35,563 --> 01:00:36,938
- Get lost for real!
- Dad!

1392
01:00:37,438 --> 01:00:38,521
What are you doing?

1393
01:00:38,813 --> 01:00:40,521
- Get it together, Dad.
- Why would you push him?

1394
01:00:40,771 --> 01:00:41,896
You're unnecessarily causing a problem.

1395
01:00:42,063 --> 01:00:43,021
I'll kill you!

1396
01:00:44,396 --> 01:00:45,396
Lovely shot!

1397
01:00:45,646 --> 01:00:46,521
4 runs!

1398
01:00:48,813 --> 01:00:49,771
What are you doing?

1399
01:00:50,521 --> 01:00:51,771
How dare you raise your hand on him?

1400
01:00:52,521 --> 01:00:53,646
I will kill you myself!

1401
01:00:54,188 --> 01:00:56,396
- Mom, it was him...
- I know everything. Get inside.

1402
01:00:57,396 --> 01:00:58,021
Go!

1403
01:01:06,271 --> 01:01:07,021
Honey...

1404
01:01:15,271 --> 01:01:16,146
Come inside.

1405
01:01:40,771 --> 01:01:41,396
Dad!

1406
01:01:41,771 --> 01:01:44,187
It's been a long time
since love has bloomed between us.

1407
01:01:44,188 --> 01:01:44,895
Let me have it.

1408
01:01:44,896 --> 01:01:46,771
I have something important to ask you.

1409
01:01:46,896 --> 01:01:48,438
- I want to love, damn it!
- Come on!

1410
01:01:50,646 --> 01:01:52,021
Tell me. What is it?

1411
01:01:53,521 --> 01:01:56,896
It's something important.
Are you sober enough?

1412
01:01:57,021 --> 01:02:01,146
I'm the most sober when I'm drunk.

1413
01:02:01,688 --> 01:02:02,521
However...

1414
01:02:02,896 --> 01:02:05,021
you can’t expect me to recall
our conversation in the morning.

1415
01:02:05,271 --> 01:02:07,146
I would have already forgotten by then.

1416
01:02:07,396 --> 01:02:08,146
Whatever!

1417
01:02:09,771 --> 01:02:11,396
Let's say I'm in love.

1418
01:02:11,521 --> 01:02:12,271
Really?

1419
01:02:13,063 --> 01:02:14,271
My son!

1420
01:02:14,396 --> 01:02:16,521
Not actually, though.

1421
01:02:16,646 --> 01:02:18,688
But if I did...

1422
01:02:18,896 --> 01:02:20,688
What kind of girl should I fall for?

1423
01:02:21,021 --> 01:02:23,563
Your family can’t find
a single fault in her.

1424
01:02:24,396 --> 01:02:28,646
Yes! Perfect! Super!
Should be their only responses.

1425
01:02:29,521 --> 01:02:31,063
Don’t end up like your old man.

1426
01:02:32,021 --> 01:02:34,021
Fell in love with a different caste girl

1427
01:02:34,396 --> 01:02:36,771
and still live to regret it
by drowning in alcohol.

1428
01:02:37,813 --> 01:02:40,396
Instead of being in a loveless marriage...

1429
01:02:40,771 --> 01:02:42,937
Why not fight for what you love?

1430
01:02:42,938 --> 01:02:46,021
Then she should have been brave
like my Sarala.

1431
01:02:46,646 --> 01:02:49,771
Did you see
how she defended me back there?

1432
01:02:51,146 --> 01:02:52,521
But my Ex-lover!

1433
01:02:53,271 --> 01:02:58,271
While I was getting beaten up
by her Dad and mine.

1434
01:02:58,521 --> 01:03:00,521
All she did was watch.

1435
01:03:00,646 --> 01:03:01,562
Hey, Mental!

1436
01:03:01,563 --> 01:03:03,395
Then why get drunk every day,
sulking over her?

1437
01:03:03,396 --> 01:03:04,021
Hey!

1438
01:03:05,271 --> 01:03:06,396
That's what love is.

1439
01:03:07,063 --> 01:03:08,313
You won’t get it.

1440
01:03:08,771 --> 01:03:10,396
Just don't fall in love, though.

1441
01:03:10,771 --> 01:03:13,271
Your mom would never approve.

1442
01:03:13,646 --> 01:03:14,938
Not in a million years.

1443
01:03:16,688 --> 01:03:19,646
But the way she called me <i>honey</i>, though.

1444
01:03:21,313 --> 01:03:23,520
Your wedding is next month...

1445
01:03:23,521 --> 01:03:25,813
It’s too late to talk about love,
you moron!

1446
01:03:29,813 --> 01:03:33,021
You may be onto something, Dad.

1447
01:03:33,313 --> 01:03:35,313
Love isn't in the cards for me.

1448
01:03:42,521 --> 01:03:43,563
Wonderland?

1449
01:03:45,938 --> 01:03:48,563
I can’t handle the suspense.

1450
01:03:52,271 --> 01:03:53,021
She’s here!

1451
01:03:53,271 --> 01:03:54,646
- Hi!
- Hi!

1452
01:03:56,396 --> 01:03:58,188
Why are we suddenly meeting here?

1453
01:03:58,938 --> 01:04:00,896
Like you said during college days...

1454
01:04:01,146 --> 01:04:04,021
all important news
must be shared here in Wonderland.

1455
01:04:04,813 --> 01:04:06,688
Important news?

1456
01:04:06,813 --> 01:04:08,146
Yes, it's a matter of love.

1457
01:04:08,271 --> 01:04:09,146
Love matter?

1458
01:04:09,396 --> 01:04:10,146
Yeah, man!

1459
01:04:10,896 --> 01:04:13,146
There's an Anglo guy
who lives on my street.

1460
01:04:13,896 --> 01:04:15,646
He always checks me out.

1461
01:04:15,771 --> 01:04:17,313
On the street and at the church.

1462
01:04:17,646 --> 01:04:18,896
You probably know him.

1463
01:04:19,188 --> 01:04:19,813
Clifton?

1464
01:04:20,396 --> 01:04:23,271
Clifton?
I have seen him during cricket practice.

1465
01:04:23,521 --> 01:04:24,645
He proposed to me.

1466
01:04:24,646 --> 01:04:25,271
What?!

1467
01:04:25,563 --> 01:04:26,146
Huh?

1468
01:04:28,396 --> 01:04:29,438
He proposed to you?

1469
01:04:30,021 --> 01:04:31,021
Keep going.

1470
01:04:32,396 --> 01:04:32,938
Yeah!

1471
01:04:33,646 --> 01:04:37,521
He said that since we both
want to move to Australia.

1472
01:04:37,896 --> 01:04:40,938
It'll be perfect.
So, he asked me to marry him.

1473
01:04:48,021 --> 01:04:49,063
One minute, Magic.

1474
01:04:55,271 --> 01:04:56,063
Yes!

1475
01:04:56,646 --> 01:04:58,813
Jesus! You saved me!

1476
01:04:58,938 --> 01:05:01,313
Jesus! I can't express my happiness!

1477
01:05:01,813 --> 01:05:03,896
Poor thing. He got possessive.

1478
01:05:11,771 --> 01:05:12,313
Yes!

1479
01:05:21,813 --> 01:05:22,521
Hey, bugger!

1480
01:05:22,896 --> 01:05:24,563
Are you upset?

1481
01:05:25,188 --> 01:05:26,770
I've told you from the beginning.

1482
01:05:26,771 --> 01:05:28,021
We’re just friends.

1483
01:05:28,896 --> 01:05:31,021
I can't hold back my emotions, Magic.

1484
01:05:31,813 --> 01:05:33,521
You're doing what you think is right.

1485
01:05:33,688 --> 01:05:34,271
But...

1486
01:05:34,896 --> 01:05:36,563
Your happiness is all that matters to me.

1487
01:05:40,271 --> 01:05:42,938
Aww! You are so sweet!

1488
01:05:43,188 --> 01:05:44,271
Indeed, it's sweet.

1489
01:05:45,521 --> 01:05:48,145
Shall I tell you how he proposed?

1490
01:05:48,146 --> 01:05:49,313
No, Magic.

1491
01:05:49,646 --> 01:05:50,938
You need to listen.

1492
01:05:51,396 --> 01:05:52,896
He started with a poem.

1493
01:05:53,896 --> 01:05:54,521
Poem?

1494
01:05:54,646 --> 01:05:57,271
In Tamil, you call it, Kavithai.

1495
01:05:57,688 --> 01:05:58,813
It's pronounced "Po-em."

1496
01:05:59,271 --> 01:05:59,771
Poem!

1497
01:06:01,813 --> 01:06:02,896
Okay, tell me

1498
01:06:14,521 --> 01:06:15,188
My love.

1499
01:06:16,271 --> 01:06:17,688
In this fast-paced world...

1500
01:06:18,771 --> 01:06:21,646
the only face
that brings me peace is yours.

1501
01:06:22,896 --> 01:06:24,313
From the moment I saw you...

1502
01:06:24,563 --> 01:06:26,813
the directions of my heart
changed completely.

1503
01:06:28,646 --> 01:06:29,938
This is not just love.

1504
01:06:31,146 --> 01:06:32,313
This is a promise.

1505
01:06:33,646 --> 01:06:35,521
This is not just a moment's feeling.

1506
01:06:37,021 --> 01:06:38,521
This is a lifetime decision.

1507
01:06:41,896 --> 01:06:42,396
I--

1508
01:06:44,771 --> 01:06:45,646
That's what he told me.

1509
01:06:48,771 --> 01:06:50,771
Whether it’s Australia...

1510
01:06:51,563 --> 01:06:53,271
Or America

1511
01:06:54,396 --> 01:06:56,646
there’s someone waiting for me
all these years.

1512
01:06:57,188 --> 01:06:58,896
I told him
he’s the one I'm going to marry.

1513
01:07:01,646 --> 01:07:03,063
I want to marry you, Krishna.

1514
01:07:05,271 --> 01:07:06,021
I love you!

1515
01:07:16,521 --> 01:07:17,521
<i>♪ You're done, Buddy! ♪</i>

1516
01:07:18,146 --> 01:07:20,521
<i>♪ I'm trapped beyond escape ♪</i>

1517
01:07:20,771 --> 01:07:23,271
<i>♪ Everything keeps piling up ♪</i>

1518
01:07:23,563 --> 01:07:26,146
<i>♪ Every nerve tingles ♪</i>

1519
01:07:26,438 --> 01:07:29,063
<i>♪ I've been hit hard by love ♪</i>

1520
01:07:50,021 --> 01:07:51,646
<i>♪ She's got me chasing after her ♪</i>

1521
01:08:10,896 --> 01:08:12,646
Hey, stop that song!
It's pissing me off!

1522
01:08:12,771 --> 01:08:14,646
Did you really think
it would be that easy?

1523
01:08:14,896 --> 01:08:16,270
It'll happen
when you least expect it.

1524
01:08:16,271 --> 01:08:18,271
Life always throws you for a loop.

1525
01:08:18,646 --> 01:08:19,896
You asked for it, didn't you?

1526
01:08:20,271 --> 01:08:21,187
Now, pay the price!

1527
01:08:21,188 --> 01:08:22,313
- Get lost!
- Hit me!

1528
01:08:22,521 --> 01:08:23,438
Hit me all you want.

1529
01:08:23,688 --> 01:08:25,562
But you're going endure it, Bro!

1530
01:08:25,563 --> 01:08:27,437
I told you to get lost!

1531
01:08:27,438 --> 01:08:30,062
- He's irking me.
- Dude, let him go.

1532
01:08:30,063 --> 01:08:31,271
Think about your next move.

1533
01:08:31,521 --> 01:08:32,188
Like I'd know!

1534
01:08:33,271 --> 01:08:34,646
I have no clue!

1535
01:08:35,063 --> 01:08:36,396
Then do what I say.

1536
01:08:36,771 --> 01:08:42,146
Imagine if she moved into your home
after you married.

1537
01:08:42,396 --> 01:08:44,688
Think long and hard about it.

1538
01:08:53,396 --> 01:08:55,396
Hey! What kind of dress is this?

1539
01:08:55,646 --> 01:08:56,896
Modern dress, Mom.

1540
01:09:00,188 --> 01:09:01,063
What?

1541
01:09:04,521 --> 01:09:05,645
What meat are you cooking?

1542
01:09:05,646 --> 01:09:06,521
Beef, Auntie!

1543
01:09:06,688 --> 01:09:09,187
Your son got it from the meat market
early in the morning.

1544
01:09:09,188 --> 01:09:10,021
Beef!

1545
01:09:11,313 --> 01:09:12,146
What, Mummy?

1546
01:09:14,771 --> 01:09:16,146
It’s for a nuptial ritual, dear.

1547
01:09:16,271 --> 01:09:17,146
Show me your nuptial chain.

1548
01:09:19,771 --> 01:09:22,396
Krishna, I must have left it
in the hanger. Get it for me.

1549
01:09:23,938 --> 01:09:24,938
One minute, Auntie!

1550
01:09:25,521 --> 01:09:26,896
You just doomed my fate.

1551
01:09:31,021 --> 01:09:32,396
You can hang it back there.

1552
01:09:38,521 --> 01:09:39,271
Krishna!

1553
01:09:41,063 --> 01:09:41,771
What?

1554
01:09:41,938 --> 01:09:42,771
Sing!

1555
01:09:45,313 --> 01:09:46,438
Oh, no, no!

1556
01:09:50,813 --> 01:09:51,770
Praise the lord, my son.

1557
01:09:51,771 --> 01:09:52,688
Cheers!

1558
01:09:52,938 --> 01:09:54,896
- Cheers, Daughter-in-law.
- Cheers, Uncle.

1559
01:09:55,396 --> 01:09:56,146
Cheers!

1560
01:09:57,271 --> 01:09:59,563
Sarala, would you like some?
It's delicious!

1561
01:10:02,396 --> 01:10:03,271
Krishna!

1562
01:10:03,688 --> 01:10:06,438
I can't even imagine this happening.

1563
01:10:07,063 --> 01:10:09,062
What would happen
if I introduce her as my fiance?

1564
01:10:09,063 --> 01:10:10,146
What do you think?

1565
01:10:10,271 --> 01:10:12,062
Either you leave your home for her.

1566
01:10:12,063 --> 01:10:13,271
Which you probably won't do.

1567
01:10:13,396 --> 01:10:14,896
They might just kick you out of the house.

1568
01:10:15,021 --> 01:10:16,063
Which is more likely to happen.

1569
01:10:16,188 --> 01:10:17,146
You're not helping.

1570
01:10:17,646 --> 01:10:20,646
Dude, I'm repeating now.

1571
01:10:21,021 --> 01:10:23,521
You're worrying over nothing.

1572
01:10:23,688 --> 01:10:25,313
All she did was confess her love.

1573
01:10:25,813 --> 01:10:27,438
She's a modern girl.

1574
01:10:27,646 --> 01:10:29,270
Based on what you told us...

1575
01:10:29,271 --> 01:10:31,396
she's not the type
to get tied down by marriage.

1576
01:10:31,813 --> 01:10:34,895
She might date you for a few days
and then break up.

1577
01:10:34,896 --> 01:10:36,271
What makes you so sure?

1578
01:10:36,396 --> 01:10:39,020
Because I know everything
about Anglos--

1579
01:10:39,021 --> 01:10:40,146
Do you even have to ask?

1580
01:10:42,271 --> 01:10:45,312
Like you mentioned
if she's not the marrying type I'm happy.

1581
01:10:45,313 --> 01:10:46,896
My Uncle is already planning an engagement.

1582
01:10:48,771 --> 01:10:49,896
Hey, it's Magic.

1583
01:10:50,813 --> 01:10:51,646
Hello, Magic!

1584
01:10:51,813 --> 01:10:53,063
<i>Krish, Where are you?</i>

1585
01:10:53,438 --> 01:10:54,813
I'm at Baba's shop.

1586
01:10:55,438 --> 01:10:57,188
I told my Dad about our relationship.

1587
01:10:57,396 --> 01:10:59,271
He wants to see you immediately.

1588
01:10:59,396 --> 01:11:00,771
<i>Could you come over
to my house tomorrow?</i>

1589
01:11:02,938 --> 01:11:04,646
Dude, was I right?

1590
01:11:04,896 --> 01:11:06,812
Because I know everything
about Anglos--

1591
01:11:06,813 --> 01:11:08,438
Shut your trap!

1592
01:11:08,813 --> 01:11:11,271
If I hear you repeat that phrase,
I'll kill you.

1593
01:11:15,021 --> 01:11:15,938
Were they relatives?

1594
01:11:16,063 --> 01:11:17,646
They look really fair.

1595
01:11:20,021 --> 01:11:20,646
Magic.

1596
01:11:21,063 --> 01:11:23,438
Why did you act in haste
and tell your father?

1597
01:11:23,563 --> 01:11:25,020
I haven't told him yet.
But you have to.

1598
01:11:25,021 --> 01:11:26,187
Haven't you told him yet?

1599
01:11:26,188 --> 01:11:27,771
Then, why did you make me come over?

1600
01:11:28,146 --> 01:11:30,270
I lied so that you came.
Would you have come otherwise?

1601
01:11:30,271 --> 01:11:31,021
Go and tell him.

1602
01:11:31,313 --> 01:11:33,020
Magic, why are we rushing into this?

1603
01:11:33,021 --> 01:11:34,395
We still have a time left.

1604
01:11:34,396 --> 01:11:35,646
I already told you.

1605
01:11:35,938 --> 01:11:37,437
That Clifton proposed to me.

1606
01:11:37,438 --> 01:11:39,396
Yesterday, he also proposed to my father.

1607
01:11:39,521 --> 01:11:40,063
What?!

1608
01:11:40,313 --> 01:11:41,563
He proposed to your dad, too?

1609
01:11:41,688 --> 01:11:43,188
- Eww!
- Oh, God!

1610
01:11:43,396 --> 01:11:44,563
Marriage proposal!

1611
01:11:44,938 --> 01:11:47,771
If you keep avoiding my Dad
with these lame jokes...

1612
01:11:48,021 --> 01:11:49,937
he'll drag me to Australia as his wife.

1613
01:11:49,938 --> 01:11:51,438
Magic, please hear me out--

1614
01:11:51,813 --> 01:11:52,938
No more arguments!

1615
01:11:53,146 --> 01:11:54,771
Shut up and do as I say.
Come with me.

1616
01:11:55,313 --> 01:11:56,313
Follow me!

1617
01:11:56,771 --> 01:11:58,896
What's in a name?

1618
01:11:59,521 --> 01:12:03,813
That which we call a rose
by any other name.

1619
01:12:04,021 --> 01:12:08,396
Smells just as sweet...

1620
01:12:09,938 --> 01:12:11,021
What is he doing?

1621
01:12:11,146 --> 01:12:12,020
...as candy!

1622
01:12:12,021 --> 01:12:14,771
He's rehearsing for an English play.

1623
01:12:14,896 --> 01:12:18,021
- Dad?
- Yes, my dear!

1624
01:12:18,146 --> 01:12:19,396
Krishna wants to talk to you.

1625
01:12:19,688 --> 01:12:21,896
Yes, Krishna. Tell me.

1626
01:12:22,021 --> 01:12:24,271
I'm all ears!

1627
01:12:24,688 --> 01:12:26,063
I don't understand

1628
01:12:26,188 --> 01:12:29,520
I meant
I'm ready to hear you out.

1629
01:12:29,521 --> 01:12:31,146
Oh, ah, okay!

1630
01:12:32,021 --> 01:12:34,145
I don't know how to begin, Uncle...

1631
01:12:34,146 --> 01:12:34,646
You see...

1632
01:12:36,271 --> 01:12:36,771
The thing is...

1633
01:12:41,271 --> 01:12:42,521
I'm in love with your daughter, Uncle.

1634
01:12:48,896 --> 01:12:49,938
And you, Magic?

1635
01:12:50,688 --> 01:12:52,521
Yes, Dad. I love him too.

1636
01:12:52,646 --> 01:12:53,771
I like him so much.

1637
01:12:54,646 --> 01:12:55,896
Uncle...

1638
01:12:56,396 --> 01:13:00,062
I get it, Uncle.
No father would approve this--

1639
01:13:00,063 --> 01:13:00,896
I approve!

1640
01:13:02,146 --> 01:13:02,771
Uncle?

1641
01:13:05,396 --> 01:13:06,270
I don't understand.

1642
01:13:06,271 --> 01:13:08,896
I approve of your relationship.

1643
01:13:09,146 --> 01:13:10,438
If you two like each other.

1644
01:13:10,563 --> 01:13:12,646
Who am I to get in the way?

1645
01:13:13,646 --> 01:13:14,271
Uncle...

1646
01:13:14,646 --> 01:13:16,062
Why did you have to say <i>yes</i>?

1647
01:13:16,063 --> 01:13:16,771
What?!

1648
01:13:18,021 --> 01:13:22,063
Did you approve
because I'm a good boy?

1649
01:13:22,438 --> 01:13:24,396
Not even close.

1650
01:13:24,938 --> 01:13:26,437
What I'm trying to say is...

1651
01:13:26,438 --> 01:13:28,646
It’s the faith
I have in my daughter.

1652
01:13:28,771 --> 01:13:31,521
If we don't trust our children,
who else will?

1653
01:13:32,146 --> 01:13:32,896
Why, Krishna?

1654
01:13:33,021 --> 01:13:34,646
Doesn't your family trust you?

1655
01:13:35,771 --> 01:13:37,521
Sure, they trust me.

1656
01:13:37,896 --> 01:13:39,145
They trust me like crazy!

1657
01:13:39,146 --> 01:13:40,021
See, anyway,

1658
01:13:40,188 --> 01:13:41,688
I'm fine with you two marrying.

1659
01:13:41,896 --> 01:13:43,146
But I have one condition.

1660
01:13:43,438 --> 01:13:47,437
I want my daughter
to have a Grand church wedding.

1661
01:13:47,438 --> 01:13:48,063
That's all!

1662
01:13:48,563 --> 01:13:50,021
I can't convert my religion, Uncle.

1663
01:13:54,021 --> 01:13:55,896
I never asked you to convert.

1664
01:13:57,563 --> 01:13:59,395
There's a marriage class
you need to attend for 10 days.

1665
01:13:59,396 --> 01:14:01,145
Only if you attend it
they will issue a certificate

1666
01:14:01,146 --> 01:14:02,646
to get married in a church.

1667
01:14:03,021 --> 01:14:05,396
Aww! Thanks, Dad.

1668
01:14:05,521 --> 01:14:07,021
- Are you happy, child?
- Yeah.

1669
01:14:07,313 --> 01:14:09,146
Hey, Bugger, are you happy?

1670
01:14:09,813 --> 01:14:11,521
Overjoyed, Magic!

1671
01:14:12,271 --> 01:14:14,271
Okay, come,
let's get him something to eat.

1672
01:14:14,396 --> 01:14:15,021
Yeah, sure.

1673
01:14:19,563 --> 01:14:20,771
Christ Almighty!

1674
01:14:23,063 --> 01:14:26,563
Dude, when will you tell your family?

1675
01:14:26,896 --> 01:14:28,396
Like that will change anything.

1676
01:14:28,646 --> 01:14:30,188
- How much longer?
- Mummy! Mummy!

1677
01:14:32,521 --> 01:14:33,563
My dear son.

1678
01:14:33,771 --> 01:14:35,395
You look great in the shirt.

1679
01:14:35,396 --> 01:14:36,146
Thanks, Mom.

1680
01:14:36,271 --> 01:14:38,271
Now, where is this Mangababu?

1681
01:14:38,396 --> 01:14:39,395
It’s getting late.

1682
01:14:39,396 --> 01:14:41,313
Big sis!

1683
01:14:43,688 --> 01:14:45,646
Here I am!

1684
01:14:49,896 --> 01:14:50,771
He never changes.

1685
01:14:50,896 --> 01:14:52,313
Look at your Uncle.

1686
01:14:59,688 --> 01:15:00,813
What is all this?

1687
01:15:01,063 --> 01:15:03,646
- All for my son-in-law.
- Wow!

1688
01:15:04,521 --> 01:15:06,021
- Your uncle is really fond of you.
- Hand it to me.

1689
01:15:07,271 --> 01:15:09,063
Tanisha, sit close to the air conditioning.

1690
01:15:09,396 --> 01:15:10,896
- He's torturing me.
- Son-in-law.

1691
01:15:11,396 --> 01:15:13,021
- Uncle.
- You’re still pretty young.

1692
01:15:13,396 --> 01:15:15,813
Over the years,
you might have run out of fuel.

1693
01:15:16,521 --> 01:15:18,438
So if you’re looking for nourishment.

1694
01:15:18,563 --> 01:15:21,396
That’s what these cashews and nuts are for.

1695
01:15:21,813 --> 01:15:22,938
Foolish Uncle!

1696
01:15:23,396 --> 01:15:25,313
Don’t be gross!

1697
01:15:25,563 --> 01:15:28,438
Are you such a pure soul, my son?

1698
01:15:28,813 --> 01:15:29,771
So innocent!

1699
01:15:30,021 --> 01:15:32,021
Tanisha, you’re very lucky!

1700
01:15:32,521 --> 01:15:34,396
Decorations are totally awesome!

1701
01:15:34,896 --> 01:15:36,563
Hey, kid. Go over there.

1702
01:15:36,938 --> 01:15:38,688
Dude, get over here.

1703
01:15:38,896 --> 01:15:39,521
Come on!

1704
01:15:46,021 --> 01:15:46,896
Hey, BulBul!

1705
01:15:47,021 --> 01:15:47,895
Go sit in a corner

1706
01:15:47,896 --> 01:15:49,188
You are not the Groom today.

1707
01:15:49,688 --> 01:15:51,312
- Uncle.
- Stop looking and get up.

1708
01:15:51,313 --> 01:15:52,395
Just go!

1709
01:15:52,396 --> 01:15:54,021
- Insult! I'm totally angry.
- Him and his style.

1710
01:15:54,271 --> 01:15:55,896
Son-in-law, you sit in the middle.

1711
01:15:57,771 --> 01:15:59,188
Tanisha, sit next to him.

1712
01:16:00,271 --> 01:16:01,145
Closer!

1713
01:16:01,146 --> 01:16:02,895
What’s with his nagging?

1714
01:16:02,896 --> 01:16:04,146
Big sis, hurry up.

1715
01:16:04,271 --> 01:16:06,146
The groom is waiting.
Quick!

1716
01:16:06,271 --> 01:16:07,438
- Hurry up!
- Hey, Mangababu!

1717
01:16:07,938 --> 01:16:08,771
Your son-in-law is not going anywhere.

1718
01:16:09,021 --> 01:16:09,895
Quit hopping!

1719
01:16:09,896 --> 01:16:10,437
Sit down.

1720
01:16:10,438 --> 01:16:11,646
Yeah, Okay

1721
01:16:11,896 --> 01:16:13,771
My son-in-law neck looks empty.

1722
01:16:13,896 --> 01:16:16,063
- That's for the ceremony!
- Okay, fine.

1723
01:16:16,396 --> 01:16:17,396
Oh, God!

1724
01:16:17,771 --> 01:16:19,062
Shut up for once

1725
01:16:19,063 --> 01:16:19,813
Listen!

1726
01:16:45,646 --> 01:16:46,771
I am going to the station!

1727
01:16:47,146 --> 01:16:47,937
Hey, no need to yell!

1728
01:16:47,938 --> 01:16:50,146
- I'm wearing the machine.
- Cool! Cool!

1729
01:16:50,813 --> 01:16:52,188
Why are you coming with me?

1730
01:16:52,396 --> 01:16:54,062
Are you sending away
your daughter today?

1731
01:16:54,063 --> 01:16:55,312
I can travel by Auto.

1732
01:16:55,313 --> 01:16:57,271
While the bride and groom
can ride together.

1733
01:16:57,438 --> 01:16:58,396
Good idea!

1734
01:16:58,521 --> 01:17:00,146
Drop her off, Son.

1735
01:17:00,271 --> 01:17:01,271
Your uncle is calling for you.

1736
01:17:01,813 --> 01:17:02,895
Come along.

1737
01:17:02,896 --> 01:17:03,896
Go ahead, Son.

1738
01:17:04,396 --> 01:17:05,438
Him too? Whatever!

1739
01:17:06,438 --> 01:17:07,187
Bye!

1740
01:17:07,188 --> 01:17:09,188
- Monkey! Sit inside.
- Bye, sweetie.

1741
01:17:09,688 --> 01:17:11,271
I am so happy today, darling.

1742
01:17:15,646 --> 01:17:16,521
Darling!

1743
01:17:17,563 --> 01:17:18,521
I love you.

1744
01:17:20,396 --> 01:17:21,313
What’s wrong?

1745
01:17:22,396 --> 01:17:23,271
Please get down.

1746
01:17:23,646 --> 01:17:24,521
What for?

1747
01:17:25,146 --> 01:17:26,396
Get down!

1748
01:17:29,271 --> 01:17:30,646
What happened, dude?

1749
01:17:30,771 --> 01:17:32,270
Dude, don’t take this the wrong way.

1750
01:17:32,271 --> 01:17:33,438
But could you drop her off instead?

1751
01:17:34,021 --> 01:17:35,770
Something came up.
I need to leave now.

1752
01:17:35,771 --> 01:17:37,646
He will drop you at the station.
Don't take me wrong.

1753
01:17:37,771 --> 01:17:39,438
- Dude, drop her off.
- Me?

1754
01:17:58,646 --> 01:18:00,021
- Uncle, second ball.
- Hey, wait, wait.

1755
01:18:04,396 --> 01:18:05,688
- Hello!
<i>- Hey, Krish!</i>

1756
01:18:05,896 --> 01:18:07,146
- Yes, Magic. What’s up?
- Hey, Man!

1757
01:18:07,563 --> 01:18:09,770
Can you come over
for like 10 minutes?

1758
01:18:09,771 --> 01:18:11,896
There is a house party at Barbara's place.

1759
01:18:12,021 --> 01:18:12,688
Would you like to join?

1760
01:18:13,021 --> 01:18:15,562
I’m in the middle of something important.

1761
01:18:15,563 --> 01:18:17,187
- So, I can’t make it.
<i>- Important, you say?</i>

1762
01:18:17,188 --> 01:18:18,146
Yeah, exactly!

1763
01:18:18,313 --> 01:18:19,645
Magic, I’ll call you later.

1764
01:18:19,646 --> 01:18:21,270
- I'll call you back.
<i>- It won’t take more than 10 minutes.</i>

1765
01:18:21,271 --> 01:18:22,771
I’ll finish work and call later.

1766
01:18:22,896 --> 01:18:23,438
Hello.

1767
01:18:42,438 --> 01:18:45,146
<i>He seems distant
after the talk with my Dad.</i>

1768
01:18:45,938 --> 01:18:48,146
I have no idea what’s going on with him.

1769
01:18:50,646 --> 01:18:51,646
Dude!

1770
01:18:52,146 --> 01:18:54,021
If you don't like her,
you have to end it.

1771
01:18:54,271 --> 01:18:55,895
You can’t drag this out forever.

1772
01:18:55,896 --> 01:18:57,021
It’s frustrating!

1773
01:18:57,271 --> 01:18:58,771
I can’t say <i>no</i> to her either.

1774
01:18:59,146 --> 01:19:00,688
I am not able to muster the courage
to say it.

1775
01:19:00,896 --> 01:19:02,313
Sometimes, when I look at her...

1776
01:19:02,521 --> 01:19:04,396
She’s a spitting image of my mother.

1777
01:19:06,896 --> 01:19:07,771
Sorry.

1778
01:19:08,563 --> 01:19:09,771
What’s going on with you?

1779
01:19:10,771 --> 01:19:12,771
There’s a tryout
for a government coach, Magic.

1780
01:19:12,938 --> 01:19:15,771
I was tied up with the exam preparations.

1781
01:19:17,396 --> 01:19:19,270
Okay, I can understand.

1782
01:19:19,271 --> 01:19:20,646
Don't stress too much, okay?

1783
01:19:21,146 --> 01:19:21,896
Okay.

1784
01:19:22,646 --> 01:19:23,521
I love you.

1785
01:19:25,771 --> 01:19:26,438
Thanks.

1786
01:19:34,438 --> 01:19:37,145
I said I’d take care of it.

1787
01:19:37,146 --> 01:19:38,437
Quit pestering me.

1788
01:19:38,438 --> 01:19:39,771
I’m trusting you on this.

1789
01:19:39,896 --> 01:19:40,896
I will take care of it.

1790
01:19:41,146 --> 01:19:41,895
Yeah, okay.

1791
01:19:41,896 --> 01:19:43,563
You have nothing to worry about.

1792
01:19:44,646 --> 01:19:45,520
Stop, Uncle!
Leave him alone!

1793
01:19:45,521 --> 01:19:46,896
- How many times should I tell you?
- Uncle!

1794
01:19:47,563 --> 01:19:48,563
I’ll kill you!

1795
01:19:48,771 --> 01:19:51,021
He’s already engaged to another woman.
Yet stringing you along.

1796
01:19:51,521 --> 01:19:52,813
Don't you have any sense?

1797
01:19:53,438 --> 01:19:54,688
Auto! Come over here.

1798
01:19:55,688 --> 01:19:56,437
Get in!

1799
01:19:56,438 --> 01:19:57,688
- Uncle.
- Get inside!

1800
01:19:58,021 --> 01:19:58,938
You too!

1801
01:20:02,896 --> 01:20:04,271
<i>Sis, I caught the love birds!</i>

1802
01:20:04,396 --> 01:20:05,521
<i>I’ll meet you back at the police station.</i>

1803
01:20:11,313 --> 01:20:12,020
Sir!

1804
01:20:12,021 --> 01:20:13,271
- Hey, Baba.
- Greetings, Baba.

1805
01:20:14,021 --> 01:20:15,271
- Everything is fine, sir.
- One minute.

1806
01:20:15,896 --> 01:20:16,896
Baba, brother!

1807
01:20:18,063 --> 01:20:19,563
Oh! What's she doing here?

1808
01:20:20,188 --> 01:20:22,562
Brother, I want to ask you something.

1809
01:20:22,563 --> 01:20:23,688
Will you tell me the truth?

1810
01:20:24,396 --> 01:20:26,146
I’ll tell you what I know.

1811
01:20:26,521 --> 01:20:28,563
Krishna has been avoiding me.

1812
01:20:28,938 --> 01:20:30,313
He is not telling me anything, either.

1813
01:20:30,688 --> 01:20:31,688
What happened to him?

1814
01:20:34,021 --> 01:20:36,646
Would you prefer the truth or the lie?

1815
01:20:36,771 --> 01:20:39,146
I’ve been told
that Bangalore people don’t lie.

1816
01:20:41,688 --> 01:20:43,895
He will never marry you.

1817
01:20:43,896 --> 01:20:44,896
He’s going to break up with you.

1818
01:20:45,313 --> 01:20:46,271
What are you saying?

1819
01:20:46,396 --> 01:20:48,438
Because you're not the right fit for him.

1820
01:20:48,563 --> 01:20:49,896
Not the right fit? Why not?

1821
01:20:50,146 --> 01:20:52,146
Well, you look quite modern.

1822
01:20:52,271 --> 01:20:54,146
You wear tiny shorts.

1823
01:20:54,313 --> 01:20:55,645
Can’t hold your liquor.

1824
01:20:55,646 --> 01:20:57,146
You dance with other men.

1825
01:20:57,271 --> 01:20:58,771
There was something else.

1826
01:20:58,938 --> 01:20:59,645
What was it?

1827
01:20:59,646 --> 01:21:00,645
I can’t remember.

1828
01:21:00,646 --> 01:21:01,521
Got it!

1829
01:21:01,646 --> 01:21:03,188
That you hug people head on.

1830
01:21:03,771 --> 01:21:05,770
Since those things don't suit his family.

1831
01:21:05,771 --> 01:21:07,188
He is going to break up with you.

1832
01:21:07,521 --> 01:21:09,812
Brother, don’t make things up.

1833
01:21:09,813 --> 01:21:10,688
Tell me the truth.

1834
01:21:11,438 --> 01:21:13,396
Without you doing it all...

1835
01:21:13,521 --> 01:21:15,813
how would I know
if he didn’t tell me?

1836
01:21:17,313 --> 01:21:19,062
All I'm saying is...

1837
01:21:19,063 --> 01:21:23,146
he is going to break up with you.

1838
01:21:23,313 --> 01:21:26,563
It's without a doubt.

1839
01:21:29,896 --> 01:21:31,521
Where is he now?

1840
01:21:32,271 --> 01:21:33,438
At home!

1841
01:21:37,396 --> 01:21:39,563
What are you going to do with it?

1842
01:21:40,146 --> 01:21:41,021
Oh, no!

1843
01:21:41,146 --> 01:21:42,395
Baba, this cover is not right.

1844
01:21:42,396 --> 01:21:44,188
Get lost!
It's not the Champions League.

1845
01:21:55,688 --> 01:21:57,271
Magic! What are you doing here?

1846
01:21:57,771 --> 01:21:58,271
Hey!

1847
01:22:01,271 --> 01:22:02,937
Magic, have you lost it?

1848
01:22:02,938 --> 01:22:03,938
What are you doing?

1849
01:22:04,063 --> 01:22:06,271
Does our feelings mean nothing to you?

1850
01:22:06,646 --> 01:22:09,521
You will follow us for years
till we fall in love.

1851
01:22:09,771 --> 01:22:10,896
But the second we reciprocate...

1852
01:22:11,146 --> 01:22:13,771
You break up, citing
that it won't suit your family.

1853
01:22:14,313 --> 01:22:16,521
If you can't commit to a relationship.

1854
01:22:16,646 --> 01:22:18,563
Why the heck do you fall in love
in the first place?

1855
01:22:19,813 --> 01:22:21,396
Who told you that?

1856
01:22:21,563 --> 01:22:22,563
Hey, she's...

1857
01:22:24,438 --> 01:22:25,521
If your family disapproved--

1858
01:22:25,646 --> 01:22:27,063
Who told you this?

1859
01:22:28,896 --> 01:22:33,146
Who told you
that I’d break up with you?

1860
01:22:33,271 --> 01:22:34,146
It was me!

1861
01:22:36,813 --> 01:22:39,521
I can’t take responsibility
for a blabber mouth.

1862
01:22:39,771 --> 01:22:41,771
I know how to stay loyal.

1863
01:22:42,396 --> 01:22:43,396
Did you ask me?

1864
01:22:43,771 --> 01:22:45,896
Did you ask me before lashing out?

1865
01:22:46,396 --> 01:22:47,021
I did not.

1866
01:22:47,646 --> 01:22:49,062
You are-- You are right.

1867
01:22:49,063 --> 01:22:50,271
I probably should have asked you.

1868
01:22:50,396 --> 01:22:52,021
Yes, you should have!

1869
01:22:52,271 --> 01:22:53,813
Instead, you're smashing the television.

1870
01:22:54,396 --> 01:22:55,146
Oh, no!

1871
01:22:55,563 --> 01:22:56,313
Sorry

1872
01:22:56,438 --> 01:22:57,687
Really sorry, Krishna!

1873
01:22:57,688 --> 01:22:59,395
I overreacted.

1874
01:22:59,396 --> 01:23:00,563
- Sorry!
- Forget it!

1875
01:23:00,896 --> 01:23:01,896
Listen here, Magic.

1876
01:23:02,646 --> 01:23:06,188
You can’t let a third person
come between us.

1877
01:23:06,396 --> 01:23:07,937
Brother, why didn’t you--

1878
01:23:07,938 --> 01:23:08,563
Magic!

1879
01:23:08,938 --> 01:23:10,563
You don't have to ask anyone else.

1880
01:23:11,271 --> 01:23:12,271
There's no need.

1881
01:23:12,688 --> 01:23:13,938
Trust me, first.

1882
01:23:14,396 --> 01:23:16,437
Your lack of trust caused this.

1883
01:23:16,438 --> 01:23:18,145
That’s a complete 180.

1884
01:23:18,146 --> 01:23:19,771
- Sorry, Krishna. My bad.
- Too late!

1885
01:23:20,146 --> 01:23:22,437
- I'm sorry, Krishna.
- You don't trust me.

1886
01:23:22,438 --> 01:23:23,812
- Let it go.
- Sorry! Sorry!

1887
01:23:23,813 --> 01:23:24,688
Sorry, Bugger!

1888
01:23:25,896 --> 01:23:27,020
We’re cool!

1889
01:23:27,021 --> 01:23:28,146
Hi, Magic!

1890
01:23:29,896 --> 01:23:31,562
Hi Bommi, how are you?

1891
01:23:31,563 --> 01:23:33,521
- Why do you do this, Dude?
- Fine!

1892
01:23:33,896 --> 01:23:35,895
Is no one else home?

1893
01:23:35,896 --> 01:23:36,646
Where is everyone?

1894
01:23:36,771 --> 01:23:38,021
Did they all go out somewhere?

1895
01:23:40,396 --> 01:23:42,146
Please don't tell her.
Don't tell her.

1896
01:23:42,396 --> 01:23:44,770
Don't say anything.

1897
01:23:44,771 --> 01:23:46,146
Please don't say anything.

1898
01:23:48,438 --> 01:23:50,146
Since Krishna Uncle’s...

1899
01:23:50,271 --> 01:23:55,271
Fiance came over last week for the feast.

1900
01:23:55,396 --> 01:24:00,896
So it’s our family’s turn
to go over to their house for a feast.

1901
01:24:01,021 --> 01:24:02,063
Game over!

1902
01:24:02,521 --> 01:24:05,313
Magic, I can explain--

1903
01:24:07,896 --> 01:24:08,937
Damn it, you bugger!

1904
01:24:08,938 --> 01:24:09,770
- Magic!
- It wasn't me.

1905
01:24:09,771 --> 01:24:10,520
Magic!

1906
01:24:10,521 --> 01:24:12,146
Are you mad or what?

1907
01:24:12,271 --> 01:24:13,437
Sorry, dude!

1908
01:24:13,438 --> 01:24:15,063
She brought it out of me.

1909
01:24:26,521 --> 01:24:28,937
Mom, I keep telling you
I don't want anything.

1910
01:24:28,938 --> 01:24:30,520
Why are you irritating me like this?

1911
01:24:30,521 --> 01:24:32,062
Please leave me alone for once.

1912
01:24:32,063 --> 01:24:32,771
Please!

1913
01:24:34,021 --> 01:24:35,646
- Hello!
- Darling!

1914
01:24:36,688 --> 01:24:40,563
I’m sorry if I offended you.

1915
01:24:41,146 --> 01:24:43,271
I shouldn’t have said what I said.

1916
01:24:43,896 --> 01:24:45,521
It’s nothing like that.

1917
01:24:46,563 --> 01:24:48,146
It was my fault. Sorry!

1918
01:24:48,521 --> 01:24:50,645
Why are you apologizing?!

1919
01:24:50,646 --> 01:24:51,563
Please don't apologize!

1920
01:24:53,438 --> 01:24:57,396
I’m coming to Chennai tomorrow.

1921
01:24:58,396 --> 01:25:01,271
Can you show me around?

1922
01:25:10,146 --> 01:25:13,063
Is Marina Beach always clean?
Or there are a lot of stones...

1923
01:25:14,146 --> 01:25:14,896
Tanisha...

1924
01:25:15,271 --> 01:25:17,021
The only thing modern about her
is her name.

1925
01:25:17,938 --> 01:25:19,770
So you don’t like it
if they’re modern.

1926
01:25:19,771 --> 01:25:21,188
And you don’t like it
if they’re not.

1927
01:25:21,313 --> 01:25:22,813
Do you even know what you want?

1928
01:25:25,021 --> 01:25:25,896
Clifton...

1929
01:25:26,438 --> 01:25:27,896
I can't decide yet.

1930
01:25:29,396 --> 01:25:30,771
I think I need some more time.

1931
01:25:36,188 --> 01:25:37,396
Maybe this is for the best, Dude.

1932
01:25:37,563 --> 01:25:39,312
You were going to do it yourself.

1933
01:25:39,313 --> 01:25:40,521
Time to move on!

1934
01:25:41,521 --> 01:25:42,896
I indeed thought about it.

1935
01:25:43,896 --> 01:25:45,646
But there's a way to do it.

1936
01:25:47,438 --> 01:25:49,271
Maybe she doesn't fit into my family.

1937
01:25:49,646 --> 01:25:51,396
But I never stopped loving her.

1938
01:25:57,313 --> 01:25:58,396
I’ve said all I can.

1939
01:25:58,938 --> 01:26:00,562
And I can’t keep dodging
my Mom’s questions.

1940
01:26:00,563 --> 01:26:02,646
Dad, did you shave your beard?

1941
01:26:02,813 --> 01:26:05,438
Mom, can you turn on
the grinder for me?

1942
01:26:05,688 --> 01:26:07,437
- Bommi! I ought to!
- Sathya!

1943
01:26:07,438 --> 01:26:10,187
Please, Mom

1944
01:26:10,188 --> 01:26:11,563
You switch it on. I'll be there.

1945
01:26:12,146 --> 01:26:13,145
Yay!

1946
01:26:13,146 --> 01:26:15,896
Don’t deflect your anger towards me
onto the child.

1947
01:26:18,271 --> 01:26:19,395
I can’t move out of my parents’ house.

1948
01:26:19,396 --> 01:26:20,021
Period.

1949
01:26:21,021 --> 01:26:22,271
I can’t just abandon my mother.

1950
01:26:23,646 --> 01:26:25,021
Imagine yourself in my shoes.

1951
01:26:26,521 --> 01:26:27,896
Then abandon the two of us.

1952
01:26:28,021 --> 01:26:29,521
What? What do you mean?

1953
01:26:30,188 --> 01:26:31,271
Where do you want me to go?

1954
01:26:31,438 --> 01:26:32,313
Where the hell am I supposed to go?

1955
01:26:49,021 --> 01:26:49,771
What happened?

1956
01:26:51,646 --> 01:26:53,063
Did he say something?

1957
01:26:54,521 --> 01:26:55,688
It’s not his fault.

1958
01:26:57,063 --> 01:26:58,021
It’s my own.

1959
01:26:58,688 --> 01:26:59,313
Hey!

1960
01:27:00,521 --> 01:27:01,771
Neither here nor there.

1961
01:27:03,438 --> 01:27:05,771
Each day,
I feel increasingly conflicted.

1962
01:27:07,438 --> 01:27:08,646
The fault is my own.

1963
01:27:10,313 --> 01:27:12,063
If you like something,
you need to fight for it.

1964
01:27:13,146 --> 01:27:15,813
Or you should let it go.

1965
01:27:18,646 --> 01:27:21,146
But I can't seem to decide on anything.

1966
01:27:21,438 --> 01:27:22,063
Sathya!

1967
01:27:22,521 --> 01:27:24,187
I'm struggling with it.

1968
01:27:24,188 --> 01:27:25,313
Hey, idiot!

1969
01:27:25,688 --> 01:27:26,938
Stop crying.

1970
01:27:27,771 --> 01:27:28,938
He’s also at fault here.

1971
01:27:30,146 --> 01:27:30,896
No!

1972
01:27:31,896 --> 01:27:33,646
He likes me too much.

1973
01:27:34,396 --> 01:27:36,063
He’s struggling without me
by his side.

1974
01:27:36,646 --> 01:27:39,021
Caught between his mom and me.

1975
01:27:39,896 --> 01:27:40,521
Look here...

1976
01:27:41,146 --> 01:27:42,313
that’s not for you to decide.

1977
01:27:42,646 --> 01:27:43,521
Let him do it.

1978
01:27:45,021 --> 01:27:46,313
He doesn't need to.

1979
01:27:48,063 --> 01:27:49,396
You can see it in their actions.

1980
01:27:50,896 --> 01:27:53,021
When someone really likes us...

1981
01:27:54,521 --> 01:27:57,896
and they realize they’d be miserable
without us

1982
01:27:59,271 --> 01:28:00,771
they'll definitely come back to us.

1983
01:28:01,813 --> 01:28:03,271
One day or another

1984
01:28:04,188 --> 01:28:06,063
hoping that we'll forgive
and take them back.

1985
01:28:16,521 --> 01:28:17,146
Magic!

1986
01:28:18,021 --> 01:28:18,646
Magic!

1987
01:28:20,271 --> 01:28:21,021
Magic!

1988
01:28:27,396 --> 01:28:28,146
Magic!

1989
01:28:34,146 --> 01:28:35,396
Sorry, Magic.

1990
01:28:36,813 --> 01:28:38,521
I never meant to hurt you.

1991
01:28:46,521 --> 01:28:47,563
Dear, Jesus!

1992
01:28:48,021 --> 01:28:50,896
I committed a grave sin
by hurting my lover.

1993
01:28:51,313 --> 01:28:54,396
Please forgive me
and get her to talk to me.

1994
01:28:54,646 --> 01:28:57,521
You sound foolish
when you try to act smart.

1995
01:28:58,188 --> 01:29:00,271
I'm enraged enough to break your teeth.

1996
01:29:00,938 --> 01:29:02,896
If you have shame, stay away.

1997
01:29:05,021 --> 01:29:06,646
Jesus, what was that?

1998
01:29:17,146 --> 01:29:18,021
Hi, Magic!

1999
01:29:21,313 --> 01:29:23,646
What the heck do you want,
you bloody bugger?

2000
01:29:24,188 --> 01:29:25,521
Don't make me smack you.

2001
01:29:25,938 --> 01:29:28,646
I have no pride left in me.

2002
01:29:29,271 --> 01:29:32,188
No matter what you say or do...

2003
01:29:32,521 --> 01:29:33,563
I won't leave your side.

2004
01:29:33,896 --> 01:29:34,521
Hey!

2005
01:29:35,646 --> 01:29:36,771
What the hell do you want?

2006
01:29:37,646 --> 01:29:39,396
Do you think you’re some hero?

2007
01:29:40,146 --> 01:29:42,938
Do you think
I won’t make a scene in public?

2008
01:29:43,896 --> 01:29:45,521
Driver, stop the bus!

2009
01:29:47,813 --> 01:29:49,146
You'd better get off the bus now.

2010
01:29:49,646 --> 01:29:51,313
Or else, you'll be humiliated
beyond your imagination.

2011
01:30:18,271 --> 01:30:20,688
Now, do you realize
how it hurts to be rejected?

2012
01:30:22,313 --> 01:30:24,896
That's how it feels when you're
humiliated in public for love.

2013
01:30:25,021 --> 01:30:26,438
That's how I was feeling the other day.

2014
01:30:27,063 --> 01:30:29,146
I never meant to hurt you.

2015
01:30:30,521 --> 01:30:31,938
I shouldn't have done that either.

2016
01:30:32,521 --> 01:30:33,188
Sorry!

2017
01:30:34,021 --> 01:30:35,021
I'm too sorry, Magic.

2018
01:30:35,771 --> 01:30:37,188
I shouldn't have hurt you.

2019
01:30:38,188 --> 01:30:41,770
I was worried you wouldn’t fit
into my family--

2020
01:30:41,771 --> 01:30:42,563
See, Krishna!

2021
01:30:43,021 --> 01:30:46,021
I know our families don’t share
the same culture.

2022
01:30:46,896 --> 01:30:48,645
If you were worried about how I’d fit in...

2023
01:30:48,646 --> 01:30:49,938
You should have asked me first.

2024
01:30:50,896 --> 01:30:52,646
But how is that possible?

2025
01:30:52,896 --> 01:30:55,563
You can try to adapt to my culture.

2026
01:30:56,146 --> 01:30:58,646
While I try to adapt to your family.

2027
01:30:59,063 --> 01:31:00,645
Or we could move out.

2028
01:31:00,646 --> 01:31:01,771
And lead our own lives.

2029
01:31:02,396 --> 01:31:03,313
Isn’t that what love is?

2030
01:31:04,688 --> 01:31:05,521
Sorry, Magic.

2031
01:31:06,146 --> 01:31:07,312
Really sorry, Magic.

2032
01:31:07,313 --> 01:31:08,938
Apologies from the bottom of my heart.

2033
01:31:09,146 --> 01:31:10,521
From here on out...

2034
01:31:10,813 --> 01:31:13,021
You’ll be the one I marry.

2035
01:31:13,646 --> 01:31:15,520
Please, Magic.
Sorry, Magic.

2036
01:31:15,521 --> 01:31:17,521
Trust me.
One last chance, Magic

2037
01:31:17,771 --> 01:31:19,271
- Last chance--
- What about your fiancé?

2038
01:31:22,021 --> 01:31:23,937
We were never meant to be.

2039
01:31:23,938 --> 01:31:26,521
She’s better off with someone else.

2040
01:31:27,271 --> 01:31:28,563
I’ll confront my family.

2041
01:31:29,021 --> 01:31:30,188
With all the courage I can muster.

2042
01:31:30,396 --> 01:31:31,771
That I like Magic.

2043
01:31:32,438 --> 01:31:33,396
Can I trust you this time?

2044
01:31:33,771 --> 01:31:36,521
Trust me, one last chance please.

2045
01:31:37,896 --> 01:31:39,396
Last chance, you bugger.

2046
01:31:40,021 --> 01:31:41,021
Thank you, Magic!

2047
01:31:54,146 --> 01:31:55,938
You need to tell our Mom
about my love.

2048
01:31:56,146 --> 01:31:57,521
Hey, why me?

2049
01:31:57,813 --> 01:31:59,645
Oh, no! Please spare me.

2050
01:31:59,646 --> 01:32:01,646
Didn't you agree to help me back then?

2051
01:32:01,771 --> 01:32:03,938
That was an isolated event.
I can't go through with it.

2052
01:32:04,146 --> 01:32:05,270
No way!

2053
01:32:05,271 --> 01:32:08,688
- Not happening.
- Please, please.

2054
01:32:08,813 --> 01:32:10,021
- I said please.
- Hey!

2055
01:32:11,146 --> 01:32:12,688
Chiranjeevi might be able to
persuade Mom.

2056
01:32:12,813 --> 01:32:13,646
Who are you again?

2057
01:32:13,938 --> 01:32:14,438
Hey!

2058
01:32:15,021 --> 01:32:16,312
Just hear me out first.

2059
01:32:16,313 --> 01:32:17,771
And why should I?

2060
01:32:18,063 --> 01:32:19,396
When have you ever listened to me?

2061
01:32:19,521 --> 01:32:21,063
Ma’am, check this.
Here you go.

2062
01:32:21,396 --> 01:32:23,521
Didn’t I tell you
to take that government exam?

2063
01:32:23,646 --> 01:32:26,312
You're talking irrelevant
to what I'm about to say.

2064
01:32:26,313 --> 01:32:27,146
I will talk irrelevant!

2065
01:32:27,438 --> 01:32:28,396
If you'd like then listen.

2066
01:32:28,563 --> 01:32:29,521
On second thought, don’t.

2067
01:32:29,938 --> 01:32:31,146
Get out of my office!

2068
01:32:31,896 --> 01:32:32,563
Hey!

2069
01:32:32,771 --> 01:32:33,563
Get out!

2070
01:32:35,313 --> 01:32:35,938
Hey!

2071
01:32:36,271 --> 01:32:37,396
Why are you worried?

2072
01:32:37,563 --> 01:32:38,646
I can talk to your Mom.

2073
01:32:39,271 --> 01:32:40,021
Seriously?

2074
01:32:40,146 --> 01:32:41,895
Yeah, why not!
I'm not scared of her.

2075
01:32:41,896 --> 01:32:43,896
Can you run it by me once?

2076
01:32:44,021 --> 01:32:45,813
For God’s sake, I’m not a child.

2077
01:32:45,938 --> 01:32:48,187
I’ll tell her myself.

2078
01:32:48,188 --> 01:32:49,521
Wait, wait!

2079
01:32:49,813 --> 01:32:51,813
My Mom will never believe
that I’m in love.

2080
01:32:53,771 --> 01:32:54,771
Don't add too much water.

2081
01:32:55,021 --> 01:32:56,270
Auntie, how are you?

2082
01:32:56,271 --> 01:32:57,145
All good?

2083
01:32:57,146 --> 01:32:58,020
I’m doing just fine.

2084
01:32:58,021 --> 01:32:59,520
What brought you here?

2085
01:32:59,521 --> 01:33:01,063
Just wanted to tell you something.

2086
01:33:01,271 --> 01:33:02,146
What is it about?

2087
01:33:02,271 --> 01:33:05,521
Our boy Krishna
is in love with a girl.

2088
01:33:05,646 --> 01:33:06,562
Love?!

2089
01:33:06,563 --> 01:33:07,770
Who's the girl?

2090
01:33:07,771 --> 01:33:09,271
I’m glad you asked.

2091
01:33:09,688 --> 01:33:11,771
She looks like an actress.

2092
01:33:12,146 --> 01:33:13,646
Take a look, Auntie.

2093
01:33:16,146 --> 01:33:18,021
Our boy’s got good taste.

2094
01:33:18,646 --> 01:33:19,938
She’s pretty, isn’t she?

2095
01:33:20,271 --> 01:33:22,146
You can't say no to her.

2096
01:33:22,271 --> 01:33:23,938
Good choice, right?

2097
01:33:34,271 --> 01:33:35,687
I tried to warn you.

2098
01:33:35,688 --> 01:33:38,313
My Mom will never believe
that I’m in love.

2099
01:33:39,563 --> 01:33:41,188
It’s true that your Mom never bought it.

2100
01:33:41,396 --> 01:33:43,146
But not the part about you being in love.

2101
01:33:44,396 --> 01:33:47,271
It was the fact
that any girl would love you back.

2102
01:33:51,771 --> 01:33:53,020
It hurts to laugh.

2103
01:33:53,021 --> 01:33:54,021
Hilarious!

2104
01:33:54,396 --> 01:33:55,146
Dad!

2105
01:33:55,271 --> 01:33:56,646
I’m in love with a girl.

2106
01:33:56,896 --> 01:33:57,521
What?

2107
01:33:57,813 --> 01:33:58,396
Love?

2108
01:33:58,688 --> 01:33:59,146
You?

2109
01:33:59,396 --> 01:34:00,063
Really?

2110
01:34:00,396 --> 01:34:02,438
Fantastic news!

2111
01:34:02,646 --> 01:34:04,020
Dad, about the girl...

2112
01:34:04,021 --> 01:34:04,937
The one you spoke about the other day.

2113
01:34:04,938 --> 01:34:06,021
Exactly, Dad!

2114
01:34:06,188 --> 01:34:07,562
If you can meet her first...

2115
01:34:07,563 --> 01:34:09,020
then I can introduce her to Mom.

2116
01:34:09,021 --> 01:34:10,646
Why wait?
I’ll meet her tomorrow.

2117
01:34:12,563 --> 01:34:13,521
Super, Dad.

2118
01:34:14,146 --> 01:34:17,396
Dad still remembers
that the girl is Anglo-Indian.

2119
01:34:18,021 --> 01:34:18,771
Superb!

2120
01:34:20,563 --> 01:34:21,520
Just like he said...

2121
01:34:21,521 --> 01:34:23,896
looks like he found a girl
from our caste.

2122
01:34:24,771 --> 01:34:26,062
Magic, that's my dad.

2123
01:34:26,063 --> 01:34:27,521
Brother, that's a fantastic song.

2124
01:34:28,313 --> 01:34:28,938
Dad!

2125
01:34:30,521 --> 01:34:32,021
- [in Telugu] How are you, dear?
- I'll get us tea.

2126
01:34:32,146 --> 01:34:33,020
Uncle?

2127
01:34:33,021 --> 01:34:34,146
[in Telugu] I asked How are you doing?

2128
01:34:35,646 --> 01:34:37,562
Uncle, I don’t understand Telugu.

2129
01:34:37,563 --> 01:34:40,146
I assumed a girl from our caste
would speak Telugu.

2130
01:34:40,271 --> 01:34:42,146
How could you assume
I belong to your caste?

2131
01:34:43,896 --> 01:34:44,521
Son...

2132
01:34:44,813 --> 01:34:45,771
Isn’t she one of us?

2133
01:34:45,896 --> 01:34:46,563
Dad!

2134
01:34:46,771 --> 01:34:48,188
She’s an Anglo-Indian!

2135
01:34:48,313 --> 01:34:49,771
Can’t you tell from the way she looks?

2136
01:35:01,021 --> 01:35:03,021
It can’t be an Anglo-Indian!

2137
01:35:03,313 --> 01:35:04,021
Hey!

2138
01:35:04,313 --> 01:35:06,896
Did you throw a challenge the other day?

2139
01:35:07,271 --> 01:35:08,521
I was clearly bluffing.

2140
01:35:08,646 --> 01:35:10,771
That doesn't mean you take it seriously
and act on it.

2141
01:35:11,146 --> 01:35:11,813
Dad!

2142
01:35:12,396 --> 01:35:14,395
These people cannot adapt
to our family's culture.

2143
01:35:14,396 --> 01:35:16,646
- Please hear me out--
- And who are you to decide that?

2144
01:35:18,063 --> 01:35:19,646
You're meeting me for the first time.

2145
01:35:20,146 --> 01:35:24,021
You only have the right
to approve or reject me.

2146
01:35:24,271 --> 01:35:26,771
Instead don't judge
or assume things on my behalf.

2147
01:35:27,438 --> 01:35:29,146
Now, do you approve or not?

2148
01:35:29,646 --> 01:35:31,146
What’s your verdict?

2149
01:35:36,396 --> 01:35:37,063
My dear son...

2150
01:35:38,063 --> 01:35:39,271
What your mother is to me.

2151
01:35:40,396 --> 01:35:41,271
She is to you.

2152
01:35:42,271 --> 01:35:44,771
Men like us are bound to end up
with women like her.

2153
01:35:45,521 --> 01:35:46,646
Thanks, Uncle!

2154
01:35:47,146 --> 01:35:48,063
Let’s have some coffee.

2155
01:35:49,146 --> 01:35:50,396
- Phew!
- Dad!

2156
01:35:50,688 --> 01:35:52,521
Could you also tell mom about this?

2157
01:35:53,146 --> 01:35:53,896
As if!

2158
01:35:54,146 --> 01:35:54,937
Dad!

2159
01:35:54,938 --> 01:35:56,563
It won’t be that easy.

2160
01:35:56,896 --> 01:35:58,812
First we need to change her
for your Mom.

2161
01:35:58,813 --> 01:36:00,520
Change what?

2162
01:36:00,521 --> 01:36:02,813
Why are you always on the edge?

2163
01:36:02,938 --> 01:36:05,020
I was just asking, Uncle.

2164
01:36:05,021 --> 01:36:06,021
Is this the tone you always speak in?

2165
01:36:06,813 --> 01:36:09,021
Never mind, Dad. Tell us what to do.

2166
01:36:09,313 --> 01:36:12,646
His mom considers her caste and creed
as the most important aspects.

2167
01:36:13,271 --> 01:36:14,688
I reckon it doesn't matter to you.

2168
01:36:15,146 --> 01:36:15,771
My dear!

2169
01:36:15,938 --> 01:36:18,312
Since it's new to you,
try to get the hang of it.

2170
01:36:18,313 --> 01:36:18,896
Dad!

2171
01:36:19,146 --> 01:36:21,063
- This will never work out.
- It’s fine, Krish.

2172
01:36:21,313 --> 01:36:22,146
I can learn.

2173
01:36:24,438 --> 01:36:26,813
My father too asked you to attend
the marriage classes.

2174
01:36:28,896 --> 01:36:31,021
We’ll learn each others cultures.

2175
01:36:31,521 --> 01:36:33,063
Love is all about adapting, right?

2176
01:36:33,688 --> 01:36:34,521
Let's learn!

2177
01:36:36,938 --> 01:36:37,646
Cheers, dear!

2178
01:36:38,396 --> 01:36:39,271
Cheers, Uncle.

2179
01:36:56,688 --> 01:36:58,563
<i>♪ We're a match made in heaven ♪</i>

2180
01:36:58,896 --> 01:37:00,646
<i>♪ No match could be finer ♪</i>

2181
01:37:01,021 --> 01:37:05,021
<i>♪ Here we are,
Writing a brand-new love story. ♪</i>

2182
01:37:05,396 --> 01:37:06,771
<i>♪ Love robs me of sleep ♪</i>

2183
01:37:06,896 --> 01:37:07,938
Krishna Benjamin

2184
01:37:08,396 --> 01:37:09,646
Magic Gonsalves

2185
01:37:10,188 --> 01:37:13,896
I’m glad to have you both here.

2186
01:37:14,146 --> 01:37:16,021
<i>♪ As I seek my way ♪</i>

2187
01:37:16,313 --> 01:37:18,021
<i>♪ Every path finds you ♪</i>

2188
01:37:18,146 --> 01:37:21,646
<i>♪ Somehow, magic and miracles entwined ♪</i>

2189
01:37:21,771 --> 01:37:24,396
You should see the lengths
she goes to for Mom’s approval.

2190
01:37:24,938 --> 01:37:26,563
I was too quick to judge her.

2191
01:37:26,688 --> 01:37:27,645
That’s great!

2192
01:37:27,646 --> 01:37:29,395
- When are you going to tell Mom?
- Hey!

2193
01:37:29,396 --> 01:37:30,771
Can you tell her instead?

2194
01:37:30,896 --> 01:37:32,021
You’re on your own!

2195
01:37:33,771 --> 01:37:35,646
<i>♪ Wedding bells fill the air ♪</i>

2196
01:37:35,896 --> 01:37:37,896
<i>♪ Even butterflies found their soulmates ♪</i>

2197
01:37:38,146 --> 01:37:40,146
<i>♪ Two hearts have become one ♪</i>

2198
01:37:40,271 --> 01:37:42,271
<i>♪ Hare Rama...
What a beautiful madness ♪</i>

2199
01:37:42,521 --> 01:37:44,521
<i>♪ Wedding bells fill the air ♪</i>

2200
01:37:45,021 --> 01:37:48,271
[Prayer] "Om Vigna Vinayaka Pada Namaste."

2201
01:37:48,521 --> 01:37:50,021
Coming 8th is Ammavasai.

2202
01:37:50,188 --> 01:37:51,146
What’s that?

2203
01:37:51,688 --> 01:37:53,645
It means no moon day.

2204
01:37:53,646 --> 01:37:54,895
And Povurnami is a full moon day.

2205
01:37:54,896 --> 01:37:59,646
This book will tell you
how to use this rosary.

2206
01:38:07,688 --> 01:38:08,688
Hey! What’s all this?

2207
01:38:08,938 --> 01:38:10,688
She is in a spiritual awakening.

2208
01:38:11,521 --> 01:38:15,271
[Chanting Prayer]

2209
01:38:26,063 --> 01:38:28,063
<i>♪ Wedding bells fill the air ♪</i>

2210
01:38:28,271 --> 01:38:30,271
<i>♪ Even butterflies found their soulmates ♪</i>

2211
01:38:30,438 --> 01:38:32,438
<i>♪ Two hearts have become one ♪</i>

2212
01:38:32,646 --> 01:38:34,646
<i>♪ Hare Rama...
What a beautiful madness ♪</i>

2213
01:38:34,896 --> 01:38:36,896
<i>♪ Hare Rama...
What a beautiful madness ♪</i>

2214
01:38:37,021 --> 01:38:39,021
<i>♪ Hare Rama...
What a beautiful madness ♪</i>

2215
01:38:39,188 --> 01:38:41,896
<i>♪ Hare Rama...
What a beautiful madness ♪</i>

2216
01:38:42,146 --> 01:38:42,896
That’s it!

2217
01:38:43,271 --> 01:38:44,521
You’re almost ready.

2218
01:38:45,146 --> 01:38:46,312
Tomorrow is Sashti.

2219
01:38:46,313 --> 01:38:47,271
No, Uncle.

2220
01:38:47,396 --> 01:38:48,521
Sashti isn’t tomorrow.

2221
01:38:48,646 --> 01:38:49,395
It’s Pradosham.

2222
01:38:49,396 --> 01:38:50,562
Fantastic!

2223
01:38:50,563 --> 01:38:51,938
- She's fantastic.
- Well done!

2224
01:38:52,271 --> 01:38:53,021
You will definitely pass the test.

2225
01:38:53,146 --> 01:38:54,937
You come to the temple tomorrow.
We'll break the new over there.

2226
01:38:54,938 --> 01:38:56,271
She has to say yes.
Don’t you worry.

2227
01:38:56,646 --> 01:38:57,271
Okay, Uncle.

2228
01:38:57,438 --> 01:38:59,020
Don’t forget to wear the outfit I chose.

2229
01:38:59,021 --> 01:38:59,646
Okay, done!

2230
01:39:01,563 --> 01:39:02,271
Hey!

2231
01:39:02,396 --> 01:39:03,146
That was our thing.

2232
01:39:13,896 --> 01:39:15,395
This is a surprise.

2233
01:39:15,396 --> 01:39:16,813
I’ve never seen you here before.

2234
01:39:17,896 --> 01:39:19,563
We wanted to pray?
Start praying.

2235
01:39:20,271 --> 01:39:21,021
Really?

2236
01:39:21,813 --> 01:39:23,771
Do you expect me to believe that?

2237
01:39:26,646 --> 01:39:27,521
Time is running out.

2238
01:39:27,646 --> 01:39:29,145
She’ll be here soon.

2239
01:39:29,146 --> 01:39:29,896
Whatever!

2240
01:39:35,521 --> 01:39:36,521
Dad she's here.

2241
01:40:00,146 --> 01:40:00,896
Come on, dear.

2242
01:40:02,021 --> 01:40:02,563
Come!

2243
01:40:03,313 --> 01:40:04,771
You look stunning in a saree.

2244
01:40:06,438 --> 01:40:07,645
You’re just in the nick of time.

2245
01:40:07,646 --> 01:40:09,521
She just started the rounds.

2246
01:40:09,688 --> 01:40:11,188
After the 8th round,
she'll halt right there.

2247
01:40:11,646 --> 01:40:13,563
Fall at her feet, right then and there.

2248
01:40:13,771 --> 01:40:15,563
She won’t get angry at that time.

2249
01:40:15,896 --> 01:40:16,521
All the best!

2250
01:40:16,813 --> 01:40:17,646
Thank you, Uncle.

2251
01:40:17,813 --> 01:40:18,896
Okay, carry on.

2252
01:40:19,938 --> 01:40:20,521
Hang on a second...

2253
01:40:20,688 --> 01:40:23,062
How did you figure out
Mom won't get angry out there?

2254
01:40:23,063 --> 01:40:25,271
Cause that’s where I told her
of my old love.

2255
01:40:26,063 --> 01:40:28,021
You’re hopeless!

2256
01:40:47,813 --> 01:40:48,813
Fall at her feet.

2257
01:40:49,646 --> 01:40:50,313
Do it!

2258
01:41:01,063 --> 01:41:02,021
Fall at her feet.

2259
01:41:02,813 --> 01:41:04,188
Please, Magic.

2260
01:41:14,563 --> 01:41:16,021
Bless me, aunty.

2261
01:41:21,646 --> 01:41:22,313
Mom...

2262
01:41:22,688 --> 01:41:23,938
This is my lover, Revathy.

2263
01:41:24,396 --> 01:41:25,146
Lover?!

2264
01:41:25,646 --> 01:41:26,521
Oh, no!

2265
01:41:26,646 --> 01:41:27,646
Hey, Chiranjeevi!

2266
01:41:28,146 --> 01:41:29,146
What do you mean?

2267
01:41:29,271 --> 01:41:31,021
She is one of us, Mom.

2268
01:41:31,396 --> 01:41:32,646
Oh! Our caste?

2269
01:41:34,271 --> 01:41:35,313
I’m glad!

2270
01:41:37,438 --> 01:41:38,646
Even in love...

2271
01:41:38,896 --> 01:41:40,938
you stayed loyal to your caste.

2272
01:41:42,438 --> 01:41:44,063
I’m very happy!

2273
01:41:44,271 --> 01:41:45,021
Thanks, Mom!

2274
01:41:45,146 --> 01:41:46,646
What does your father do, Dear?

2275
01:41:46,813 --> 01:41:48,646
Her father is my office head.
It's her daughter.

2276
01:41:48,896 --> 01:41:49,770
He never changes!

2277
01:41:49,771 --> 01:41:50,437
Super!

2278
01:41:50,438 --> 01:41:51,396
Mom!

2279
01:41:52,146 --> 01:41:52,771
This is...

2280
01:41:53,646 --> 01:41:55,188
This is my lover.

2281
01:41:56,771 --> 01:41:57,646
Her name is...

2282
01:41:58,396 --> 01:41:59,146
Her name...

2283
01:41:59,938 --> 01:42:00,646
Magic!

2284
01:42:03,688 --> 01:42:05,396
Magic Gonsalves.

2285
01:42:07,188 --> 01:42:07,771
Go for it

2286
01:42:08,563 --> 01:42:09,646
Bless me too, Auntie.

2287
01:42:18,938 --> 01:42:20,521
Who gave you permission
to fall in love?

2288
01:42:20,771 --> 01:42:21,688
And with Christian--

2289
01:42:22,063 --> 01:42:23,688
I can't even pronounce her name.

2290
01:42:23,813 --> 01:42:25,646
Where did you even find her?

2291
01:42:25,771 --> 01:42:27,396
Mom, we just came from the temple.

2292
01:42:28,021 --> 01:42:28,896
I can't eat egg now...

2293
01:42:29,521 --> 01:42:30,313
Learn from him.

2294
01:42:31,021 --> 01:42:32,646
I’m proud to call him my son.

2295
01:42:33,146 --> 01:42:35,521
He kept his family in mind
while falling in love.

2296
01:42:36,521 --> 01:42:38,146
I can never refuse him.

2297
01:42:38,271 --> 01:42:39,062
Thanks, Mom!

2298
01:42:39,063 --> 01:42:40,063
Good son!

2299
01:42:40,188 --> 01:42:42,020
Mom, Magic is alike.

2300
01:42:42,021 --> 01:42:44,063
She even wore a saree for your sake.

2301
01:42:45,063 --> 01:42:49,021
Wearing a saree won't change
one's religion.

2302
01:42:49,146 --> 01:42:50,063
Zip it!

2303
01:42:50,188 --> 01:42:51,270
If you keep talking

2304
01:42:51,271 --> 01:42:52,020
I’ll kill you myself.

2305
01:42:52,021 --> 01:42:53,020
It’s not like that, Mom.

2306
01:42:53,021 --> 01:42:54,770
Just meet her once.
She's a good girl.

2307
01:42:54,771 --> 01:42:55,396
Shush!

2308
01:42:56,438 --> 01:42:57,770
I've already spoken.

2309
01:42:57,771 --> 01:42:59,188
There’s nothing more to say.

2310
01:43:01,271 --> 01:43:03,271
How will I explain it to my niece?

2311
01:43:03,438 --> 01:43:04,146
Besides...

2312
01:43:04,396 --> 01:43:05,938
What will he say to his father-in-law?

2313
01:43:06,438 --> 01:43:09,521
That his brother is marrying
a Christian girl?

2314
01:43:09,646 --> 01:43:10,646
You should be ashamed!

2315
01:43:10,771 --> 01:43:11,646
Sarala!

2316
01:43:15,271 --> 01:43:15,771
What?

2317
01:43:16,271 --> 01:43:17,813
You go along with all of his whims.

2318
01:43:18,021 --> 01:43:19,896
But deny all his requests.

2319
01:43:20,438 --> 01:43:21,395
Is he your only son?

2320
01:43:21,396 --> 01:43:22,271
Isn’t he your son, too?

2321
01:43:23,771 --> 01:43:26,021
You can’t judge someone
without meeting them first.

2322
01:43:26,188 --> 01:43:27,271
We are going tomorrow.

2323
01:43:27,438 --> 01:43:28,521
We are meeting them.

2324
01:43:28,646 --> 01:43:29,895
- And you must come along!
- But...

2325
01:43:29,896 --> 01:43:30,563
Say nothing!

2326
01:43:31,146 --> 01:43:32,063
You too!

2327
01:43:32,271 --> 01:43:32,937
But I didn’t speak.

2328
01:43:32,938 --> 01:43:34,521
Especially you!

2329
01:43:34,896 --> 01:43:35,521
Quiet!

2330
01:43:51,563 --> 01:43:52,146
Dad...

2331
01:43:52,563 --> 01:43:55,313
How did you find courage while still sober?

2332
01:43:56,021 --> 01:43:56,938
I have no idea.

2333
01:43:57,188 --> 01:43:58,313
I just went with the flow.

2334
01:43:58,438 --> 01:43:59,812
- Was that okay?
- Okay?!

2335
01:43:59,813 --> 01:44:01,021
You just nailed it, Dad!

2336
01:44:01,271 --> 01:44:02,812
Mom will definitely come along.

2337
01:44:02,813 --> 01:44:03,812
No, she won't.

2338
01:44:03,813 --> 01:44:04,438
Come on, Dad!

2339
01:44:04,896 --> 01:44:07,146
Hey, I know all about her.

2340
01:44:07,521 --> 01:44:08,771
I’ll convince her somehow.

2341
01:44:09,521 --> 01:44:12,188
I know how to tackle your mother.

2342
01:44:12,396 --> 01:44:13,563
Tell them we’ll be there tomorrow.

2343
01:44:13,896 --> 01:44:15,146
Can I really trust you?

2344
01:44:17,646 --> 01:44:18,396
Trust me!

2345
01:44:21,396 --> 01:44:23,896
You look like a clown in that coat.

2346
01:44:24,146 --> 01:44:25,270
You’re going to stick out
like a sore thumb.

2347
01:44:25,271 --> 01:44:26,145
It’s fine, Mom--

2348
01:44:26,146 --> 01:44:27,520
Take it off!

2349
01:44:27,521 --> 01:44:28,687
Mom, it looks good!

2350
01:44:28,688 --> 01:44:30,020
Where are we now?

2351
01:44:30,021 --> 01:44:31,396
It’s her cousin's wedding.

2352
01:44:32,021 --> 01:44:33,312
- Hello, Uncle.
- Hey!

2353
01:44:33,313 --> 01:44:34,521
- Hi, Aunty
- Hi.

2354
01:44:35,896 --> 01:44:37,271
Come, let's go. It'll be fun.

2355
01:44:37,396 --> 01:44:38,146
Go!

2356
01:44:39,021 --> 01:44:39,646
Let's go!

2357
01:44:41,021 --> 01:44:41,563
Hi!

2358
01:44:54,146 --> 01:44:55,396
<i>♪ You wake up early ♪</i>

2359
01:44:55,771 --> 01:44:56,813
<i>♪ I stay up late ♪</i>

2360
01:44:57,271 --> 01:44:58,313
<i>♪ I say relax ♪</i>

2361
01:44:58,771 --> 01:45:00,188
<i>♪ You say we're late ♪</i>

2362
01:45:00,521 --> 01:45:01,563
<i>♪ You fill my stomach ♪</i>

2363
01:45:02,063 --> 01:45:03,396
<i>♪ You fill my heart ♪</i>

2364
01:45:03,646 --> 01:45:05,063
<i>♪ We're stuck together ♪</i>

2365
01:45:05,313 --> 01:45:06,771
<i>♪ Till death do us part ♪</i>

2366
01:45:33,271 --> 01:45:34,563
See who has come.

2367
01:45:38,313 --> 01:45:41,021
Don’t go, man. Come back here.

2368
01:45:41,146 --> 01:45:42,146
Come back!

2369
01:45:47,521 --> 01:45:48,146
Dad!

2370
01:45:49,813 --> 01:45:50,521
Stop!

2371
01:45:51,688 --> 01:45:53,021
Why did you just storm out?

2372
01:45:54,646 --> 01:45:56,688
I’ll support you marrying any girl...

2373
01:45:57,188 --> 01:45:58,563
But not his daughter.

2374
01:46:02,438 --> 01:46:03,396
Why’s that?

2375
01:46:05,521 --> 01:46:06,770
I asked you a question!

2376
01:46:06,771 --> 01:46:08,771
Because he’s the reason I lost my hearing!

2377
01:46:10,896 --> 01:46:11,521
Huh?

2378
01:46:16,438 --> 01:46:17,146
Hey, Ron!

2379
01:46:17,521 --> 01:46:18,771
Take over for my section, too.

2380
01:46:22,438 --> 01:46:23,188
Hey, Ron!

2381
01:46:23,396 --> 01:46:24,646
Finish all my work, too.

2382
01:46:25,313 --> 01:46:26,313
What’s with the look?

2383
01:46:26,563 --> 01:46:27,395
Do you refuse?

2384
01:46:27,396 --> 01:46:28,021
Why?

2385
01:46:28,396 --> 01:46:29,812
Why should I do your work for you?

2386
01:46:29,813 --> 01:46:30,813
Go do it yourself, man.

2387
01:46:30,938 --> 01:46:31,688
Hey!

2388
01:46:33,146 --> 01:46:34,646
Are you ganging up on me?

2389
01:46:35,771 --> 01:46:37,271
You guys are just temporary.

2390
01:46:37,813 --> 01:46:39,438
You won't keep your job for long.

2391
01:46:39,563 --> 01:46:40,521
What happened, man?

2392
01:46:41,146 --> 01:46:43,895
He's going to get whacked by me.

2393
01:46:43,896 --> 01:46:45,521
He's been poking me unnecessarily.

2394
01:46:45,896 --> 01:46:47,438
<i>I'm a key member of the union.</i>

2395
01:46:48,146 --> 01:46:49,646
<i>They shouldn’t have messed with me.</i>

2396
01:46:50,188 --> 01:46:53,271
<i>So, I got them all fired as I mentioned.</i>

2397
01:47:06,896 --> 01:47:07,563
Let go of me!

2398
01:47:25,021 --> 01:47:26,021
Don't you dare!

2399
01:47:40,938 --> 01:47:43,271
Aren't you even ashamed?

2400
01:47:43,813 --> 01:47:45,271
Someone has beaten up your Dad.

2401
01:47:45,396 --> 01:47:46,771
And the others laughed him out of the room.

2402
01:47:47,271 --> 01:47:48,896
And you’re just staring at them.

2403
01:47:50,021 --> 01:47:51,271
You’re no son of mine.

2404
01:47:51,521 --> 01:47:52,021
Damn you!

2405
01:49:02,313 --> 01:49:03,271
Relax! Relax!

2406
01:49:03,396 --> 01:49:04,313
It’s alright. Come on!

2407
01:49:12,771 --> 01:49:13,563
Dad!

2408
01:49:15,188 --> 01:49:16,562
What the hell are you doing, Bugger?!

2409
01:49:16,563 --> 01:49:17,063
Hey!

2410
01:49:18,771 --> 01:49:20,438
I know exactly what I'm doing.

2411
01:49:21,021 --> 01:49:22,521
You should ask him what happened!

2412
01:49:26,063 --> 01:49:29,521
Nothing matters more to me
than my Dad.

2413
01:49:29,896 --> 01:49:31,896
I don't want you anymore in my life.

2414
01:49:35,896 --> 01:49:36,646
Hey!

2415
01:49:37,271 --> 01:49:37,896
Stop!

2416
01:49:39,396 --> 01:49:40,021
Hey!

2417
01:49:41,396 --> 01:49:42,146
Krishna!

2418
01:49:50,313 --> 01:49:52,563
I've never seen a bigger idiot than you.

2419
01:49:53,146 --> 01:49:54,563
Why? What did I do?

2420
01:49:55,396 --> 01:49:56,813
You fell right into your Mom’s trap.

2421
01:49:56,938 --> 01:49:57,813
And you started a fight!

2422
01:49:58,313 --> 01:49:59,396
Do you think you're some kind of a hero?

2423
01:49:59,771 --> 01:50:01,438
Nothing matters more to me
than my Dad.

2424
01:50:02,146 --> 01:50:03,313
You really are a fool.

2425
01:50:03,646 --> 01:50:04,687
Hey, Bhaskar!

2426
01:50:04,688 --> 01:50:06,146
My patience is running thin.

2427
01:50:06,521 --> 01:50:07,313
Then what?

2428
01:50:07,938 --> 01:50:09,646
If I had waited 5 minutes,
I would've calmed down.

2429
01:50:09,938 --> 01:50:12,438
What happened that day
was my own fault?

2430
01:50:17,521 --> 01:50:18,146
Krishna...

2431
01:50:19,438 --> 01:50:21,063
Your only chance at happiness...

2432
01:50:22,146 --> 01:50:23,188
is if you marry Magic.

2433
01:50:23,771 --> 01:50:24,646
That’s all I have to say.

2434
01:50:25,313 --> 01:50:27,021
But, Mom has to agree to that.

2435
01:50:27,146 --> 01:50:29,271
That girl has to agree, first.

2436
01:50:29,813 --> 01:50:32,313
Apologize and make peace.

2437
01:50:32,521 --> 01:50:33,771
We'll deal with your Mom later.

2438
01:50:38,271 --> 01:50:38,770
Dad!

2439
01:50:38,771 --> 01:50:40,646
I don't want to talk to
any buggers out here!

2440
01:50:45,771 --> 01:50:46,438
Uncle...

2441
01:50:47,146 --> 01:50:49,521
I didn't mean for it
to get out of hand.

2442
01:50:49,771 --> 01:50:51,146
I'm terribly sorry, Uncle.

2443
01:50:54,313 --> 01:50:55,396
It's okay, Krishna.

2444
01:50:55,688 --> 01:50:56,145
Huh?

2445
01:50:56,146 --> 01:50:59,146
No son would have reacted differently.

2446
01:50:59,271 --> 01:51:00,771
I would have done the same thing, as well.

2447
01:51:01,521 --> 01:51:04,521
I had no idea he lost his hearing
because of me.

2448
01:51:04,771 --> 01:51:06,146
I feel very bad about it.

2449
01:51:06,396 --> 01:51:07,521
I'm sorry, Krishna.

2450
01:51:07,771 --> 01:51:09,146
My apologies to you...

2451
01:51:09,271 --> 01:51:11,146
your dad and to your entire family.

2452
01:51:11,396 --> 01:51:12,063
Oh, wow!

2453
01:51:13,646 --> 01:51:14,896
I’m glad you guys made peace.

2454
01:51:15,271 --> 01:51:16,063
Very good!

2455
01:51:16,646 --> 01:51:18,396
Not reason enough to marry you.

2456
01:51:18,521 --> 01:51:20,188
What else do you want him to do,
Magic?

2457
01:51:20,521 --> 01:51:21,771
That's his line.

2458
01:51:22,021 --> 01:51:23,563
He needs to ask that question.

2459
01:51:24,021 --> 01:51:24,812
Okay, tell me.

2460
01:51:24,813 --> 01:51:25,646
What should I do now?

2461
01:51:26,063 --> 01:51:27,688
Can you convince your Mom?

2462
01:51:28,271 --> 01:51:31,646
Will you leave that house for me
if she doesn't approve?

2463
01:51:31,771 --> 01:51:32,313
Why?

2464
01:51:32,646 --> 01:51:36,396
Is it impossible to marry someone
with their parent's approval?

2465
01:51:36,563 --> 01:51:37,938
What’s stopping you?

2466
01:51:38,146 --> 01:51:39,896
Do it! If you can!

2467
01:51:40,271 --> 01:51:43,146
Don't face me again
until you convince your Mom.

2468
01:51:43,396 --> 01:51:45,188
Or else don't come to my house ever.

2469
01:51:46,021 --> 01:51:47,021
You coward Bugger!

2470
01:51:48,021 --> 01:51:48,646
Magic...

2471
01:51:51,396 --> 01:51:52,063
Krishna!

2472
01:51:54,021 --> 01:51:55,521
Take as long as you want.

2473
01:51:56,313 --> 01:51:58,020
But I'm moving to Australia next week.

2474
01:51:58,021 --> 01:51:59,313
My visa has been confirmed.

2475
01:52:05,521 --> 01:52:07,521
Quit asking me the same thing.

2476
01:52:07,771 --> 01:52:09,021
Like I said before.

2477
01:52:09,396 --> 01:52:11,146
Engagement doesn't have to be
a separate expense.

2478
01:52:11,438 --> 01:52:13,271
It can be the same as reception.

2479
01:52:14,771 --> 01:52:16,395
Why should I ask Krishna?

2480
01:52:16,396 --> 01:52:17,896
What I say goes around here!

2481
01:52:18,146 --> 01:52:20,896
It's not like he can decide anyway.

2482
01:52:23,521 --> 01:52:24,646
Hey, Mangababu!

2483
01:52:25,146 --> 01:52:26,937
Inform all our people.

2484
01:52:26,938 --> 01:52:29,146
I want all of them to attend the wedding.

2485
01:52:30,646 --> 01:52:31,396
Understood?

2486
01:52:32,771 --> 01:52:33,688
This ends tonight

2487
01:52:33,896 --> 01:52:34,937
- Dad, don't.
- Let me go!

2488
01:52:34,938 --> 01:52:36,813
<i>You don't bring up new things.</i>

2489
01:52:37,521 --> 01:52:38,270
Understood?

2490
01:52:38,271 --> 01:52:39,188
Are you even human?!

2491
01:52:39,563 --> 01:52:40,771
Let me call you back.

2492
01:52:41,688 --> 01:52:42,646
I just want to know!

2493
01:52:43,271 --> 01:52:44,438
What kind of a human are you?

2494
01:52:45,896 --> 01:52:47,396
Are you going to stay like this forever?

2495
01:52:49,438 --> 01:52:51,896
Are you the only authority in this house?

2496
01:52:53,063 --> 01:52:54,688
Always grumpy.

2497
01:52:54,896 --> 01:52:56,021
Yelling at everyone.

2498
01:52:56,146 --> 01:52:57,146
You might as well be Hitler!

2499
01:52:59,438 --> 01:53:02,395
Why are you always so obsessed
with caste?

2500
01:53:02,396 --> 01:53:04,563
Did you ever think about
your son's happiness?

2501
01:53:05,521 --> 01:53:08,688
Cause she values her caste
over her own children.

2502
01:53:09,271 --> 01:53:10,146
Hey, Krishna!

2503
01:53:12,396 --> 01:53:13,188
Yes, indeed!

2504
01:53:13,396 --> 01:53:15,146
My people are important to me.

2505
01:53:15,896 --> 01:53:17,396
I never cared about my children.

2506
01:53:17,563 --> 01:53:19,062
Nor do I care about this family?

2507
01:53:19,063 --> 01:53:19,812
Is that what you want to hear?

2508
01:53:19,813 --> 01:53:21,313
- Mom?
- What?!

2509
01:53:22,896 --> 01:53:24,146
I may have a temper.

2510
01:53:25,396 --> 01:53:29,188
Have you wondered,
what made me this way?

2511
01:53:29,896 --> 01:53:30,896
Your Dad here...

2512
01:53:31,188 --> 01:53:33,021
...is a railway employee for namesake.

2513
01:53:33,646 --> 01:53:35,438
Ever since you were a kids...

2514
01:53:35,563 --> 01:53:37,313
he burns away his entire salary

2515
01:53:37,521 --> 01:53:40,563
on friends, food and drinking.

2516
01:53:40,771 --> 01:53:42,813
In fact, he’s still the same.

2517
01:53:44,688 --> 01:53:46,021
If I'm not the way that I am...

2518
01:53:46,188 --> 01:53:48,646
we could never have raised
all 3 kids and built this house.

2519
01:53:48,813 --> 01:53:51,021
We would have ended up
on the streets.

2520
01:53:54,313 --> 01:53:56,646
Have you ever treated me
as your wife?

2521
01:53:56,813 --> 01:53:58,896
You won't even look me in the eye.

2522
01:53:59,688 --> 01:54:00,813
You can't!

2523
01:54:01,063 --> 01:54:02,895
Because everything you do
is immoral.

2524
01:54:02,896 --> 01:54:03,938
Wrong!

2525
01:54:06,063 --> 01:54:08,688
You want to know
why I stay loyal to my community?

2526
01:54:09,188 --> 01:54:10,687
When we were dead broke...

2527
01:54:10,688 --> 01:54:13,938
the one who loaned us the money
to start my flour shop

2528
01:54:14,271 --> 01:54:15,396
was someone from my caste!

2529
01:54:15,688 --> 01:54:17,688
Without them,
we won't have this house.

2530
01:54:17,938 --> 01:54:18,938
Do you get it now?

2531
01:54:22,313 --> 01:54:24,563
They may have helped you
start the shop.

2532
01:54:25,563 --> 01:54:27,813
But not the one who kept it running.

2533
01:55:46,146 --> 01:55:49,521
<i>♪ A single drop of your love
Is enough to fill my heart ♪</i>

2534
01:55:49,896 --> 01:55:53,646
<i>♪ Every dream I've cherished
Becomes reality ♪</i>

2535
01:55:55,146 --> 01:55:58,646
<i>♪ A single smile is enough
To make a petal bloom ♪</i>

2536
01:55:58,813 --> 01:56:02,521
<i>♪ All the pain in my heart
Melts away ♪</i>

2537
01:56:03,771 --> 01:56:11,521
<i>♪ Beneath the endless sky,
Life unfolds before us ♪</i>

2538
01:56:12,688 --> 01:56:16,313
<i>♪ In the end... ♪</i>

2539
01:56:17,271 --> 01:56:21,563
<i>♪ Only a love that never runs dry
Remains between us ♪</i>

2540
01:56:21,771 --> 01:56:23,688
<i>♪ You're the guiding star ♪</i>

2541
01:56:23,896 --> 01:56:25,938
<i>♪ That shines your light upon me ♪</i>

2542
01:56:26,146 --> 01:56:29,646
<i>♪ A radiant glow ♪</i>

2543
01:56:30,771 --> 01:56:32,812
<i>♪ You're the raindrop... ♪</i>

2544
01:56:32,813 --> 01:56:35,146
<i>♪ Yet the moment you touch me, ♪</i>

2545
01:56:35,271 --> 01:56:38,146
<i>♪ You become an endless ocean ♪</i>

2546
01:56:52,646 --> 01:56:53,521
How much is in there?

2547
01:56:53,896 --> 01:56:54,771
50,000.

2548
01:56:55,271 --> 01:56:56,396
Come on, now!

2549
01:56:56,563 --> 01:56:58,396
I brought 10 people with me.

2550
01:56:58,771 --> 01:57:00,771
Everyone in our group was afraid
to voice opinions against.

2551
01:57:00,896 --> 01:57:04,563
- I went to a lot of trouble.
- I will pay you later.

2552
01:57:05,896 --> 01:57:07,396
Check if they're here.

2553
01:57:07,563 --> 01:57:08,271
Will do!

2554
01:57:13,521 --> 01:57:14,813
Bommi, behave!

2555
01:57:14,938 --> 01:57:16,396
They’re here, brother.

2556
01:57:16,521 --> 01:57:17,521
Bring them in.

2557
01:57:18,771 --> 01:57:21,313
- Leave everything to us.
- Bommi! Slow down!

2558
01:57:21,938 --> 01:57:25,396
Granny, did you eat?

2559
01:57:26,021 --> 01:57:27,563
- Hey!
- What the hell, Mom?

2560
01:57:27,771 --> 01:57:28,646
I'm warning you.

2561
01:57:28,771 --> 01:57:29,687
She's like a child.

2562
01:57:29,688 --> 01:57:31,646
- Dad, I'm leaving.
- Sathya, you stay.

2563
01:57:32,021 --> 01:57:32,812
Look at her.

2564
01:57:32,813 --> 01:57:34,062
Everybody, take a look.

2565
01:57:34,063 --> 01:57:35,896
Who wouldn't get mad over this?

2566
01:57:36,396 --> 01:57:38,895
And when I called her a nutcase,
she left the house.

2567
01:57:38,896 --> 01:57:39,896
Why do you think?

2568
01:57:40,396 --> 01:57:42,021
Meena, she's just a child.

2569
01:57:42,146 --> 01:57:43,396
Yes, indeed!

2570
01:57:43,646 --> 01:57:44,896
It’s not like I tortured her.

2571
01:57:45,271 --> 01:57:47,187
I only told them to try again
for a good child.

2572
01:57:47,188 --> 01:57:47,937
What's wrong with that?

2573
01:57:47,938 --> 01:57:48,938
What do you mean by "Good child?"

2574
01:57:49,271 --> 01:57:50,396
Isn't she a good child?

2575
01:57:50,896 --> 01:57:51,646
Look here...

2576
01:57:52,771 --> 01:57:54,396
- Do you know what mild autism is?
- Brother!

2577
01:57:54,646 --> 01:57:56,146
I don't need anymore lectures.

2578
01:57:56,396 --> 01:57:58,021
Your daughter
has already taken enough classes.

2579
01:57:58,146 --> 01:57:59,396
Now decide the next move.

2580
01:57:59,646 --> 01:58:00,896
The next move?

2581
01:58:01,188 --> 01:58:02,438
It’s to live together.

2582
01:58:02,646 --> 01:58:03,896
To reunite the family.

2583
01:58:04,021 --> 01:58:06,146
Isn't that why all our folks
have gathered around.

2584
01:58:06,271 --> 01:58:08,188
For that, she needs to come back
to our house.

2585
01:58:08,396 --> 01:58:09,271
That's right.

2586
01:58:09,396 --> 01:58:11,396
Sarala, your daughter,
should be the one to move out.

2587
01:58:11,521 --> 01:58:14,063
If she stays at your house,
what can we do?

2588
01:58:14,271 --> 01:58:16,895
If this is how they act in public...

2589
01:58:16,896 --> 01:58:18,938
there is no saying
what they might do in private.

2590
01:58:19,188 --> 01:58:21,895
My sister will only come back
if it’s an individual household.

2591
01:58:21,896 --> 01:58:25,146
Hey!
What's your sister's problem?

2592
01:58:25,646 --> 01:58:27,145
Always insisting on a separate family

2593
01:58:27,146 --> 01:58:29,187
It just sounds suspicious.

2594
01:58:29,188 --> 01:58:31,021
Watch your tongue!

2595
01:58:35,188 --> 01:58:36,521
I’ll beat him to a pulp.

2596
01:58:36,938 --> 01:58:37,938
Let go of him.

2597
01:58:38,521 --> 01:58:39,437
Get away from him.

2598
01:58:39,438 --> 01:58:41,646
Have you lost your mind?
What are you doing?

2599
01:58:41,896 --> 01:58:43,145
It's wrong to hit your elders.

2600
01:58:43,146 --> 01:58:45,396
- Did he act like an elder?
- That's enough!

2601
01:58:46,021 --> 01:58:47,146
That’s enough!

2602
01:58:47,521 --> 01:58:50,646
We didn't gather here
to see you guys fighting.

2603
01:58:51,396 --> 01:58:54,146
Sarala, will your daughter
go to their house?

2604
01:58:54,396 --> 01:58:56,521
If it’s a separate household,
I’ll send her right away.

2605
01:58:56,646 --> 01:58:58,520
I won't throw her to the wolves

2606
01:58:58,521 --> 01:59:00,063
Dear lord in heaven!

2607
01:59:00,521 --> 01:59:02,813
Shankar, are you seeing this?

2608
01:59:03,188 --> 01:59:05,270
They're making me look like the villain.

2609
01:59:05,271 --> 01:59:06,021
Aren't you?

2610
01:59:06,146 --> 01:59:07,312
- Shankar!
- Mom!

2611
01:59:07,313 --> 01:59:09,020
This is your life.
You take it from here.

2612
01:59:09,021 --> 01:59:09,896
- I'm leaving!
- Mom!

2613
01:59:10,146 --> 01:59:10,896
Mom!

2614
01:59:11,021 --> 01:59:12,812
Good riddance!
She’s such a drama queen.

2615
01:59:12,813 --> 01:59:14,645
- Mom, get back over here.
- Let go of me.

2616
01:59:14,646 --> 01:59:16,063
- Please hear me out.
- Let go of her!

2617
01:59:16,396 --> 01:59:16,938
Let her leave.

2618
01:59:18,271 --> 01:59:20,395
How would we come to a solution
if you leave?

2619
01:59:20,396 --> 01:59:21,063
Look here...

2620
01:59:21,438 --> 01:59:22,896
there nothing more to say.

2621
01:59:23,146 --> 01:59:24,271
She can come back home,
if she wants to.

2622
01:59:24,771 --> 01:59:25,895
Or let’s agree on a mutual divorce.

2623
01:59:25,896 --> 01:59:26,520
What?

2624
01:59:26,521 --> 01:59:27,271
Son in law?!

2625
01:59:28,271 --> 01:59:29,771
What are you even suggesting?

2626
01:59:30,646 --> 01:59:33,521
This wasn’t the reason
I married her within our community.

2627
01:59:34,063 --> 01:59:38,146
No matter what happens,
we'd adjust among ourselves.

2628
01:59:38,396 --> 01:59:40,395
Auntie, why do you still cling to caste?

2629
01:59:40,396 --> 01:59:41,270
It doesn’t matter.

2630
01:59:41,271 --> 01:59:42,396
What matters is a person’s character.

2631
01:59:42,521 --> 01:59:44,146
If their character is bad,
how does caste help in that matter?

2632
01:59:44,938 --> 01:59:46,312
Shankar has a point.

2633
01:59:46,313 --> 01:59:48,646
Character is what matters.
You can’t hide behind caste.

2634
01:59:49,646 --> 01:59:53,896
So that's why Sarala ends each sentence
with <i>Our people</i>.

2635
01:59:54,521 --> 01:59:56,021
We stand on the side of justice.

2636
01:59:56,146 --> 01:59:57,896
That’s the loyalty we owe to our caste.

2637
01:59:58,146 --> 02:00:00,146
Caste isn't a means to escape.

2638
02:00:00,271 --> 02:00:03,188
Send over your daughter
or agree to a mutual divorce.

2639
02:00:03,396 --> 02:00:05,396
We'll find another wife for Shankar.

2640
02:00:05,521 --> 02:00:06,520
There's plenty of other girls.

2641
02:00:06,521 --> 02:00:07,063
Hey!

2642
02:00:07,896 --> 02:00:09,146
My niece is close by.

2643
02:00:09,313 --> 02:00:10,188
I can talk to her--

2644
02:00:18,271 --> 02:00:19,271
Get out!

2645
02:00:19,521 --> 02:00:20,646
- Sarala?
- Say what?

2646
02:00:21,396 --> 02:00:22,895
Get the hell out, you dogs!

2647
02:00:22,896 --> 02:00:24,895
Show some respect.

2648
02:00:24,896 --> 02:00:27,562
Someone who separates a family
for money doesn't deserve respect.

2649
02:00:27,563 --> 02:00:28,896
Get out of here!

2650
02:00:29,646 --> 02:00:34,188
- Get lost!
- Alright, you heard her. Let's go

2651
02:00:34,396 --> 02:00:36,146
This is the end of this committee.

2652
02:00:36,438 --> 02:00:37,646
What do you want?

2653
02:00:37,771 --> 02:00:40,021
What do you want!?

2654
02:00:40,271 --> 02:00:42,396
If you want your wife and child

2655
02:00:42,521 --> 02:00:45,271
Stop listening to her
and live your own lives.

2656
02:00:45,563 --> 02:00:46,521
Or else...

2657
02:00:47,896 --> 02:00:49,188
Do you need him?

2658
02:00:49,813 --> 02:00:51,313
Not if he's going to stay like this.

2659
02:00:53,021 --> 02:00:53,938
You heard her.

2660
02:00:55,646 --> 02:00:56,313
Go away!

2661
02:00:56,521 --> 02:00:58,688
- What?
- Get the hell out!

2662
02:00:59,021 --> 02:01:00,521
You can always remarry.

2663
02:01:00,646 --> 02:01:01,813
Shut up, mom!

2664
02:01:02,063 --> 02:01:02,896
You're the cause of all this.

2665
02:01:03,021 --> 02:01:04,896
I know.
I'll live my own life.

2666
02:01:05,146 --> 02:01:05,813
Enough!

2667
02:01:06,271 --> 02:01:08,271
Why, Mom?

2668
02:01:37,021 --> 02:01:37,646
Sarala...

2669
02:01:38,146 --> 02:01:39,396
Why did you antagonize our son-in-law?

2670
02:01:40,021 --> 02:01:42,646
Then what should I have done?

2671
02:01:43,063 --> 02:01:45,271
Does he make a decision on his own?

2672
02:01:46,021 --> 02:01:47,688
If he just keeps living for his mother...

2673
02:01:48,021 --> 02:01:49,146
What about his life?

2674
02:01:49,646 --> 02:01:51,521
He likes Sathya, right?

2675
02:01:51,771 --> 02:01:52,938
Why not just leave his mother behind?

2676
02:01:53,646 --> 02:01:54,938
You’re against your son-in-law doing this.

2677
02:01:55,271 --> 02:01:56,896
But isn't your son doing the same thing.

2678
02:02:00,438 --> 02:02:01,813
You feel it when you're daughter suffers.

2679
02:02:02,188 --> 02:02:04,021
But you don't care about the other girl.

2680
02:02:04,396 --> 02:02:05,771
What can I do now?

2681
02:02:06,271 --> 02:02:07,771
The wedding is in two weeks.

2682
02:02:07,938 --> 02:02:08,896
It's too late now.

2683
02:02:09,271 --> 02:02:10,396
What am I supposed to do?

2684
02:02:10,813 --> 02:02:11,813
What if it was earlier?

2685
02:02:12,896 --> 02:02:14,271
Okay, he didn't.

2686
02:02:15,021 --> 02:02:16,646
But why couldn't he?

2687
02:02:17,271 --> 02:02:19,521
We never had
that sort of an environment.

2688
02:02:20,646 --> 02:02:23,271
We expect our children to be obedient.

2689
02:02:24,188 --> 02:02:27,313
But think about
how we actually treat that obedient kid.

2690
02:02:28,396 --> 02:02:29,396
Then you'll understand.

2691
02:02:31,271 --> 02:02:32,021
Big sis!

2692
02:02:32,396 --> 02:02:33,395
My dear, sister!

2693
02:02:33,396 --> 02:02:34,396
There he comes!

2694
02:02:34,563 --> 02:02:35,895
Oh, there you are!

2695
02:02:35,896 --> 02:02:38,146
Brother-in-law is here too.
Saves me the trouble.

2696
02:02:38,771 --> 02:02:40,521
Here's the wedding invite.

2697
02:02:40,646 --> 02:02:41,896
Check it out!

2698
02:02:47,646 --> 02:02:48,313
For god's sake!

2699
02:02:48,896 --> 02:02:50,313
I still can't read Telugu!

2700
02:02:51,521 --> 02:02:52,770
I forgot about that.

2701
02:02:52,771 --> 02:02:55,271
Sis, I handed the invitation
to all our folks back home.

2702
02:02:55,521 --> 02:02:58,938
I brought some Telugu invitations
in case there's anyone here.

2703
02:03:00,313 --> 02:03:02,521
Tanisha is very happy

2704
02:03:03,146 --> 02:03:04,562
Wedding hall has been fixed.

2705
02:03:04,563 --> 02:03:06,020
Catering has been fixed.

2706
02:03:06,021 --> 02:03:07,521
Live music has been fixed.

2707
02:03:08,021 --> 02:03:13,813
<i>♪ Won't this aching pain of love
Ever fade away? ♪</i>

2708
02:03:15,813 --> 02:03:20,688
<i>♪ Won't this aching pain of love
Ever fade away? ♪</i>

2709
02:03:20,896 --> 02:03:25,688
<i>♪ I ask
Through my tears ♪</i>

2710
02:03:26,063 --> 02:03:30,896
<i>♪ Isn't your disdain enough
To break me? ♪</i>

2711
02:03:31,188 --> 02:03:35,938
<i>♪ With each passing day ♪</i>

2712
02:03:36,313 --> 02:03:38,021
<i>♪ I'm unraveling ♪</i>

2713
02:03:38,396 --> 02:03:40,646
<i>♪ I'm losing myself ♪</i>

2714
02:03:41,021 --> 02:03:43,271
<i>♪ With every breath I have ♪</i>

2715
02:03:43,688 --> 02:03:45,521
<i>♪ I fill my soul with you ♪</i>

2716
02:03:46,271 --> 02:03:48,146
<i>♪ Will this go on forever? ♪</i>

2717
02:03:48,771 --> 02:03:50,771
<i>♪ Or will it finally end? ♪</i>

2718
02:03:51,813 --> 02:03:53,146
<i>♪ I'm breaking apart ♪</i>

2719
02:03:53,313 --> 02:03:54,396
<i>♪ Piece by piece ♪</i>

2720
02:03:54,646 --> 02:03:56,270
<i>♪ Will the deepest part of me ♪</i>

2721
02:03:56,271 --> 02:03:58,521
<i>♪ Ever learn to hate you? ♪</i>

2722
02:05:10,646 --> 02:05:11,771
Hey, Baba!

2723
02:05:12,813 --> 02:05:13,646
Tell me, Dude!

2724
02:05:15,521 --> 02:05:16,937
I need a small favor.

2725
02:05:16,938 --> 02:05:17,771
What, dude?

2726
02:05:18,021 --> 02:05:19,771
Do you plan to run away
from the wedding?

2727
02:05:20,063 --> 02:05:22,188
And you want me to sneak you out.

2728
02:05:22,563 --> 02:05:25,395
Magic is waiting in her car
at the end of this street.

2729
02:05:25,396 --> 02:05:26,521
Like hell!

2730
02:05:28,563 --> 02:05:30,021
Don't make me lose my temper.

2731
02:05:32,021 --> 02:05:33,396
I think you already did.

2732
02:05:34,688 --> 02:05:35,771
What's the favor?

2733
02:05:37,771 --> 02:05:39,771
I asked my brother to get me some shoes.

2734
02:05:39,938 --> 02:05:42,146
Look at what he got me.

2735
02:05:42,396 --> 02:05:43,896
I need something casual.

2736
02:05:44,146 --> 02:05:45,021
To go with the suit.

2737
02:05:45,146 --> 02:05:46,146
Can you get me that?

2738
02:05:50,646 --> 02:05:54,521
I thought you might commit suicide
after losing Magic.

2739
02:05:54,771 --> 02:05:57,521
But I’m glad you found
a compromise with your shoes.

2740
02:05:57,646 --> 02:05:59,146
You’re great, Dude!

2741
02:05:59,438 --> 02:06:00,146
Don't test me.

2742
02:06:00,688 --> 02:06:02,563
My rage is at its peak and I'd kill you.

2743
02:06:02,813 --> 02:06:03,896
Walk away!

2744
02:06:34,188 --> 02:06:36,188
- Carry them one by one.
- Come on, hurry up!

2745
02:06:36,396 --> 02:06:38,271
- It's getting late. Hurry up!
- Where is your husband?

2746
02:06:38,896 --> 02:06:41,770
He's upstairs.
He isn't responding.

2747
02:06:41,771 --> 02:06:43,021
- I'll go get him.
- Fine, try.

2748
02:06:43,313 --> 02:06:46,938
You look great!
Like an action star.

2749
02:06:47,146 --> 02:06:48,937
- Stop torturing him.
- I forgot about it.

2750
02:06:48,938 --> 02:06:49,937
I'll get your Dad.

2751
02:06:49,938 --> 02:06:51,438
Wait, I'll bring him down.

2752
02:06:51,646 --> 02:06:53,438
Be quick about it.
It's almost time

2753
02:06:53,646 --> 02:06:55,896
He'll take care of it.
You do your work.

2754
02:07:00,646 --> 02:07:01,396
Dad?

2755
02:07:03,646 --> 02:07:06,771
This isn't going resolve anything.

2756
02:07:07,021 --> 02:07:08,521
Even I moved on!

2757
02:07:14,771 --> 02:07:15,521
Dad?

2758
02:07:44,313 --> 02:07:45,063
Hey!

2759
02:07:48,063 --> 02:07:49,813
Bhaskar, wake up!

2760
02:07:50,396 --> 02:07:52,271
You look like you've seen a ghost.

2761
02:07:52,521 --> 02:07:55,271
You scared me for a second, Dad.

2762
02:07:55,563 --> 02:07:58,396
I thought you died cause I lost Magic.

2763
02:07:58,646 --> 02:07:59,396
What?

2764
02:08:00,271 --> 02:08:01,770
If you can't marry your lover...

2765
02:08:01,771 --> 02:08:02,771
Maybe you should die.

2766
02:08:02,896 --> 02:08:04,021
Why should I?

2767
02:08:04,521 --> 02:08:06,770
You don’t have the guts
to convince your mother.

2768
02:08:06,771 --> 02:08:08,438
Were you counting on on my death
to stop the wedding?

2769
02:08:08,771 --> 02:08:10,146
Hey, Bhaskar!

2770
02:08:10,271 --> 02:08:12,145
Watch yourself.
My rage is at its peak.

2771
02:08:12,146 --> 02:08:12,771
Hey!

2772
02:08:13,146 --> 02:08:14,562
If you spoke to your mother this way

2773
02:08:14,563 --> 02:08:16,020
Magic would have been the bride.

2774
02:08:16,021 --> 02:08:16,646
Not her.

2775
02:08:17,438 --> 02:08:18,646
Your fate is sealed!

2776
02:08:19,146 --> 02:08:21,312
Nobody can stop this wedding!

2777
02:08:21,313 --> 02:08:23,646
Oh, God! Oh, God!

2778
02:08:24,396 --> 02:08:25,646
Oh, God!

2779
02:08:25,771 --> 02:08:27,020
Hey move aside.

2780
02:08:27,021 --> 02:08:29,313
- Don't cry!
- What’s wrong?

2781
02:08:29,646 --> 02:08:31,645
Hey, Mangababu!
Why are you crying?

2782
02:08:31,646 --> 02:08:32,271
What happened?

2783
02:08:32,396 --> 02:08:33,688
I lost her for good.

2784
02:08:33,813 --> 02:08:35,312
Lost who?

2785
02:08:35,313 --> 02:08:37,313
Your daughter is just moving
into our house.

2786
02:08:37,521 --> 02:08:38,812
You haven’t lost her.

2787
02:08:38,813 --> 02:08:39,645
Wear the damn machine!

2788
02:08:39,646 --> 02:08:41,146
Watch your tone!

2789
02:08:42,771 --> 02:08:43,770
Now, tell me.

2790
02:08:43,771 --> 02:08:45,396
My daughter is missing.

2791
02:08:45,521 --> 02:08:48,562
All I found was a letter in her room.

2792
02:08:48,563 --> 02:08:49,771
Read it out!

2793
02:08:49,896 --> 02:08:50,521
Big sis!

2794
02:08:50,688 --> 02:08:51,937
We'll handle it.

2795
02:08:51,938 --> 02:08:52,563
Hey!

2796
02:08:53,063 --> 02:08:56,270
For the last time,
I can’t read Telugu!

2797
02:08:56,271 --> 02:08:57,312
Read it for yourself!

2798
02:08:57,313 --> 02:08:59,270
But I can't to read any language.

2799
02:08:59,271 --> 02:09:00,020
For God’s sake!

2800
02:09:00,021 --> 02:09:00,645
Give that back.

2801
02:09:00,646 --> 02:09:01,813
Mom you read this.

2802
02:09:04,563 --> 02:09:05,520
- Oh no!
- What?!

2803
02:09:05,521 --> 02:09:06,271
What happened , Mom?

2804
02:09:07,021 --> 02:09:08,646
I don’t think this is Telugu.

2805
02:09:09,771 --> 02:09:11,021
I think we can guess what’s in there.

2806
02:09:11,271 --> 02:09:14,520
Probably that she eloped
with some other guy.

2807
02:09:14,521 --> 02:09:15,770
Watch your tongue!

2808
02:09:15,771 --> 02:09:17,271
She might have gone out
to get some air.

2809
02:09:17,438 --> 02:09:20,646
Do you believe that she went out
to grab a coffee?

2810
02:09:21,021 --> 02:09:21,937
You fool!

2811
02:09:21,938 --> 02:09:22,896
She ran off with some guy.

2812
02:09:23,146 --> 02:09:24,146
Oh, no!

2813
02:09:26,813 --> 02:09:28,145
Don't cry, Brother.

2814
02:09:28,146 --> 02:09:29,396
Please calm down.

2815
02:09:29,646 --> 02:09:30,812
Do you know to read?

2816
02:09:30,813 --> 02:09:31,895
Give me a second.

2817
02:09:31,896 --> 02:09:33,812
Doesn’t anyone in this family
know how to read?

2818
02:09:33,813 --> 02:09:35,645
Krishna will bring her back.

2819
02:09:35,646 --> 02:09:36,563
Don't worry!

2820
02:09:36,896 --> 02:09:37,688
Dude!

2821
02:09:38,021 --> 02:09:39,896
I found the perfect shoe for you.

2822
02:09:40,063 --> 02:09:42,646
A perfect match for your coat.

2823
02:09:43,021 --> 02:09:44,271
Hang up, you moron!

2824
02:09:44,521 --> 02:09:45,063
Oh, no!

2825
02:09:46,146 --> 02:09:47,396
What happened, dude?

2826
02:09:47,646 --> 02:09:49,645
The girl ran away.

2827
02:09:49,646 --> 02:09:50,938
<i>- The girl eloped?</i>
- Yeah!

2828
02:09:51,563 --> 02:09:52,895
Then forget about it.

2829
02:09:52,896 --> 02:09:54,396
Let’s grab ourselves some tea.

2830
02:09:55,396 --> 02:09:56,188
Hey!

2831
02:09:56,521 --> 02:09:59,438
Did you hear what I just said?

2832
02:09:59,813 --> 02:10:00,813
Dude...

2833
02:10:01,146 --> 02:10:03,813
It’s not like being there
is going to solve anything.

2834
02:10:04,021 --> 02:10:05,271
Get over here.

2835
02:10:05,813 --> 02:10:07,146
You do have a point.

2836
02:10:07,521 --> 02:10:09,020
- I'll come.
<i>- Just get here.</i>

2837
02:10:09,021 --> 02:10:09,896
She can’t even run properly.

2838
02:10:10,021 --> 02:10:11,188
This man I say.

2839
02:10:12,688 --> 02:10:14,187
Hey, I need to borrow your bike.

2840
02:10:14,188 --> 02:10:15,688
Dude, where are you off to?

2841
02:10:16,646 --> 02:10:17,520
The bride ran away.

2842
02:10:17,521 --> 02:10:18,521
I see... the bride ran away.

2843
02:10:18,646 --> 02:10:20,271
Did you say the bride ran away?

2844
02:10:20,396 --> 02:10:21,395
How did it happen
without my knowledge?

2845
02:10:21,396 --> 02:10:22,771
Why is he shocked?

2846
02:10:44,646 --> 02:10:45,271
Hey!

2847
02:10:53,271 --> 02:10:55,521
You damn traitor!
I'm going to kill you.

2848
02:10:55,646 --> 02:10:57,021
It’s not what you think, Dude.

2849
02:10:57,146 --> 02:10:58,021
It’s true love.

2850
02:10:58,146 --> 02:10:59,145
I’ll end you!

2851
02:10:59,146 --> 02:11:00,812
We sincerely love each other.

2852
02:11:00,813 --> 02:11:01,895
As if!

2853
02:11:01,896 --> 02:11:03,020
In 2 weeks?

2854
02:11:03,021 --> 02:11:03,563
Dude!

2855
02:11:03,938 --> 02:11:06,521
You believed it when Kamal Haasan
said it in Vettaiyaadu Vilaiyaadu.

2856
02:11:07,063 --> 02:11:08,395
2 weeks is plenty time.

2857
02:11:08,396 --> 02:11:09,521
I’ll kill you!

2858
02:11:09,771 --> 02:11:12,021
Did Kamal Hassan run away
with his friend's bride?

2859
02:11:12,396 --> 02:11:13,812
I enraged. I'm going to--

2860
02:11:13,813 --> 02:11:14,895
Please don't harm him.

2861
02:11:14,896 --> 02:11:16,645
I’ll rip out your stupid hair.

2862
02:11:16,646 --> 02:11:17,187
I'll kill you!

2863
02:11:17,188 --> 02:11:18,020
Boys!

2864
02:11:18,021 --> 02:11:18,896
You can’t play here.

2865
02:11:19,063 --> 02:11:20,771
Play outside after having tea.

2866
02:11:21,146 --> 02:11:24,146
Is my anger a joke to you people?

2867
02:11:24,396 --> 02:11:25,771
Do I look like a fool?

2868
02:11:26,021 --> 02:11:27,895
I look like a mockery, aren't I?

2869
02:11:27,896 --> 02:11:29,646
- You’re the one to blame for this.
- Step aside!

2870
02:11:29,896 --> 02:11:32,021
- I ought to!
- Let’s think about our next move.

2871
02:11:32,271 --> 02:11:34,937
- I'm going to crack open your head.
- Dude, hear me out.

2872
02:11:34,938 --> 02:11:35,562
Wait! Wait! Wait!

2873
02:11:35,563 --> 02:11:36,437
This is the end for you!

2874
02:11:36,438 --> 02:11:37,396
One Tea!

2875
02:11:42,521 --> 02:11:43,270
<i>I’ll kill you!</i>

2876
02:11:43,271 --> 02:11:44,396
<i>Auto! Come over here.</i>

2877
02:11:44,646 --> 02:11:45,646
<i>Get in!</i>

2878
02:11:46,063 --> 02:11:46,688
<i>You too!</i>

2879
02:11:51,188 --> 02:11:52,021
Auto!

2880
02:11:52,521 --> 02:11:53,521
Get over here!

2881
02:11:53,771 --> 02:11:55,521
He’ll help us out.

2882
02:11:58,146 --> 02:12:00,437
Are you taking us to get married
at the temple?

2883
02:12:00,438 --> 02:12:02,020
Just shut up and get in!

2884
02:12:02,021 --> 02:12:02,771
Get in!

2885
02:12:02,896 --> 02:12:04,646
You too! Get in!

2886
02:12:05,021 --> 02:12:06,396
Thank you, Brother!

2887
02:12:07,313 --> 02:12:08,396
What just happened?

2888
02:12:08,688 --> 02:12:09,688
Please go to Lord Perumal's temple.

2889
02:12:10,438 --> 02:12:11,521
Hey, get out!

2890
02:12:11,938 --> 02:12:13,521
I told you to get out!

2891
02:12:13,896 --> 02:12:15,646
Hey, step out.

2892
02:12:15,771 --> 02:12:17,188
- Don't do it, Dude.
- It’s your funeral!

2893
02:12:17,688 --> 02:12:19,021
Dude! Dude!

2894
02:12:19,521 --> 02:12:21,188
Please, don't do this.

2895
02:12:22,271 --> 02:12:23,895
How dare you run away?

2896
02:12:23,896 --> 02:12:26,021
Hey, Mangababu, stop crying and look.

2897
02:12:26,521 --> 02:12:29,145
My son and his friend
brought your daughter back.

2898
02:12:29,146 --> 02:12:30,396
Hey, they're back!

2899
02:12:30,521 --> 02:12:31,395
You’ll have your wedding.

2900
02:12:31,396 --> 02:12:32,521
I’ll smack you!

2901
02:12:33,146 --> 02:12:34,146
You’re right, Uncle.

2902
02:12:34,438 --> 02:12:35,520
We caught her together.

2903
02:12:35,521 --> 02:12:37,021
I’ll smack you twice.
Get away!

2904
02:12:37,271 --> 02:12:39,271
Where did you run off to?

2905
02:12:39,396 --> 02:12:42,145
If it weren’t for this kind soul--

2906
02:12:42,146 --> 02:12:43,562
You fool!

2907
02:12:43,563 --> 02:12:45,146
This kind soul was the one
who ran off with her.

2908
02:12:45,646 --> 02:12:47,312
Baba, It was you!

2909
02:12:47,313 --> 02:12:48,063
You got that right!

2910
02:12:48,688 --> 02:12:49,688
I'm sorry.

2911
02:12:50,563 --> 02:12:53,021
Did he teach you to write
in gibberish Telugu?

2912
02:12:53,271 --> 02:12:55,271
That wasn’t Telugu, Uncle.

2913
02:12:55,396 --> 02:12:56,021
It’s Kannada!

2914
02:12:56,146 --> 02:12:57,313
I wrote that letter

2915
02:12:57,563 --> 02:12:59,895
Sorry I made you read it, Brother.

2916
02:12:59,896 --> 02:13:01,813
You fool! Get lost!

2917
02:13:02,021 --> 02:13:03,146
It’s not like I can read Kannada.

2918
02:13:03,271 --> 02:13:04,396
Hey, Mangababu!

2919
02:13:04,521 --> 02:13:05,896
Tell us what to do next.

2920
02:13:06,021 --> 02:13:06,895
What else?

2921
02:13:06,896 --> 02:13:08,145
The bride is back.

2922
02:13:08,146 --> 02:13:09,145
Let's get them married!

2923
02:13:09,146 --> 02:13:09,771
Oh!

2924
02:13:09,938 --> 02:13:11,395
You want me to go through with it?

2925
02:13:11,396 --> 02:13:13,021
I must look like a fool to you.

2926
02:13:13,396 --> 02:13:15,146
They can marry each other
for all I care!

2927
02:13:15,396 --> 02:13:16,396
Dude!

2928
02:13:16,521 --> 02:13:18,063
Now you’re speaking in gibberish.
I can't understand.

2929
02:13:18,271 --> 02:13:19,270
Are you going to marry her?

2930
02:13:19,271 --> 02:13:20,271
As if!

2931
02:13:20,396 --> 02:13:21,771
I will marry her myself.

2932
02:13:21,896 --> 02:13:23,271
Am I a joke to you?

2933
02:13:23,396 --> 02:13:25,395
I asked you to give
her a ride

2934
02:13:25,396 --> 02:13:27,020
Not to steal her

2935
02:13:27,021 --> 02:13:28,020
You expect me to marry her?

2936
02:13:28,021 --> 02:13:29,395
What do you think of me?

2937
02:13:29,396 --> 02:13:30,770
I’m not a chump!

2938
02:13:30,771 --> 02:13:32,271
I’m ready to throw hands!

2939
02:13:32,521 --> 02:13:34,896
Forget about it, Bro!

2940
02:13:35,021 --> 02:13:35,895
Chill out!

2941
02:13:35,896 --> 02:13:38,438
[in Hindi] Harish, my friend.
Tell me what should I do?

2942
02:13:38,646 --> 02:13:41,395
Whatever my family asks of me
I quietly do it.

2943
02:13:41,396 --> 02:13:42,896
But look what they have done to me.

2944
02:13:44,563 --> 02:13:47,146
Everyone thinks I'm an idiot.

2945
02:13:47,271 --> 02:13:47,938
Krishna!

2946
02:13:48,688 --> 02:13:49,770
Have you seen Magic?

2947
02:13:49,771 --> 02:13:50,895
She’s late for her flight.

2948
02:13:50,896 --> 02:13:51,771
I can’t find her.

2949
02:13:52,063 --> 02:13:53,813
Oh, really?
You can't find her, Uncle?

2950
02:13:54,146 --> 02:13:54,687
You can’t find her--

2951
02:13:54,688 --> 02:13:56,271
Yeah, I have her in my pockets.
See!

2952
02:13:56,438 --> 02:13:57,563
I got her right here!

2953
02:13:58,313 --> 02:13:59,896
You’re just mocking me, aren’t you?

2954
02:14:00,688 --> 02:14:02,021
I lost her, Uncle.

2955
02:14:02,563 --> 02:14:05,771
Because I lacked the guts
to tell my family that I need her.

2956
02:14:06,271 --> 02:14:07,063
Now, I lost her.

2957
02:14:07,396 --> 02:14:08,146
I'm a bugger!

2958
02:14:08,438 --> 02:14:10,313
Stupid bugger as Magic says.

2959
02:14:11,771 --> 02:14:12,646
My son...

2960
02:14:13,688 --> 02:14:15,271
I’m sorry, I thought you were dumb.

2961
02:14:15,646 --> 02:14:16,813
But your English is surprisingly good!

2962
02:14:17,438 --> 02:14:19,270
Hey! Why does that matter!

2963
02:14:19,271 --> 02:14:20,521
What do you want us to do?

2964
02:14:20,771 --> 02:14:23,813
Can you ever decide on what you want?

2965
02:14:24,021 --> 02:14:24,813
I guess not.

2966
02:14:25,271 --> 02:14:26,396
I don’t know how

2967
02:14:26,688 --> 02:14:27,896
That’s how I was raised.

2968
02:14:28,271 --> 02:14:29,021
Not just me...

2969
02:14:29,313 --> 02:14:36,145
Most of us grow up trapped
between your dreams and our own.

2970
02:14:36,146 --> 02:14:38,521
We're never allowed to speak our minds.

2971
02:14:39,271 --> 02:14:40,395
Then how do we know what you want?

2972
02:14:40,396 --> 02:14:41,271
Put in some effort.

2973
02:14:41,688 --> 02:14:42,896
Try to understand.

2974
02:14:43,021 --> 02:14:44,688
Don’t we kids
try to understand grown ups?

2975
02:14:44,896 --> 02:14:45,896
Then why can’t you do the same.

2976
02:14:46,146 --> 02:14:47,521
I get it now!

2977
02:14:47,896 --> 02:14:48,938
No matter what

2978
02:14:49,396 --> 02:14:50,895
I’ll marry Tanisha.

2979
02:14:50,896 --> 02:14:52,021
As if!

2980
02:14:52,146 --> 02:14:53,896
My daughter is out of your league.

2981
02:14:54,021 --> 02:14:54,688
Hey!

2982
02:14:54,938 --> 02:14:56,145
Why not?

2983
02:14:56,146 --> 02:14:57,688
He is family, too.

2984
02:14:58,521 --> 02:14:59,646
But he’s not our caste.

2985
02:14:59,771 --> 02:15:00,646
So what?

2986
02:15:01,021 --> 02:15:01,771
Oh!

2987
02:15:01,896 --> 02:15:04,771
You will pick matches
from our caste for your children.

2988
02:15:04,896 --> 02:15:06,145
But I should get my daughter
married to someone else.

2989
02:15:06,146 --> 02:15:08,896
I realized it a while ago
that it does not matter anymore.

2990
02:15:09,896 --> 02:15:12,396
Here on out,
my son makes his own decisions.

2991
02:15:13,521 --> 02:15:15,021
What else am I going to ask now?

2992
02:15:15,521 --> 02:15:17,146
I going to ask for Magic.

2993
02:15:18,938 --> 02:15:19,896
Then bring her here.

2994
02:15:20,021 --> 02:15:20,646
What?

2995
02:15:24,021 --> 02:15:26,520
This is some sort of trap, isn’t it?

2996
02:15:26,521 --> 02:15:28,270
I swear it isn’t.

2997
02:15:28,271 --> 02:15:29,271
Bring her here.

2998
02:15:31,313 --> 02:15:32,520
I'll bring her.

2999
02:15:32,521 --> 02:15:33,771
Bring her!

3000
02:15:34,021 --> 02:15:35,145
I'll bring her.

3001
02:15:35,146 --> 02:15:36,646
We insist!

3002
02:15:37,146 --> 02:15:38,145
I'll bring her for sure.

3003
02:15:38,146 --> 02:15:39,646
Do it already!

3004
02:15:41,396 --> 02:15:42,937
Okay! Thank you!

3005
02:15:42,938 --> 02:15:45,313
Son-in-law,
please don’t leave me!

3006
02:15:45,563 --> 02:15:46,438
Krishna!

3007
02:15:46,688 --> 02:15:48,437
Do you know where Magic is?

3008
02:15:48,438 --> 02:15:50,146
I know exactly where she’d be, Uncle.

3009
02:15:51,063 --> 02:15:52,271
Thank you! Thank you!
Co-in-law.

3010
02:15:52,396 --> 02:15:53,520
I'm sorry for what I did.

3011
02:15:53,521 --> 02:15:54,437
We’re all family now!

3012
02:15:54,438 --> 02:15:55,313
Water under the bridge.

3013
02:15:55,521 --> 02:15:56,896
Okay!

3014
02:16:13,021 --> 02:16:13,771
Hey, Bugger!

3015
02:16:14,521 --> 02:16:15,646
Didn’t you get married?

3016
02:16:20,438 --> 02:16:22,271
In this fast-paced world...

3017
02:16:23,771 --> 02:16:27,146
the only face
that brings me peace is yours.

3018
02:16:33,646 --> 02:16:34,438
I love you!

3019
02:16:35,271 --> 02:16:36,646
I love you too, my bugger.

3020
02:17:13,646 --> 02:17:17,146
<i>♪ A little love is enough
To fill my soul ♪</i>

3021
02:17:17,438 --> 02:17:20,896
<i>♪ Here, our lives are made whole ♪</i>

3022
02:17:22,646 --> 02:17:26,063
<i>♪ A smile brimming with joy
Is enough ♪</i>

3023
02:17:26,396 --> 02:17:29,771
<i>♪ Every trace of pain drifts away ♪</i>

3024
02:17:31,313 --> 02:17:38,896
<i>♪ Hearts that speak
Become boundless love ♪</i>

3025
02:17:43,813 --> 02:17:45,562
- Babu!
- Hey, Mangababu. Get over here!

3026
02:17:45,563 --> 02:17:46,688
I refuse!

3027
02:17:50,563 --> 02:17:53,146
Why does it have to me?

3028
02:17:55,271 --> 02:17:56,646
Oh, no!

3029
02:17:58,646 --> 02:18:02,063
<i>♪ A yearning
To bring my heart's dreams to life ♪</i>

3030
02:18:02,813 --> 02:18:05,438
<i>♪ O Radiant One ♪</i>

3031
02:18:05,771 --> 02:18:07,770
- I’m like that too.
- Is that right?

3032
02:18:07,771 --> 02:18:09,396
- Have some tea.
- Coffee!

3033
02:18:11,063 --> 02:18:12,146
Bless us!

3034
02:18:12,896 --> 02:18:14,271
We wish you the best.

3035
02:18:17,146 --> 02:18:18,521
- Let’s go to our new home.
- I'm leaving, Mom.

3036
02:18:26,438 --> 02:18:27,395
Don’t laugh!

3037
02:18:27,396 --> 02:18:29,646
It’s getting hard to shoot
with our star here.

3038
02:18:29,938 --> 02:18:31,438
Look at his fan club.

3039
02:18:33,646 --> 02:18:36,021
Many roses (Roja) welcomes
the only Roja (Name).

3040
02:18:40,313 --> 02:18:41,271
I yelled at him!

3041
02:18:46,896 --> 02:18:47,896
My Love...

3042
02:18:48,646 --> 02:18:49,521
I forgot the lines.

3043
02:18:50,021 --> 02:18:51,145
And if she doesn’t approve--

3044
02:18:51,146 --> 02:18:51,688
Line?

3045
02:18:52,063 --> 02:18:54,020
Hey, Magic!
What do I do with you?

3046
02:18:54,021 --> 02:18:55,521
Tell her
how much Magic means to you.

3047
02:18:56,063 --> 02:18:57,271
I’ll smack you down

3048
02:18:58,146 --> 02:18:58,813
Good Lord!

3049
02:18:59,146 --> 02:19:00,895
Why don’t you say “Cut!”?

3050
02:19:00,896 --> 02:19:01,770
Magic! Magic! Magic!

3051
02:19:01,771 --> 02:19:02,646
- Get Lost
- Oh, no!

3052
02:19:02,771 --> 02:19:04,021
We need to get rid of street dogs.

3053
02:19:04,188 --> 02:19:05,645
You’re doing "Naipavangal" instead
of "Parithabangal."

3054
02:19:05,646 --> 02:19:07,937
Yes, indeed.
“Naipavangal”, “Maadupavangal.”

3055
02:19:07,938 --> 02:19:10,646
That’s the only thing Gopi & Sudhagar
hasn’t done yet.

3056
02:19:10,771 --> 02:19:12,646
Only because
there are no audience for it.

3057
02:19:12,771 --> 02:19:13,937
He won’t let us show our acting ability.

3058
02:19:13,938 --> 02:19:15,271
Thinking it over and over--

3059
02:19:15,688 --> 02:19:17,563
Your line is “Magic.”

3060
02:19:19,021 --> 02:19:20,646
Next shot can be from the front.

3061
02:19:22,938 --> 02:19:24,813
Are you still reading that!?

3062
02:19:24,938 --> 02:19:26,395
I’m not coming up!

3063
02:19:26,396 --> 02:19:27,646
I’d rather take a photo with her.

3064
02:19:29,146 --> 02:19:30,146
What’s my line again?

3065
02:19:30,271 --> 02:19:31,646
Slow down, Director.

3066
02:19:34,271 --> 02:19:35,645
You’re enjoying this way too much.

3067
02:19:35,646 --> 02:19:36,645
First of all...

3068
02:19:36,646 --> 02:19:38,146
“Thaipusam”

3069
02:19:38,313 --> 02:19:40,145
I meant to say “Puratasi”.
Sorry! Sorry!

3070
02:19:40,146 --> 02:19:42,937
Beforehand, You need to woo Magic
and her Mom--

3071
02:19:42,938 --> 02:19:44,396
Not her Mom!

3072
02:19:45,771 --> 02:19:46,896
I got tongue tied.

